\li2 \v 16 \rb Obadiah|וְעֹבַדְיָה֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Galal|גָּלָ֖ל\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jeduthun|יְדוּת֑וּן\rb*;
\li2 \rb and Berechiah|וּבֶרֶכְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Asa|אָסָא֙\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb who lived|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in the villages|בְּחַצְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Netophathites|נְטוֹפָתִֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 17 \rb These were the gatekeepers|וְהַשֹּׁעֲרִים֙\rb*:
\li2 \rb Shallum|שַׁלּ֣וּם\rb*, \rb Akkub|וְעַקּ֔וּב\rb*, \rb Talmon|וְטַלְמֹ֖ן\rb*, \rb Ahiman|וַאֲחִימָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and their relatives|וַאֲחִיהֶ֥ם\rb*.
\li2 \rb Shallum|שַׁלּ֖וּם\rb* \rb was their chief|הָרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb*; \v 18 \rb |וְֽעַד־\rb*\rb |הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb he was previously stationed at the King’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Gate|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb on the east side|מִזְרָ֑חָה\rb*. \rb These|הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb were the gatekeepers|הַשֹּׁ֣עֲרִ֔ים\rb* \rb from the camp|לְמַחֲנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the Levites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |לֵוִֽי׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Shallum|וְשַׁלּ֣וּם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kore|ק֠וֹרֵא\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ebiasaph|אֶבְיָסָ֨ף\rb*,\f + \fr 9:19 \fqa Ebiasaph \ft is a variant of \fqa Abiasaph\ft ; see \ref Exodus 6:24|EXO 6:24\ref*.\f* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Korah|קֹ֜רַח\rb*, \rb and his relatives|וְֽאֶחָ֧יו\rb*\rb |אָבִ֣יו\rb*\rb |לְבֵית־\rb* \rb from the Korahites|הַקָּרְחִ֗ים\rb* \rb were assigned to guard|שֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the thresholds|הַסִּפִּ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Tent|לָאֹ֑הֶל\rb*, \rb just as their fathers|וַאֲבֹֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb had been assigned to|עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb*\rb |הָעֲבוֹדָ֔ה\rb* \rb guard|שֹׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the entrance|הַמָּבֽוֹא׃\rb* \rb to the dwelling|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*.
\li2 \v 20 \rb In earlier times|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb Phinehas|וּפִֽינְחָ֣ס\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֗ר\rb* \rb had been|הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb in charge|נָגִ֨יד\rb* \rb of the gatekeepers|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb was with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\li2 \v 21 \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָה֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּ֣ן\rb* \rb of Meshelemiah|מְשֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb was the gatekeeper|שֹׁעֵ֥ר\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|לְאֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*.
\li2 \v 22 \rb The number|כֻּלָּ֤ם\rb* \rb of those chosen|הַבְּרוּרִים֙\rb* \rb to be gatekeepers|לְשֹׁעֲרִ֣ים\rb* \rb at the thresholds|בַּסִּפִּ֔ים\rb* \rb was 212|מָאתַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ר\rb*. \rb They|הֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb were registered by genealogy|הִתְיַחְשָׂ֔ם\rb* \rb in their villages|בְחַצְרֵיהֶם֙\rb*. \rb David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb and Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb the seer|הָרֹאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb had appointed|יִסַּ֥ד\rb* \rb them|הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb to their positions of trust|בֶּאֱמוּנָתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb So they|וְהֵ֨ם\rb* \rb and their descendants|וּבְנֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb were assigned to|עַל־\rb* \rb guard|לְמִשְׁמָרֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb the gates|הַשְּׁעָרִ֧ים\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* — \rb the house|לְבֵ֥ית־\rb* \rb called the Tent|הָאֹ֖הֶל\rb*. \v 24 \rb The gatekeepers|הַשֹּׁעֲרִ֑ים\rb* \rb were stationed|יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb on the four|לְאַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb sides|רוּח֔וֹת\rb*: \rb east|מִזְרָ֥ח\rb*, \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*, \rb north|צָפ֥וֹנָה\rb*, \rb and south|וָנֶֽגְבָּה׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Their relatives|וַאֲחֵיהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb came|לָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb from their villages|בְּחַצְרֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb at fixed times|מֵעֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to serve with|עִם־\rb* \rb them|אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb for seven-day periods|לְשִׁבְעַ֧ת\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֛ים\rb*. \v 26 \rb But|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |בֶאֱמוּנָ֞ה\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֙עַת֙\rb* \rb chief|גִּבֹּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb gatekeepers|הַשֹּׁעֲרִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb who|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb were Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*, \rb were|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb entrusted with|עַל־\rb* \rb the rooms|הַלְּשָׁכ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |וְעַ֥ל\rb* \rb and the treasuries|הָאֹצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb They would spend the night|יָלִ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb stationed around|וּסְבִיב֥וֹת\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|עֲלֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb were responsible for guarding it|מִשְׁמֶ֔רֶת\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and opening it|הַמַּפְתֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb every morning|וְלַבֹּ֥קֶר\rb*\rb |לַבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Some of them|וּמֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb were in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb used in worship|הָעֲבוֹדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb to|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb count them|בְמִסְפָּ֣ר\rb* \rb whenever they were brought in|יְבִיא֔וּם\rb*\rb |וּבְמִסְפָּ֖ר\rb* \rb or taken out|יוֹצִיאֽוּם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb |וּמֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb Others were put|מְמֻנִּים֙\rb* \rb in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the furnishings|הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb and other|כָּל־\rb* \rb articles|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb as well as the fine flour|הַסֹּ֙לֶת֙\rb*, \rb wine|וְהַיַּ֣יִן\rb*, \rb oil|וְהַשֶּׁ֔מֶן\rb*, \rb frankincense|וְהַלְּבוֹנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and spices|וְהַבְּשָׂמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb And some|וּמִן־\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb mixed|רֹקְחֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַמִּרְקַ֖חַת\rb* \rb the spices|לַבְּשָׂמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb A Levite|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb named Mattithiah|וּמַתִּתְיָה֙\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the firstborn son|הַבְּכ֖וֹר\rb* \rb of Shallum|לְשַׁלֻּ֣ם\rb* \rb the Korahite|הַקָּרְחִ֑י\rb*, \rb was entrusted|בֶּאֱמוּנָ֕ה\rb* \rb with|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb baking|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the bread|הַחֲבִתִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb Some of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb their Kohathite|בְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |הַקְּהָתִ֛י\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb relatives|אֲחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb were responsible for|עַל־\rb* \rb preparing|לְהָכִ֖ין\rb* \rb the rows|הַֽמַּעֲרָ֑כֶת\rb* \rb of the showbread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb every Sabbath|שַׁבַּ֥ת\rb*\rb |שַׁבָּֽת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb Those who were|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb musicians|הַ֠מְשֹׁרְרִים\rb*, \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of Levite|לַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb* \rb families|אָב֧וֹת\rb*, \rb stayed in the temple chambers|בַּלְּשָׁכֹ֖ת\rb* \rb and were exempt|פְּטִירִים\rb* \rb from other duties|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb because they were|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on duty|בַּמְּלָאכָֽה׃\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֥ם\rb* \rb and night|וָלַ֛יְלָה\rb*. \v 34 \rb All these|אֵלֶּה֩\rb* \rb were heads|רָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of Levite|לַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb* \rb families|הָאָב֧וֹת\rb*, \rb chiefs|רָאשִׁ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb according to their genealogies|לְתֹלְדוֹתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and they lived|יָשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Descendants of Saul
\li1 \v 35 \rb Jeiel|יְעוּאֵל\rb* \rb the father|אֲבִֽי־\rb*\f + \fr 9:35 \ft Or \fqa the founder\f* \rb of Gibeon|וּבְגִבְע֛וֹן\rb* \rb lived|יָשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in Gibeon|גִבְע֖וֹן\rb*. \rb His wife’s|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb was Maacah|מַעֲכָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 36 \rb Abdon|עַבְדּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb was his firstborn|הַבְּכ֖וֹר\rb* \rb son|וּבְנ֥וֹ\rb*, \rb then Zur|וְצ֣וּר\rb*, \rb Kish|וְקִ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb Baal|וּבַ֥עַל\rb*, \rb Ner|וְנֵ֖ר\rb*, \rb Nadab|וְנָדָֽב׃\rb*, \v 37 \rb Gedor|וּגְד֣וֹר\rb*, \rb Ahio|וְאַחְי֔וֹ\rb*, \rb Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Mikloth|וּמִקְלֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 38 \rb Mikloth|וּמִקְל֖וֹת\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Shimeam|שִׁמְאָ֑ם\rb*.\f + \fr 9:38 \fqa Shimeam \ft is a variant of \fqa Shimeah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 8:32|1CH 8:32\ref*.\f* \rb They|הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb too|וְאַף־\rb* \rb lived|יָשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb alongside|נֶ֧גֶד\rb* \rb their relatives|אֲחֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירֽוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb*\rb |אֲחֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 39 \rb Ner|וְנֵר֙\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Kish|קִ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb Kish|וְקִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*, \rb and Saul|וְשָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֤יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מַלְכִּי־\rb* \rb Malchishua|שׁ֔וּעַ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Abinadab|אֲבִינָדָ֖ב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Esh-baal|אֶשְׁבָּֽעַל׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 40 \rb The son|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb*:\rb |מְרִ֣יב\rb*
\li2 \rb Merib-baal|בָּ֑עַל\rb*,\rb |וּמְרִי־\rb* \rb who|בַ֖עַל\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Micah|מִיכָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 41 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Micah|מִיכָ֑ה\rb*:
\li2 \rb Pithon|פִּית֥וֹן\rb*, \rb Melech|וָמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb Tahrea, and Ahaz|וְתַחְרֵֽעַ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 9:41 \ft Vulgate and Syriac (see also LXX and \ref 1 Chronicles 8:35|1CH 8:35\ref*); Hebrew \fqa Pithon, Melech, and Tahrea\ft ; note that \fqa Tahrea \ft is a variant of \fqa Tarea\ft .\f*
\li2 \v 42 \rb Ahaz|וְאָחָז֙\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jarah|יַעְרָ֔ה\rb*; \rb Jarah|וְיַעְרָ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 9:42 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX \fqa Jadah; Jadah\ft ; note that \fqa Jarah \ft and \fqa Jadah \ft are variants of \fqa Jehoaddah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 8:36|1CH 8:36\ref*.\f* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֛יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Alemeth|עָלֶ֥מֶת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Azmaveth|עַזְמָ֖וֶת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Zimri|זִמְרִ֑י\rb*; \rb and Zimri|וְזִמְרִ֖י\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moza|מוֹצָֽא׃\rb*. \v 43 \rb Moza|וּמוֹצָ֖א\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Binea|בִּנְעָ֑א\rb*. \rb Rephaiah|וּרְפָיָ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 9:43 \fqa Rephaiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Raphah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 8:37|1CH 8:37\ref*.\f* \rb was his son|בְנ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb Elasah|אֶלְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and Azel|אָצֵ֥ל\rb* \rb his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 44 \rb And Azel|וּלְאָצֵל֮\rb* \rb had six|שִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִים֒\rb*, \rb and these|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were their names|שְׁמוֹתָ֗ם\rb*:
\li2 \rb Azrikam|עַזְרִיקָ֥ם׀\rb*, \rb Bocheru|בֹּ֙כְרוּ֙\rb*, \rb Ishmael|וְיִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb*, \rb Sheariah|וּשְׁעַרְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Obadiah|וְעֹבַדְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and Hanan|וְחָנָ֑ן\rb*. \rb These were|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Azel|אָצַֽל׃פ\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 Saul’s Overthrow and Death
\r (\ref 1 Samuel 31:1–6|1SA 31:1-6\ref*; \ref 2 Samuel 1:1–16|2SA 1:1-16\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb fought|נִלְחֲמ֣וּ\rb* \rb against Israel|בְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and the men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּ֑נָס\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb them|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and many fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb slain|חֲלָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Gilboa|גִּלְבֹּֽעַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb The Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb followed hard after|וַיַּדְבְּק֣וּ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and his sons|בָנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and they killed|וַיַּכּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֧ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Abinadab|אֲבִינָדָ֛ב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מַלְכִּי־\rb* \rb and Malchishua|שׁ֖וּעַ\rb*. \v 3 \rb When the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb intensified|וַתִּכְבַּ֤ד\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb the archers|הַמּוֹרִ֣ים\rb* \rb overtook him|וַיִּמְצָאֻ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |בַּקָּ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb and wounded him|וַיָּ֖חֶל\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |הַיּוֹרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then Saul|שָׁאוּל֩\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֨א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb Draw|שְׁלֹ֥ף\rb* \rb your sword|חַרְבְּךָ֣׀\rb* \rb and run me through|וְדָקְרֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb with it|בָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb uncircumcised men|הָעֲרֵלִ֤ים\rb* \rb will come|יָבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb and torture|וְהִתְעַלְּלוּ־\rb* \rb me|בִ֔י\rb*!”
\p \rb But his armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb was terrified|יָרֵ֖א\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑דס\rb* \rb and refused|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb to do it|אָבָה֙\rb*. \rb So Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb his own sword|הַחֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb and fell|וַיִּפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When his armor-bearer|נֹשֵֽׂא־\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb he|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his own sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*. \v 6 \rb So Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb died|מֵֽתוּ׃\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֥ו\rb* \rb with his three|וּשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֤מָת\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb*.
\s1 The Philistines Possess the Towns
\r (\ref 1 Samuel 31:7–10|1SA 31:7-10\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb When all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the valley|בָּעֵ֙מֶק֙\rb* \rb saw|וַ֠יִּרְאוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the army had fled|נָ֔סוּ\rb* \rb and that|וְכִי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb had died|מֵ֖תוּ\rb*, \rb they abandoned|וַיַּעַזְב֤וּ\rb* \rb their cities|עָרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and ran away|וַיָּנֻ֔סוּ\rb*. \rb So the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and occupied|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb their cities|בָּהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb*, \rb when the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to strip|לְפַשֵּׁ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dead|הַֽחֲלָלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb they found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb fallen|נֹפְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Gilboa|גִּלְבֹּֽעַ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb They stripped Saul|וַיַּ֨פְשִׁיטֻ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb cut off his head|רֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his armor|כֵּלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and sent|וַיְשַׁלְּח֨וּ\rb* \rb messengers throughout the land|בְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb*\rb |סָבִ֗יב\rb* \rb to proclaim the news|לְבַשֵּׂ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the temple of their idols|עֲצַבֵּיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and among their people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb They put|וַיָּשִׂ֙ימוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his armor|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb* \rb in the temple|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of their gods|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and hung|תָקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb his head|גֻּלְגָּלְתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb in the temple|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Dagon|דָּגֽוֹן׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Jabesh-gilead’s Tribute to Saul
\r (\ref 1 Samuel 31:11–13|1SA 31:11-13\ref*)
\p \v 11 \rb When all the people of|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb heard about|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb had done|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*, \v 12 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of valor|חַיִל֒\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּקוּמוּ֮\rb* \rb and retrieved|וַיִּשְׂא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bodies|גּוּפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |גּוּפֹ֣ת\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and brought them|וַיְבִיא֖וּם\rb* \rb to Jabesh|יָבֵ֑ישָׁה\rb*. \rb And they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their bones|עַצְמוֹתֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb under|תַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb the oak|הָאֵלָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 10:12 \ft Or \fqa terebinth \ft or \fqa great tree\f* \rb in Jabesh|בְּיָבֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and fasted|וַיָּצ֖וּמוּ\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb*\rb |מָעַ֣ל\rb* \rb for his unfaithfulness|בְּמַֽעֲלוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb keep|שָׁמָ֑ר\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb consulted|לִשְׁא֥וֹל\rb* \rb a medium|בָּא֖וֹב\rb* \rb for guidance|לִדְרֽוֹשׁ׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb and he failed|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb to inquire|דָרַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*. \rb So the LORD put him to death|וַיְמִיתֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and turned the kingdom|הַמְּלוּכָ֔ה\rb* \rb over|וַיַּסֵּב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֖יד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשָֽׁי׃פ\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 David Anointed King of All Israel
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 5:1–5|2SA 5:1-5\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb came together|וַיִּקָּבְצ֧וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb at Hebron|חֶבְר֣וֹנָה\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb we are|אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃\rb*, \rb your own flesh|וּֽבְשָׂרְךָ֖\rb* \rb and blood|עַצְמְךָ֥\rb*. \v 2 \rb Even|גַּם־\rb*\rb |תְּמ֣וֹל\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb in times past|שִׁלְשׁ֗וֹם\rb*,\f + \fr 11:2 \ft Or \fqa For some time\f*\rb |גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb while Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb was|בִּהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb king|מֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb you were|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb the one who led|הַמּוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb Israel out|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and brought them back|וְהַמֵּבִ֖יא\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*\rb |לְךָ֗\rb*, ‘\rb You|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb will shepherd|תִרְעֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb ruler|נָגִ֔יד\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb them|עַמִּ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 3 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb came|וַ֠יָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb at Hebron|חֶבְר֔וֹנָה\rb*, \rb where|בְּחֶבְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרֹת֩\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֛ית\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And they anointed|וַיִּמְשְׁח֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\s1 David Conquers Jerusalem
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 5:6–11|2SA 5:6-11\ref*)
\p \v 4 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֧יד\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb marched|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb (that is|הִ֣יא\rb*, \rb Jebus)|יְב֑וּס\rb*, \rb where|וְשָׁם֙\rb* \rb the Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִ֔י\rb* \rb inhabited|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb The people|יֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Jebus|יְבוּס֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔יד\rb*, “\rb You will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb get in|תָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb here|הֵ֑נָּה\rb*.”
\p \rb Nevertheless , David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֤ד\rb* \rb the fortress|מְצֻדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb* (\rb that is|הִ֖יא\rb*, \rb the City|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִֽיד׃\rb*).
\p \v 6 \rb Now David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb had said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb is the first|בָּרִ֣אשׁוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb to strike down|מַכֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a Jebusite|יְבוּסִי֙\rb* \rb will become|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb chief|וּלְשָׂ֑ר\rb* \rb commander|לְרֹ֖אשׁ\rb*.”
\p \rb And Joab|יוֹאָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֖ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb first|בָּרִאשׁוֹנָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and he became|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb the chief|לְרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb So David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb took up residence|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the fortress|בַּמְצָ֑ד\rb*; \rb that is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb it was called|קָרְאוּ־\rb* \rb the City|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִֽיד׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb He built up|וַיִּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb around it|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb*, \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the supporting terraces|הַמִּלּ֖וֹא\rb*\f + \fr 11:8 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Millo\f* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the surrounding wall|הַסָּבִ֑יב\rb*, \rb while Joab|וְיוֹאָ֕ב\rb* \rb restored|יְחַיֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rest|שְׁאָ֥ר\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb And David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb became|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb greater|הָל֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb and greater|וְגָד֑וֹל\rb*, \rb for the LORD|וַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb was with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 David’s Mighty Men
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 23:8–39|2SA 23:8-39\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb Now these were|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb the chiefs|רָאשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of David’s|לְדָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבּוֹרִים֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*, \rb together with|עִמּ֧וֹ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb bolstered|לְהַמְלִיכ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and strengthened|הַמִּתְחַזְּקִ֨ים\rb* \rb his kingdom|בְמַלְכוּת֛וֹ\rb*, \rb according to|עִם־\rb* \rb the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*. \v 11 \rb This|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb is the list|מִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of David’s|לְדָוִ֑יד\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִ֖ים\rb*:\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*
\p \rb Jashobeam|יָשָׁבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hachmoni|חַכְמוֹנִ֗י\rb* \rb was chief|רֹ֚אשׁ\rb* \rb of the officers|הַשְּׁלוֹשִׁים\rb*;\f + \fr 11:11 \ft Or \fqa of the Thirty\ft ; some LXX manuscripts \fqa of the Three\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:8|2SA 23:8\ref*.\f* \rb he|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb wielded|עוֹרֵ֧ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his spear|חֲנִית֛וֹ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred men|מֵא֥וֹת\rb*, \rb whom he killed|חָלָ֖ל\rb* \rb at one|אֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb time|בְּפַ֥עַם\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Next in command was|וְאַחֲרָ֛יו\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֥ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Dodo|דּוֹד֖וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 11:12 \fqa Dodo \ft is a variant of \fqa Dodai\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 27:4|1CH 27:4\ref*.\f* \rb the Ahohite|הָאֲחוֹחִ֑י\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb*, \rb one of the three|בִּשְׁלוֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֜יד\rb*\rb |בַּפַּ֣ס\rb* \rb at Pas-dammim|דַּמִּ֗ים\rb* \rb when the Philistines|וְהַפְּלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb gathered|נֶאֱסְפוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*. \rb At|וַתְּהִ֛י\rb* \rb a place|חֶלְקַ֥ת\rb* \rb with a field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb full of|מְלֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb barley|שְׂעוֹרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb the troops|וְהָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb fled|נָ֖סוּ\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb But Eleazar and David stationed themselves|וַיִּֽתְיַצְּב֤וּ\rb*\f + \fr 11:14 \ft Literally \fqa But they stationed themselves\f* \rb in the middle|בְתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb of the field|הַחֶלְקָה֙\rb* \rb and defended it|וַיַּצִּיל֔וּהָ\rb*. \rb They struck down|וַיַּכּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb brought about|וַיּ֥וֹשַׁע\rb* \rb a great|גְדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb victory|תְּשׁוּעָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Three|שְֽׁלוֹשָׁה֩\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the thirty|הַשְּׁלוֹשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb chief men|רֹ֤אשׁ\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּרְד֡וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*, \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the rock|הַצֻּר֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cave|מְעָרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Adullam|עֲדֻלָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb while a company|וּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb was encamped|חֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Rephaim|רְפָאִֽים׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb David|וְדָוִ֖יד\rb* \rb was in the stronghold|בַּמְּצוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the garrison|וּנְצִ֣יב\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אָ֖ז\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb was at Bethlehem|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb longed for water|וַיִּתְאָו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Oh, that someone|מִ֚י\rb* \rb would get me a drink|יַשְׁקֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb of water|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from the well|מִבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb near the gate|בַּשָּֽׁעַר׃\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|לֶ֖חֶם\rb*!”\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb So the Three|הַשְּׁלֹשָׁ֜ה\rb* \rb broke|וַיִּבְקְע֨וּ\rb* \rb through the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb camp|בְּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb drew|וַיִּֽשְׁאֲבוּ־\rb* \rb water|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb from the well|מִבּ֤וֹר\rb* \rb at the gate|בַּשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*\rb |וַיִּשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and brought it|וַיָּבִ֣אוּ\rb* \rb back to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*. \rb But he|דָוִיד֙\rb* \rb refused|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אָבָ֤ה\rb* \rb to drink it|לִשְׁתּוֹתָ֔ם\rb*; \rb instead , he poured it out|וַיְנַסֵּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Far be it|חָלִילָה֩\rb* \rb from me|לִּ֨י\rb*, \rb my God|מֵאֱלֹהַ֜י\rb*, \rb to do|מֵעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb this|זֹ֗את\rb*! \rb How can I drink|אֶשְׁתֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb the blood|הֲדַ֣ם\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁים֩\rb* \rb who risked their lives|בְנַפְשׁוֹתָם֙\rb*?” \rb Because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had brought it|הֱבִיא֔וּם\rb* \rb at the risk of their lives|בְנַפְשׁוֹתָ֣ם\rb*, \rb David refused|אָבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to drink it|לִשְׁתּוֹתָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb Such|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were the exploits|עָשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb of the three|שְׁלֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבּוֹרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now Abishai|וְאַבְשַׁ֣י\rb*, \rb the brother|אֲחִֽי־\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb*, \rb was|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb chief|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the Three|הַשְּׁלוֹשָׁ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 11:20 \ft Hebrew; Syriac \fqa the Thirty\ft ; also in verse 21\f*\rb |וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb and he|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb wielded|עוֹרֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his spear|חֲנִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred men|מֵא֖וֹת\rb*, \rb killed them|חָלָ֑ל\rb*, \rb and won|וְלֹא\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb along with the Three|בַּשְּׁלוֹשָֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb He was doubly|בַשְּׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb honored|נִכְבָּ֔ד\rb* \rb above|מִן־\rb* \rb the Three|הַשְּׁלוֹשָׁ֤ה\rb*, \rb and he became|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb commander|לְשָׂ֑ר\rb*,\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb even though he was not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb included|בָֽא׃ס\rb* \rb among the Three|הַשְּׁלוֹשָׁ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb And Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֧ע\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb was a man|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֛יִל\rb* \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb Kabzeel|קַבְצְאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb a man of many|רַב־\rb* \rb exploits|פְּעָלִ֖ים\rb*. \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb struck down|הִכָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb champions|אֲרִיאֵל֙\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*,\f + \fr 11:22 \ft Or \fqa two sons of Ariel of Moab\f* \rb and on a snowy|הַשָּֽׁלֶג׃\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb he|וְ֠הוּא\rb* \rb went down|יָרַ֞ד\rb* \rb into|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb a pit|הַבּ֖וֹר\rb* \rb and killed|וְהִכָּ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb a lion|הָאֲרִ֛י\rb*. \v 23 \rb He|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb also struck down|הִכָּה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb an Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִ֜י\rb*, \rb a huge|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb man|מִדָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits tall|בָּאַמָּ֗ה\rb*.\f + \fr 11:23 \fqa 5 cubits \ft is approximately 7 feet 6 inches or 229 centimeters tall.\f* \rb Although the Egyptian|הַמִּצְרִ֤י\rb* \rb had a spear|חֲנִית֙\rb* \rb like a weaver’s|אֹרְגִ֔ים\rb* \rb beam|כִּמְנ֣וֹר\rb* \rb in his hand|וּבְיַ֨ד\rb*, \rb Benaiah went against|וַיֵּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb with a club|בַּשָּׁ֑בֶט\rb*, \rb snatched|וַיִּגְזֹ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the spear|הַחֲנִית֙\rb* \rb from his|הַמִּצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb*, \rb and killed the Egyptian|וַיַּהַרְגֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with his own spear|בַּחֲנִיתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were the exploits|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb of Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֑ע\rb*, \rb who won|וְלוֹ־\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb along with the three|בִּשְׁלוֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb mighty men|הַגִּבֹּרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb He was most honored|נִכְבָּד֙\rb* \rb among|מִן־\rb* \rb the Thirty|הַשְּׁלוֹשִׁ֗ים\rb*,\rb |הִנּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb but he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb become|בָ֑א\rb* \rb one of|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Three|הַשְּׁלוֹשָׁ֖ה\rb*. \rb And David|דָוִ֖יד\rb* \rb appointed him|וַיְשִׂימֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his guard|מִשְׁמַעְתּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Now these were the mighty men|וְגִבּוֹרֵ֖י\rb*\rb |הַחֲיָלִ֑ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb |עֲשָׂה־\rb* \rb Asahel|אֵל֙\rb* \rb the brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*,
\li1 \rb Elhanan|אֶלְחָנָ֥ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Dodo|דּוֹד֖וֹ\rb* \rb of|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Bethlehem|לָֽחֶם׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 27 \rb Shammoth|שַׁמּוֹת֙\rb* \rb the Harorite|הַהֲרוֹרִ֔י\rb*,\f + \fr 11:27 \fqa Shammoth the Harorite \ft is a variant of \fqa Shammah the Harodite\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:25|2SA 23:25\ref*.\f*
\li1 \rb Helez|חֶ֖לֶץ\rb* \rb the Pelonite|הַפְּלוֹנִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 28 \rb Ira|עִירָ֤א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ikkesh|עִקֵּשׁ֙\rb* \rb the Tekoite|הַתְּקוֹעִ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Abiezer|אֲבִיעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb the Anathothite|הָעֲנְּתוֹתִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 29 \rb Sibbecai|סִבְּכַי֙\rb* \rb the Hushathite|הַחֻ֣שָׁתִ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Ilai|עִילַ֖י\rb* \rb the Ahohite|הָאֲחוֹחִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 30 \rb Maharai|מַהְרַי֙\rb* \rb the Netophathite|הַנְּטֹ֣פָתִ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Heled|חֵ֥לֶד\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Baanah|בַּֽעֲנָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Netophathite|הַנְּטוֹפָתִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 31 \rb Ithai|אִיתַ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 11:31 \fqa Ithai \ft is a variant of \fqa Ittai\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:29|2SA 23:29\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ribai|רִיבַ֗י\rb* \rb from Gibeah|מִגִּבְעַת֙\rb* \rb of the Benjamites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִ֔ןס\rb*,
\li1 \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Pirathonite|הַפִּרְעָתֹנִֽי׃\rb*,
\li1 \v 32 \rb Hurai|חוּרַי֙\rb*\f + \fr 11:32 \fqa Hurai \ft is a variant of \fqa Hiddai\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:30|2SA 23:30\ref*.\f* \rb from the brooks|מִנַּ֣חֲלֵי\rb*\f + \fr 11:32 \ft Or \fqa from the ravines\f* \rb of Gaash|גָ֔עַשׁס\rb*,
\li1 \rb Abiel|אֲבִיאֵ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 11:32 \fqa Abiel \ft is a variant of \fqa Abi-albon\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:31|2SA 23:31\ref*.\f* \rb the Arbathite|הָעַרְבָתִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 33 \rb Azmaveth|עַזְמָ֙וֶת֙\rb* \rb the Baharumite|הַבַּ֣חֲרוּמִ֔י\rb*,\f + \fr 11:33 \fqa Baharumite \ft is a variant of \fqa Barhumite\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:31|2SA 23:31\ref*.\f*
\li1 \rb Eliahba|אֶלְיַחְבָּ֖א\rb* \rb the Shaalbonite|הַשַּׁעַלְבֹנִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 34 \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֗י\rb* \rb of Hashem|הָשֵׁם֙\rb*\f + \fr 11:34 \fqa Hashem \ft is a variant of \fqa Jashen\ft ; see LXX and \ref 2 Samuel 23:32|2SA 23:32\ref*.\f* \rb the Gizonite|הַגִּ֣זוֹנִ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֥ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shagee|שָׁגֵ֖ה\rb* \rb the Hararite|הַהֲרָרִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 35 \rb Ahiam|אֲחִיאָ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Sachar|שָׂכָ֛ר\rb*\f + \fr 11:35 \fqa Sachar \ft is a variant of \fqa Sharar\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:33|2SA 23:33\ref*.\f* \rb the Hararite|הַהֲרָרִ֖י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Eliphal|אֱלִיפַ֥ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ur|אֽוּר׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 36 \rb Hepher|חֵ֚פֶר\rb* \rb the Mecherathite|הַמְּכֵ֣רָתִ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb the Pelonite|הַפְּלֹנִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 37 \rb Hezro|חֶצְרוֹ֙\rb* \rb the Carmelite|הַֽכַּרְמְלִ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Naarai|נַעֲרַ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ezbai|אֶזְבָּֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 38 \rb Joel|יוֹאֵל֙\rb* \rb the brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb* \rb of Nathan|נָתָ֔ן\rb*,
\li1 \rb Mibhar|מִבְחָ֖ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hagri|הַגְרִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 39 \rb Zelek|צֶ֖לֶק\rb* \rb the Ammonite|הָעַמּוֹנִ֑י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Naharai|נַחְרַי֙\rb* \rb the Beerothite|הַבֵּ֣רֹתִ֔י\rb*, \rb the armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֕א\rb*\rb |כְּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָֽה׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 40 \rb Ira|עִירָא֙\rb* \rb the Ithrite|הַיִּתְרִ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Gareb|גָּרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb the Ithrite|הַיִּתְרִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 41 \rb Uriah|אֽוּרִיָּה֙\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֔י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Zabad|זָבָ֖ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahlai|אַחְלָֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 42 \rb Adina|עֲדִינָ֨א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shiza|שִׁיזָ֜א\rb* \rb the Reubenite|הָרֽאוּבֵנִ֗י\rb*, \rb chief|רֹ֛אשׁ\rb* \rb of the Reubenites|לָרֽאוּבֵנִ֖י\rb*, \rb and the thirty|שְׁלוֹשִֽׁים׃ס\rb* \rb with him|וְעָלָ֥יו\rb*,
\li1 \v 43 \rb Hanan|חָנָן֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Maacah|מַעֲכָ֔ה\rb*,
\li1 \rb Joshaphat|וְיוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb the Mithnite|הַמִּתְנִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 44 \rb Uzzia|עֻזִיָּ֖א\rb* \rb the Ashterathite|הָעֲשְׁתְּרָתִ֑י\rb*,
\li1 \rb Shama|שָׁמָע֙\rb* \rb and Jeiel|וִיעוּאֵל\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Hotham|חוֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb the Aroerite|הָעֲרֹעֵרִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 45 \rb Jediael|יְדִֽיעֲאֵל֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shimri|שִׁמְרִ֔י\rb* \rb and his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb Joha|וְיֹחָ֥א\rb* \rb the Tizite|הַתִּיצִֽי׃ס\rb*,
\li1 \v 46 \rb Eliel|אֱלִיאֵל֙\rb* \rb the Mahavite|הַֽמַּחֲוִ֔ים\rb*,
\li1 \rb Jeribai|וִירִיבַ֥י\rb* \rb and Joshaviah|וְיוֹשַׁוְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Elnaam|אֶלְנָ֑עַם\rb*,
\li1 \rb Ithmah|וְיִתְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Moabite|הַמּוֹאָבִֽי׃\rb*,
\li1 \v 47 \rb Eliel|אֱלִיאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb Obed|וְעוֹבֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb and Jaasiel|וְיַעֲשִׂיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb the Mezobaite|הַמְּצֹבָיָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 The Mighty Men Join David at Ziklag
\p \v 1 \rb Now these were the men|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb who came|הַבָּאִ֤ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb at Ziklag|לְצִ֣יקְלַ֔ג\rb*, \rb while|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb he was still banished|עָצ֔וּר\rb* \rb from the presence|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kish|קִ֑ישׁ\rb* (\rb they|וְהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb were among the mighty men|בַּגִּבּוֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb who helped him|עֹזְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb in battle|הַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*; \v 2 \rb they were archers|נֹ֣שְׁקֵי\rb*\rb |קֶ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb using both the right|מַיְמִינִ֤ים\rb* \rb and left hands|וּמַשְׂמִאלִים֙\rb* \rb to sling stones|בָּֽאֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and shoot arrows|וּבַחִצִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |בַּקָּ֑שֶׁת\rb*; \rb and they were Saul’s|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb kinsmen|מֵאֲחֵ֥י\rb* \rb from Benjamin|מִבִּנְיָמִֽן׃\rb*):
\b 
\li1 \v 3 \rb Ahiezer|אֲחִיעֶ֜זֶר\rb* \rb their chief|הָרֹ֨אשׁ\rb* \rb and Joash|וְיוֹאָ֗שׁ\rb*, \rb who were the sons|בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of Shemaah|הַשְּׁמָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb the Gibeathite|הַגִּבְעָתִ֔י\rb*;
\li1 \rb Jeziel|וִיזוּאֵל\rb* \rb and Pelet|וָפֶ֖לֶט\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Azmaveth|עַזְמָ֑וֶת\rb*;
\li1 \rb Beracah|וּבְרָכָ֕ה\rb*;
\li1 \rb Jehu|וְיֵה֖וּא\rb* \rb the Anathothite|הָעֲנְּתֹתִֽי׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 4 \rb Ishmaiah|וְיִֽשְׁמַֽעְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb the Gibeonite|הַגִּבְעוֹנִ֛י\rb*, \rb a mighty man|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb among the Thirty|בַּשְּׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and a leader over|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the Thirty|הַשְּׁלֹשִֽׁים׃\rb*;
\li1 \rb Jeremiah|וְיִרְמְיָ֤ה\rb*, \rb Jahaziel|וְיַחֲזִיאֵל֙\rb*, \rb Johanan|וְי֣וֹחָנָ֔ן\rb*, \rb and Jozabad|וְיוֹזָבָ֖ד\rb* \rb the Gederathite|הַגְּדֵרָתִֽי׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 5 \rb Eluzai|אֶלְעוּזַ֤י\rb*, \rb Jerimoth|וִירִימוֹת֙\rb*, \rb Bealiah|וּבְעַלְיָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Shemariah|וּשְׁמַרְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and Shephatiah|וּשְׁפַטְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the Haruphite|הַחֲרִיפִי׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 6 \rb Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֡ה\rb*, \rb Isshiah|וְ֠יִשִּׁיָּהוּ\rb*, \rb Azarel|וַעֲזַרְאֵ֧ל\rb*, \rb Joezer|וְיוֹעֶ֛זֶר\rb*, \rb and Jashobeam|וְיָשָׁבְעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb who were Korahites|הַקָּרְחִֽים׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 7 \rb and Joelah|וְיוֹעֵאלָ֧ה\rb* \rb and Zebadiah|וּזְבַדְיָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jeroham|יְרֹחָ֖ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Gedor|הַגְּדֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Some|וּמִן־\rb* \rb Gadites|הַגָּדִ֡י\rb* \rb defected|נִבְדְּל֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֩\rb* \rb at his stronghold|לַמְצַ֨ד\rb* \rb in the wilderness|מִדְבָּ֜רָה\rb*. \rb They were mighty|גִּבֹּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of valor|הַחַ֗יִל\rb*, \rb trained|צָבָא֙\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb experts|עֹרְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb with the shield|צִנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and spear|וָרֹ֑מַח\rb*, \rb whose faces were like|פְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the faces|וּפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of lions|אַרְיֵה֙\rb* \rb and who were as swift|לְמַהֵֽר׃ס\rb* \rb as gazelles|וְכִצְבָאיִ֥ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶהָרִ֖ים\rb*:
\li1 \v 9 \rb Ezer|עֵ֖זֶר\rb* \rb the chief|הָרֹ֑אשׁ\rb*, \rb Obadiah|עֹבַדְיָה֙\rb* \rb the second in command|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*, \rb Eliab|אֱלִיאָ֖ב\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִשִֽׁי׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb Mishmannah|מִשְׁמַנָּה֙\rb* \rb the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֔י\rb*, \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb the fifth|הַחֲמִשִֽׁי׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb Attai|עַתַּי֙\rb* \rb the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֔י\rb*, \rb Eliel|אֱלִיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִֽי׃\rb*, \v 12 \rb Johanan|יֽוֹחָנָן֙\rb* \rb the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֔י\rb*, \rb Elzabad|אֶלְזָבָ֖ד\rb* \rb the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִֽי׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִ֔יס\rb*, \rb and Machbanai|מַכְבַּנַּ֖י\rb* \rb the eleventh|עַשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb Gadites|מִבְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֖ד\rb* \rb were army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb* \rb commanders|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb*, \rb the least of whom|הַקָּטָ֔ן\rb* \rb was a match for a hundred|לְמֵאָה֙\rb*, \rb and the greatest|וְהַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb for a thousand|לְאָֽלֶף׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are|הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb the ones who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb crossed|עָבְר֤וּ\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb in the first|הָרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb when it was overflowing|מְמַלֵּ֖א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its banks|גִּדיֹתָיו\rb*, \rb and they put to flight|וַיַּבְרִ֙יחוּ֙\rb* \rb all those|כָּל־\rb* \rb in the valleys|הָ֣עֲמָקִ֔ים\rb*, \rb both to the east|לַמִּזְרָ֖ח\rb* \rb and to the west|וְלַֽמַּעֲרָֽב׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Other Benjamites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִן֙\rb* \rb and some men from Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb also came|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִֽיד׃\rb* \rb in his stronghold|לַמְצָ֖ד\rb*. \v 17 \rb And David|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb went out|דָוִיד֮\rb* \rb to meet them|לִפְנֵיהֶם֒\rb*,\rb |וַיַּ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb saying|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֔ם\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you have come|בָּאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb in peace|לְשָׁל֞וֹם\rb* \rb to help me|לְעָזְרֵ֔נִי\rb*, \rb my|לִּ֧י\rb* \rb heart|לֵבָ֖ב\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb united|לְיָ֑חַד\rb* \rb with you|עֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb*; \rb but if|וְאִֽם־\rb* \rb you have come to betray me|לְרַמּוֹתַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to my enemies|לְצָרַ֗י\rb* \rb when my hands|בְּכַפַּ֔י\rb* \rb are free|בְּלֹ֤א\rb* \rb of violence|חָמָס֙\rb*, \rb may the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb see it|יֵ֛רֶא\rb* \rb and judge you|וְיוֹכַֽח׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Then the Spirit|וְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb came upon|לָבְשָׁ֗ה\rb* \rb Amasai|עֲמָשַׂי֮\rb*, \rb the chief|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the Thirty, and he said|הַשְּׁלוֹשִׁים\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb We are yours|לְךָ֤\rb*, \rb O David|דָוִיד֙\rb*!
\q2 \rb We are with you|וְעִמְּךָ֣\rb*, \rb O son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֔י\rb*!
\q1 \rb Peace|שָׁל֨וֹם׀\rb*, \rb peace|שָׁל֜וֹם\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֗\rb*,
\q2 \rb and peace|וְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb to your helpers|לְעֹ֣זְרֶ֔ךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb helps you|עֲזָרְךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb received them|וַיְקַבְּלֵ֣ם\rb* \rb and made them|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖ם\rb* \rb leaders|בְּרָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of his troops|הַגְּדֽוּד׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Some from|נָפְל֣וּ\rb* \rb Manasseh|וּמִֽמְּנַשֶּׁ֞ה\rb* \rb defected|עַל־\rb* \rb to David|דָּוִ֗יד\rb* \rb when he went|בְּבֹא֨וֹ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֧ים\rb* \rb to fight|עַל־\rb* \rb against|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb Saul|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*. (\rb They did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb help the Philistines|עֲזָרֻ֑ם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb rulers|סַרְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb consulted|בְעֵצָ֗ה\rb* \rb and sent David away|שִׁלְּחֻ֜הוּ\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb It will cost us our heads|בְּרָאשֵׁ֕ינוּ\rb* \rb if he defects|יִפּ֖וֹל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָ֥יו\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*.”) \v 20 \rb When David went|בְּלֶכְתּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ziklag|צִֽיקְלַ֗ג\rb*, \rb these men of Manasseh|מִֽמְּנַשֶּׁ֡ה\rb* \rb defected|נָפְל֣וּ\rb* \rb to him|עָלָ֣יו׀\rb*:
\li1 \rb Adnah|עַ֠דְנַח\rb*, \rb Jozabad|וְיוֹזָבָ֤ד\rb*, \rb Jediael|וִידִֽיעֲאֵל֙\rb*, \rb Michael|וּמִיכָאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb Jozabad|וְיוֹזָבָ֔ד\rb*, \rb Elihu|וֶאֱלִיה֖וּא\rb*, \rb and Zillethai|וְצִלְּתָ֑י\rb*, \rb chiefs|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Manasseh|לִמְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb They|וְהֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb helped|עָזְר֤וּ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb against|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the raiders|הַגְּד֔וּד\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they were|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּ֑ם\rb* \rb mighty men|גִבּ֥וֹרֵי\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֖יִל\rb* \rb and commanders|שָׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the army|בַּצָּבָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb at that time|לְעֶת־\rb* \rb men came|יָבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb after day|בְּי֔וֹם\rb* \rb to help him|לְעָזְר֑וֹ\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he had a great|גָד֖וֹל\rb* \rb army|לְמַחֲנֶ֥ה\rb*, \rb like the army|כְּמַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\s1 David’s Army Grows at Hebron
\p \v 23 \rb Now these are|וְ֠אֵלֶּה\rb* \rb the numbers|מִסְפְּרֵ֞י\rb* \rb of men|רָאשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb armed|הֶֽחָלוּץ֙\rb* \rb for battle|לַצָּבָ֔א\rb* \rb who came|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb at Hebron|חֶבְר֑וֹנָה\rb* \rb to turn Saul’s|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb over|לְהָסֵ֞ב\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*, \rb in accordance with the word of|כְּפִ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*:
\pmo \v 24 \rb From Judah|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*: \rb 6,800|שֵׁ֧שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb armed|חֲלוּצֵ֥י\rb* \rb troops|צָבָֽא׃ס\rb* \rb bearing|נֹשְׂאֵ֥י\rb* \rb shields|צִנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and spears|וָרֹ֑מַח\rb*.
\pmo \v 25 \rb From|מִן־\rb* \rb Simeon|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |שִׁמְע֗וֹן\rb*: \rb 7,100|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּמֵאָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb mighty men|גִּבּ֤וֹרֵי\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֙יִל֙\rb*, \rb ready for battle|לַצָּבָ֔א\rb*.
\pmo \v 26 \rb From|מִן־\rb* \rb Levi|בְּנֵי֙\rb*\rb |הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb*: \rb 4,600|אַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃ס\rb*, \v 27 \rb including Jehoiada|וִיהוֹיָדָ֖ע\rb*, \rb leader|הַנָּגִ֣יד\rb* \rb of the house of Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb*, \rb with|וְעִמּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb 3,700|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַ֥ע\rb* \rb men|מֵאֽוֹת׃ס\rb*, \v 28 \rb and Zadok|וְצָד֥וֹק\rb*, \rb a mighty|גִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb young man|נַ֖עַר\rb* \rb of valor|חָ֑יִל\rb*, \rb with 22|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנָֽיִם׃ס\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb from his own family|אָבִ֥יו\rb*\rb |וּבֵית־\rb*.
