\c 13
\s1 David Fetches the Ark
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 6:1–4|2SA 6:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֗יד\rb* \rb conferred|וַיִּוָּעַ֣ץ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his leaders|נָגִֽיד׃\rb*, \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִ֛ים\rb* \rb and of hundreds|וְהַמֵּא֖וֹת\rb*. \v 2 \rb And he|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to the whole|לְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it seems good|ט֜וֹב\rb* \rb to you|עֲלֵיכֶ֨ם\rb*, \rb and if this is|וּמִן־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*, \rb let us send word|נִשְׁלְחָ֞ה\rb* \rb far and wide|נִפְרְצָה֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the rest|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb of our brothers|אַחֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the land|אַרְצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and also|וְעִמָּהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֥ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb in their cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and pasturelands|מִגְרְשֵׁיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that they may join|וְיִקָּבְצ֖וּ\rb* \rb us|אֵלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then let us bring back|וְנָסֵ֛בָּה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb we did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb inquire of Him|דְרַשְׁנֻ֖הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 13:3 \ft Or \fqa of it\f* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb And|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this proposal|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb seemed|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb right|יָשַׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*, \rb the whole|כָֽל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb agreed to it|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb*.\rb |כֵּ֑ן\rb* \v 5 \rb So David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיַּקְהֵ֤ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the River Shihor|שִׁיח֥וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 13:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa from the Shihor\f* \rb in Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to Lebo-hamath|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |חֲמָ֑ת\rb*,\rb |לְהָבִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to bring|לְב֣וֹא\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |מִקִּרְיַ֖ת\rb* \rb from Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb to Baalah|בַּעֲלָ֔תָה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb of|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Judah|לִיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* (\rb |קִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb that is, Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִ֖ים\rb*) \rb to bring up|לְהַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb who is enthroned|יוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb between the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֖ים\rb* — \rb the ark that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is called|נִקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb by the Name|שֵֽׁם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 13:6 \ft Or \fqa the ark of God, which is called by the Name of the LORD who is enthroned between the cherubim\ft ; or \fqa the ark of God, the LORD, who is enthroned between the cherubim, where His Name is called\f* \v 7 \rb So they carried|וַיַּרְכִּ֜יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of Abinadab|אֲבִינָדָ֑ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a new|חֲדָשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb cart|עֲגָלָ֣ה\rb*, \rb with Uzzah|וְעֻזָּ֣א\rb* \rb and Ahio|וְאַחְי֔וֹ\rb* \rb guiding|נֹהֲגִ֖ים\rb* \rb the cart|בָּעֲגָלָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Uzzah Touches the Ark
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 6:5–11|2SA 6:5-11\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb David|וְדָוִ֣יד\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb were celebrating|מְשַׂחֲקִ֛ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their might|עֹ֑ז\rb*, \rb with songs|וּבְשִׁירִ֤ים\rb* \rb and on harps|וּבְכִנֹּרוֹת֙\rb* \rb and lyres|וּבִנְבָלִ֣ים\rb*, \rb with tambourines|וּבְתֻפִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb cymbals|וּבִמְצִלְתַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and trumpets|וּבַחֲצֹצְרֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When they came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|גֹּ֣רֶן\rb* \rb of Chidon|כִּידֹ֑ן\rb*,\f + \fr 13:9 \fqa Chidon \ft is a variant of \fqa Nacon\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 6:6|2SA 6:6\ref*.\f* \rb Uzzah|עֻזָּ֜א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb and took hold|לֶאֱחֹז֙\rb* \rb of|אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הָ֣אָר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the oxen|הַבָּקָֽר׃\rb* \rb had stumbled|שָֽׁמְט֖וּ\rb*. \v 10 \rb And the anger|אַ֤ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Uzzah|בְּעֻזָּ֔א\rb*, \rb and He struck him|וַיַּכֵּ֕הוּ\rb* \rb down|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had put|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֑וֹן\rb*. \rb So he died|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then David|לְדָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb became angry|וַיִּ֣חַר\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had burst forth|פָרַ֧ץ\rb*\rb |פֶּ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb against Uzzah|בְּעֻזָּ֑א\rb*. \rb So he named|וַיִּקְרָ֞א\rb* \rb that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֤וֹם\rb*\rb |פֶּ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Perez-uzzah|עֻזָּ֔א\rb*,\f + \fr 13:11 \fqa Perez-uzzah \ft means \fqa outbreak against Uzzah\ft .\f* \rb as it is called to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb That|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb David|דָוִיד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb feared|וַיִּירָ֤א\rb* \rb God|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and asked|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb How|הֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb can I ever bring|אָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*?” \v 13 \rb So he|דָּוִ֧יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb move|הֵסִ֨יר\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֛וֹן\rb* \rb with him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb to the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*; \rb instead, he took|וַיַּטֵּ֕הוּ\rb* \rb it aside|אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |עֹבֵֽד־\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֖ם\rb* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Thus the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb remained|וַיֵּשֶׁב֩\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the family|בֵּ֨ית\rb*\rb |עֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֛ם\rb* \rb in his house|בְּבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֧רֶךְ\rb*\rb |עֹבֵֽד־\rb* \rb his|אֱדֹ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb and everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he owned|לֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 David’s Family Grows
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 5:12–16|2SA 5:12-16\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now Hiram|חִירָם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹ֥ר\rb* \rb sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb* \rb envoys|מַלְאָכִים֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֒\rb*, \rb along with cedar|אֲרָזִ֔ים\rb* \rb logs|וַעֲצֵ֣י\rb*, \rb stonemasons|וְחָרָשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |קִ֔יר\rb*, \rb and carpenters|וְחָרָשֵׁ֖י\rb*\rb |עֵצִ֑ים\rb*, \rb to build|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb a palace|בָּֽיִת׃\rb* \rb for him|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \v 2 \rb And David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb realized|וַיֵּ֣דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had established him|הֱכִינ֧וֹ\rb* \rb as king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb had highly|לְמַ֙עְלָה֙\rb* \rb exalted|נִשֵּׂ֤את\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַלְכוּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb for the sake|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb of His people|עַמּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb And David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb more|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb became the father|וַיּ֧וֹלֶד\rb* \rb of more|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֥ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb These|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the children born|הַיְלוּדִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָיוּ־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*: \rb Shammua|שַׁמּ֣וּעַ\rb*,\f + \fr 14:4 \fqa Shammua \ft is a variant of \fqa Shimea\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 3:5|1CH 3:5\ref*.\f* \rb Shobab|וְשׁוֹבָ֔ב\rb*, \rb Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb*, \rb Solomon|וּשְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb Ibhar|וְיִבְחָ֥ר\rb*, \rb Elishua|וֶאֱלִישׁ֖וּעַ\rb*, \rb Elpelet|וְאֶלְפָּֽלֶט׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb Nogah|וְנֹ֥גַהּ\rb*, \rb Nepheg|וְנֶ֖פֶג\rb*, \rb Japhia|וְיָפִֽיעַ׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb Elishama|וֶאֱלִישָׁמָ֥ע\rb*, \rb Beeliada|וּבְעֶלְיָדָ֖ע\rb*,\f + \fr 14:7 \fqa Beeliada \ft is a variant of \fqa Eliada\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 5:16|2SA 5:16\ref*.\f* \rb and Eliphelet|וֶאֱלִיפָֽלֶט׃\rb*.
\s1 Two Victories over the Philistines
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 5:17–25|2SA 5:17-25\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb When the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb had been anointed|נִמְשַׁ֨ח\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb they|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb went|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb in search|לְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of him|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*; \rb but David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb learned of this|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb and went out|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb to face them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Now the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֑אוּ\rb* \rb and raided|וַֽיִּפְשְׁט֖וּ\rb* \rb the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Rephaim|רְפָאִֽים׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb So David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֨ל\rb* \rb of God|בֵּאלֹהִים֙\rb*, “\rb Should I go up|הַאֶֽעֱלֶה֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּיִּים\rb*? \rb Will You deliver them|וּנְתַתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb into my hand|בְּיָדִ֑י\rb*?”
\p “\rb Go|עֲלֵ֔ה\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, “\rb for I will deliver them|וּנְתַתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb So David and his men went up|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb*\rb |בְּבַֽעַל־\rb* \rb to Baal-perazim|פְּרָצִים֮\rb*, \rb where he|דָּוִיד֒\rb* \rb defeated|וַיַּכֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb the Philistines|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb and|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Like a bursting|כְּפֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb flood|מָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has burst out|פָּרַ֨ץ\rb* \rb against my enemies|אוֹיְבַ֛י\rb* \rb by my hand|בְּיָדִ֖י\rb*.” \rb So|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb they called|קָֽרְא֛וּ\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |בַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb Baal-perazim|פְּרָצִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:11 \fqa Baal-perazim \ft means \fqa The Lord Bursts Out\ft .\f* \v 12 \rb There|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the Philistines abandoned|וַיַּעַזְבוּ־\rb* \rb their gods|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb that they be burned|וַיִּשָּׂרְפ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵֽשׁ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Once again|וַיֹּסִ֤יפוּ\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb raided|וַֽיִּפְשְׁט֖וּ\rb* \rb the valley|בָּעֵֽמֶק׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb So David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb again|ע֤וֹד\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֨ל\rb* \rb of God|בֵּֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb who|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb march up|תַֽעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb after them|אַֽחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb but circle around|הָסֵב֙\rb* \rb them|מֵֽעֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and attack|וּבָ֥אתָ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in front of|מִמּ֥וּל\rb* \rb the balsam trees|הַבְּכָאִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:14 \ft Or \fqa aspen trees \ft or \fqa poplar trees\ft ; also in verse 15\f* \v 15 \rb As soon as|וִ֠יהִי\rb* \rb you hear|כְּֽשָׁמְעֲךָ֞\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of marching|הַצְּעָדָה֙\rb* \rb in the tops|בְּרָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the balsam trees|הַבְּכָאִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |אָ֖ז\rb* \rb move out|תֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to battle|בַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb because this will mean that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb has gone out|יָצָ֤א\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to strike|לְהַכּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb had commanded him|צִוָּ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb and they struck down|וַיַּכּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the army of|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb all the way|וְעַד־\rb* \rb from Gibeon|מִגִּבְע֖וֹן\rb* \rb to Gezer|גָּֽזְרָה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And David’s|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb fame|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb into every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb land|הָֽאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb caused|נָתַ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb* \rb to fear him|פַּחְדּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*.
\c 15
\s1 Preparing to Move the Ark
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 6:12–15|2SA 6:12-15\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb David constructed|וַיַּֽעַשׂ־\rb* \rb buildings|בָתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for himself|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb and he prepared|וַיָּ֤כֶן\rb* \rb a place|מָקוֹם֙\rb* \rb for the ark|לַֽאֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and pitched|וַיֶּט־\rb* \rb a tent|אֹֽהֶל׃\rb* \rb for it|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \v 2 \rb Then|אָ֚ז\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb No|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb one but|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb may carry|לָשֵׂאת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb has chosen them|בָּחַ֣ר\rb* \rb to carry|לָשֵׂ֞את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and to minister|וּֽלְשָׁרְת֖וֹ\rb* \rb before Him|עַד־\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb And David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיַּקְהֵ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb to bring up|לְהַעֲלוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|מְקוֹמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had prepared|הֵכִ֥ין\rb* \rb for it|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Then he|דָּוִ֛יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered together|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֥ף\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַֽהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 5 \rb From the Kohathites|לִבְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |קְהָ֑ת\rb*, \rb Uriel|אוּרִיאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the chief|הַשָּׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and 120|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb of his relatives|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*;
\li1 \v 6 \rb from the Merarites|לִבְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |מְרָרִ֑י\rb*, \rb Asaiah|עֲשָׂיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the chief|הַשָּׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and 220|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb of his relatives|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*;
\li1 \v 7 \rb from the Gershomites|לִבְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |גֵּרְשׁ֑וֹם\rb*,\f + \fr 15:7 \fqa Gershomites \ft is a variant of \fqa Gershonites\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 23:7|1CH 23:7\ref*.\f* \rb Joel|יוֹאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the chief|הַשָּׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and 130|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִֽׁים׃ס\rb* \rb of his relatives|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*;
\li1 \v 8 \rb from the Elizaphanites|לִבְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |אֱלִֽיצָפָ֑ן\rb*, \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the chief|הַשָּׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and 200|מָאתָֽיִם׃ס\rb* \rb of his relatives|וְאֶחָ֥יו\rb*;
\li1 \v 9 \rb from the Hebronites|לִבְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |חֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb Eliel|אֱלִיאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb the chief|הַשָּׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and 80|שְׁמוֹנִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb of his relatives|וְאֶחָ֥יו\rb*;
\li1 \v 10 \rb and from the Uzzielites|לִבְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |עֻזִּיאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb Amminadab|עַמִּינָדָ֣ב\rb* \rb the chief|הַשָּׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and 112|מֵאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃ס\rb* \rb of his relatives|וְאֶחָ֕יו\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb David|דָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִ֑ים\rb* \rb Zadok|לְצָד֥וֹק\rb* \rb and Abiathar|וּלְאֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb* \rb and the Levites|וְלַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb Uriel|לְאֽוּרִיאֵ֤ל\rb*, \rb Asaiah|עֲשָׂיָה֙\rb*, \rb Joel|וְיוֹאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Eliel|וֶאֱלִיאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Amminadab|וְעַמִּינָדָֽב׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*, “\rb You|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb are the heads|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the Levitical|לַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb families|הָאָב֖וֹת\rb*. \rb You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb and your relatives|וַאֲחֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb must consecrate yourselves|הִֽתְקַדְּשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb so that you may bring|וְהַֽעֲלִיתֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb to the place|אֶל־\rb* \rb I have prepared|הֲכִינ֖וֹתִי\rb* \rb for it|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb It was because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you Levites|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb were not with us|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the first time|לְמַבָּרִ֥אשׁוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb burst forth in anger|פָּרַ֨ץ\rb* \rb against us|בָּ֔נוּ\rb*. \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb we did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb consult Him|דְרַשְׁנֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb about the proper order|כַּמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Priests and Levites Carry the Ark
\p \v 14 \rb So the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb consecrated themselves|וַיִּֽתְקַדְּשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb to bring up|לְהַעֲל֕וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And the Levites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb carried|וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb on their shoulders|בִּכְתֵפָ֥ם\rb* \rb with the poles|בַּמֹּט֖וֹת\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb in accordance with the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb David also|דָּוִיד֮\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the leaders|לְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֒\rb* \rb to appoint|לְהַֽעֲמִ֗יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their relatives|אֲחֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb as singers|הַמְשֹׁ֣רְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to lift up|לְהָרִֽים־\rb* \rb their voices|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb with joy|לְשִׂמְחָֽה׃פ\rb*, \rb accompanied by musical|שִׁ֛יר\rb* \rb instruments|בִּכְלֵי־\rb*— \rb harps|נְבָלִ֥ים\rb*, \rb lyres|וְכִנֹּר֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and cymbals|וּמְצִלְתָּ֑יִם\rb*\rb |מַשְׁמִיעִ֥ים\rb*. \v 17 \rb So the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb appointed|וַיַּעֲמִ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb Heman|הֵימָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joel|יוֹאֵ֔ל\rb*; \rb from|וּמִ֨ן־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb*, \rb Asaph|אָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Berechiah|בֶּֽרֶכְיָ֑הוּס\rb*; \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the Merarites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |מְרָרִי֙\rb*, \rb Ethan|אֵיתָ֖ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kushaiah|קֽוּשָׁיָֽהוּ׃\rb*; \v 18 \rb and with them|וְעִמָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb next in rank|הַמִּשְׁנִ֑ים\rb*: \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֡הוּ\rb*,\rb |בֵּ֡ן\rb*\f + \fr 15:18 \ft Several Hebrew manuscripts and most LXX manuscripts (see also verse 20 and \ref 1 Chronicles 16:5|1CH 16:5\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Zechariah son of \ft or \fqa Zechariah, Ben, \ft \f* \rb Jaaziel|וְיַֽעֲזִיאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb Shemiramoth|וּשְׁמִֽירָמ֡וֹת\rb*, \rb Jehiel|וִיחִיאֵ֣ל׀\rb*, \rb Unni|וְעֻנִּ֡י\rb*, \rb Eliab|אֱלִיאָ֡ב\rb*, \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Maaseiah|וּמַֽעֲשֵׂיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Mattithiah|וּמַתִּתְיָהוּ֩\rb*, \rb Eliphelehu|וֶאֱלִ֨יפְלֵ֜הוּ\rb*, \rb Mikneiah|וּמִקְנֵיָ֨הוּ\rb*, \rb and the gatekeepers|הַשֹּׁעֲרִֽים׃\rb*\rb |וְעֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֛ם\rb* \rb and Jeiel|וִֽיעִיאֵ֖ל\rb*.\f + \fr 15:18 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa Obed-edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah \ft or \fqa Obed-edom, Jeiel, and Ozias\f*
\p \v 19 \rb The musicians|וְהַמְשֹׁ֣רְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb Heman|הֵימָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Asaph|אָסָ֖ף\rb*, \rb and Ethan|וְאֵיתָ֑ן\rb* \rb were to sound|לְהַשְׁמִֽיעַ׃\rb* \rb the bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb cymbals|בִּמְצִלְתַּ֥יִם\rb*. \v 20 \rb Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֨ה\rb*, \rb Aziel|וַעֲזִיאֵ֜ל\rb*,\f + \fr 15:20 \fqa Aziel \ft is a variant of \fqa Jaaziel\ft ; see verse 18.\f* \rb Shemiramoth|וּשְׁמִֽירָמ֤וֹת\rb*, \rb Jehiel|וִֽיחִיאֵל֙\rb*, \rb Unni|וְעֻנִּ֣י\rb*, \rb Eliab|וֶֽאֱלִיאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb Maaseiah|וּמַעֲשֵׂיָ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb and Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb were to play the harps|בִּנְבָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb according to|עַל־\rb* \rb Alamoth|עֲלָמֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 15:20 \fqa Alamoth\ft is probably a musical or liturgical term; here and in \ref Psalm 46:1|PSA 46:1\ref*.\f* \v 21 \rb And Mattithiah|וּמַתִּתְיָ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb Eliphelehu|וֶאֱלִֽיפְלֵ֗הוּ\rb*, \rb Mikneiah|וּמִקְנֵיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*,\rb |וְעֹבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֔ם\rb*, \rb Jeiel|וִֽיעִיאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Azaziah|וַעֲזַזְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb were to lead the music|לְנַצֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \rb with lyres|בְּכִנֹּר֥וֹת\rb* \rb according to|עַל־\rb* \rb Sheminith|הַשְּׁמִינִ֖ית\rb*.\f + \fr 15:21 \fqa Sheminith\ft is probably a musical term; here and in \ref Psalm 6:1|PSA 6:1\ref* and Psalm 12:1.\f* \v 22 \rb Chenaniah|וּכְנַנְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the head|שַֽׂר־\rb* \rb Levite|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּמַשָּׂ֑א\rb* \rb was the director|יָסֹר֙\rb* \rb of the music|בַּמַּשָּׂ֔א\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he was|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb highly skilled|מֵבִ֖ין\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Berechiah|וּבֶֽרֶכְיָה֙\rb* \rb and Elkanah|וְאֶלְקָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb were to be guardians|שֹׁעֲרִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 15:23 \ft Literally \fqa gatekeepers\ft ; also in verse 24\f* \rb of the ark|לָאָרֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb Shebaniah|וּשְׁבַנְיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Joshaphat|וְיֽוֹשָׁפָ֡ט\rb*, \rb Nethanel|וּנְתַנְאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb Amasai|וַעֲמָשַׂ֡י\rb*, \rb Zechariah|וּ֠זְכַרְיָהוּ\rb*, \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֤הוּ\rb*, \rb and Eliezer|וֶֽאֱלִיעֶ֙זֶר֙\rb* — \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* — \rb were to blow|מַחֲצֹצְרִים\rb* \rb the trumpets|בַּחֲצֹ֣צְר֔וֹת\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*.\rb |וְעֹבֵ֤ד\rb* \rb Obed-edom|אֱדֹם֙\rb* \rb and Jehiah|וִֽיחִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb were also to be guardians|שֹׁעֲרִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the ark|לָאָרֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\s1 Moving the Ark to Jerusalem
\p \v 25 \rb So|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֛יד\rb*, \rb the elders|וְזִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb went|הַהֹֽלְכִ֗ים\rb* \rb with rejoicing|בְּשִׂמְחָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb to bring|לְֽהַעֲל֞וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |עֹבֵֽד־\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֖ם\rb*. \v 26 \rb And because God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb helped|בֶּעְזֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb who were carrying|נֹשְׂאֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb they sacrificed|וַיִּזְבְּח֥וּ\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָֽה־\rb* \rb bulls|פָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb rams|אֵילִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Now David|וְדָוִ֞יד\rb* \rb was dressed|מְכֻרְבָּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb in a robe|בִּמְעִ֣יל\rb* \rb of fine linen|בּ֗וּץ\rb*, \rb as were all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb who were carrying|הַנֹּשְׂאִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb as well as the singers|וְהַמְשֹׁ֣רְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and Chenaniah|וּכְנַנְיָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the director|הַשַּׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of music|הַמַּשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb for the singers|הַמְשֹֽׁרְרִ֑ים\rb*.\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb also wore a linen|בָּֽד׃\rb* \rb ephod|אֵפ֥וֹד\rb*. \v 28 \rb So all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb brought up|מַעֲלִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with shouting|בִּתְרוּעָה֙\rb*, \rb with the sounding|וּבְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of rams’ horns|שׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb and trumpets|וּבַחֲצֹצְר֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and with cymbals|וּבִמְצִלְתָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb and the music|מַשְׁמִעִ֕ים\rb* \rb of harps|בִּנְבָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb and lyres|וְכִנֹּרֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\s1 Michal’s Contempt for David
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 6:16|2SA 6:16\ref*)
\p \v 29 \rb As the ark|אֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb entering|בָּ֖א\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Michal|וּמִיכַ֨ל\rb* \rb looked down|נִשְׁקְפָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb from|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb a window|הַחַלּ֗וֹן\rb* \rb and saw|וַתֵּ֨רֶא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb dancing|מְרַקֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb and celebrating|וּמְשַׂחֵ֔ק\rb*, \rb and she despised|וַתִּ֥בֶז\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb in her heart|בְּלִבָּֽהּ׃פ\rb*.
\c 16
\s1 A Tent for the Ark
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 6:17–19|2SA 6:17-19\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb So they brought|וַיָּבִ֙יאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and placed|וַיַּצִּ֣יגוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb it inside|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the tent|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb had pitched|נָֽטָה־\rb* \rb for it|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \rb And they presented|וַיַּקְרִ֛יבוּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֥וֹת\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וּשְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb When David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb had finished|וַיְכַ֣ל\rb* \rb sacrificing|מֵהַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וְהַשְּׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb he blessed|וַיְבָ֥רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then he distributed|וַיְחַלֵּק֙\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb man|מֵאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |לְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb a loaf|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֔חֶם\rb*, \rb a date cake|וְאֶשְׁפָּ֖ר\rb*,\f + \fr 16:3 \ft Or \fqa a portion of meat\f* \rb and a raisin cake|וַאֲשִׁישָֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb David appointed|וַיִּתֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb to minister|מְשָׁרְתִ֑ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb to celebrate|וּלְהַזְכִּיר֙\rb*, \rb to give thanks|וּלְהוֹד֣וֹת\rb*, \rb and to praise|וּלְהַלֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*. \v 5 \rb Asaph|אָסָ֥ף\rb* \rb was the chief|הָרֹ֖אשׁ\rb*, \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֑ה\rb* \rb was second|וּמִשְׁנֵ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb then Jeiel|יְעִיאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb Shemiramoth|וּשְׁמִֽירָמ֡וֹת\rb*, \rb Jehiel|וִֽיחִיאֵ֡ל\rb*, \rb Mattithiah|וּמַתִּתְיָ֡ה\rb*, \rb Eliab|וֶאֱלִיאָ֡ב\rb*, \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָהוּ֩\rb*,\rb |וְעֹבֵ֨ד\rb* \rb Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֜ם\rb*, \rb and Jeiel|וִֽיעִיאֵ֗ל\rb*.\rb |בִּכְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb They were to play the harps|נְבָלִים֙\rb* \rb and lyres|וּבְכִנֹּר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb while Asaph|וְאָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb sounded|מַשְׁמִֽיעַ׃\rb* \rb the cymbals|בַּֽמְצִלְתַּ֥יִם\rb* \v 6 \rb and the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֑ים\rb* \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and Jahaziel|וְיַחֲזִיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb blew the trumpets|בַּחֲצֹצְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb regularly|תָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\s1 David’s Psalm of Thanksgiving
\r (\ref Psalm 105:1–15|PSA 105:1-15\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb*\rb |אָ֣ז\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb first|בָּרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb committed|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb to|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Asaph|אָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb and his associates|וְאֶחָֽיו׃פ\rb* \rb this song of thanksgiving|לְהֹד֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 8 “\rb Give thanks|הוֹד֤וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*; \rb call|קִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb upon His name|בִשְׁמ֔וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb make known|הוֹדִ֥יעוּ\rb* \rb His deeds|עֲלִילֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb among the nations|בָעַמִּ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Sing|שִׁ֤ירוּ\rb* \rb to Him|לוֹ֙\rb*, \rb sing praises|זַמְּרוּ־\rb* \rb to Him|ל֔וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb tell|שִׂ֖יחוּ\rb* \rb of all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb His wonders|נִפְלְאֹתָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Glory|הִֽתְהַֽלְלוּ֙\rb* \rb in His holy|קָדְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb let the hearts|לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb of those who seek|מְבַקְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb rejoice|יִשְׂמַ֕ח\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Seek out|דִּרְשׁ֤וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and His strength|וְעֻזּ֔וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb seek|בַּקְּשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb His face|פָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb always|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Remember|זִכְר֗וּ\rb* \rb the wonders|נִפְלְאֹתָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He has done|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb His marvels|מֹפְתָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and the judgments|וּמִשְׁפְּטֵי־\rb* \rb He has pronounced|פִֽיהוּ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 13 \rb O offspring|זֶ֚רַע\rb* \rb of His servant|עַבְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb O sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb His chosen ones|בְּחִירָֽיו׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb He|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb His judgments carry|מִשְׁפָּטָֽיו׃\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb Remember|זִכְר֤וּ\rb*\f + \fr 16:15 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa He remembers\ft ; see \ref Psalm 105:8|PSA 105:8\ref*.\f* \rb His covenant|בְּרִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the word|דָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb He ordained|צִוָּ֖ה\rb* \rb for a thousand|לְאֶ֥לֶף\rb* \rb generations|דּֽוֹר׃\rb*—
\q1 \v 16 \rb the covenant|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He made|כָּרַת֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the oath He swore|וּשְׁבוּעָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Isaac|לְיִצְחָֽק׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb He confirmed it|וַיַּעֲמִידֶ֤הָ\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb as a decree|לְחֹ֔ק\rb*,
\q2 \rb to Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as an everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb*:
\q1 \v 18 ‘\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb the land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֔עַן\rb*
\q2 \rb as the portion|חֶ֖בֶל\rb* \rb of your inheritance|נַחֲלַתְכֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb When they were|בִּֽהְיֽוֹתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb few|מְתֵ֣י\rb* \rb in number|מִסְפָּ֔ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb few indeed|כִּמְעַ֖ט\rb*, \rb and strangers|וְגָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the land|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 20 \rb they wandered|וַיִּֽתְהַלְּכוּ֙\rb* \rb from nation|מִגּ֣וֹי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb nation|גּ֔וֹי\rb*,
\q2 \rb from one kingdom|וּמִמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |עַ֥ם\rb* \rb another|אַחֵֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb He let|הִנִּ֤יחַ\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb man|לְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb oppress them|לְעָשְׁקָ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb He rebuked|וַיּ֥וֹכַח\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִֽים׃\rb* \rb on their behalf|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*:
\q1 \v 22 ‘\rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb touch|תִּגְּעוּ֙\rb* \rb My anointed ones|בִּמְשִׁיחָ֔י\rb*!
\q2 \rb Do no|אַל־\rb* \rb harm|תָּרֵֽעוּ׃פ\rb* \rb to My prophets|וּבִנְבִיאַ֖י\rb*!’
\s1 Sing to the LORD, All the Earth
\r (\ref Psalm 96:1–13|PSA 96:1-13\ref*)
\q1 \v 23 \rb Sing|שִׁ֤ירוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*.
\q2 \rb Proclaim|בַּשְּׂר֥וּ\rb* \rb His salvation|יְשׁוּעָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb day|מִיּֽוֹם־\rb* \rb after|אֶל־\rb* \rb day|י֖וֹם\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb Declare|סַפְּר֤וּ\rb* \rb His glory|כְּבוֹד֔וֹ\rb* \rb among the nations|בַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb His wonders|נִפְלְאֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb peoples|הָעַמִּ֖ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb great|גָד֨וֹל\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*, \rb and greatly|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb to be praised|וּמְהֻלָּל֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb He is to be feared|ה֖וּא\rb*\rb |וְנוֹרָ֥א\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the nations|הָעַמִּים֙\rb* \rb are idols|אֱלִילִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb but it is the LORD|וַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who made|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֥יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb Splendor|ה֤וֹד\rb* \rb and majesty|וְהָדָר֙\rb* \rb are before Him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb strength|עֹ֥ז\rb* \rb and joy|וְחֶדְוָ֖ה\rb* \rb fill His dwelling|בִּמְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb Ascribe|הָב֤וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb O families|מִשְׁפְּח֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the nations|עַמִּ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb ascribe|הָב֥וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb glory|כָּב֥וֹד\rb* \rb and strength|וָעֹֽז׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb Ascribe|הָב֥וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb due His name|שְׁמ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb bring|שְׂא֤וּ\rb* \rb an offering|מִנְחָה֙\rb* \rb and come|וּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb before Him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*.
\q1 \rb Worship|הִשְׁתַּחֲו֥וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the splendor|בְּהַדְרַת־\rb* \rb of His holiness|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*;
\q2 \v 30 \rb tremble|חִ֤ילוּ\rb* \rb before Him|מִלְּפָנָיו֙\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*.
\q1 \rb |אַף־\rb* \rb The world|תֵּבֵ֖ל\rb* \rb is firmly established|תִּכּ֥וֹן\rb*;
\q2 \rb it cannot|בַּל־\rb* \rb be moved|תִּמּֽוֹט׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 31 \rb Let the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb be glad|יִשְׂמְח֤וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb rejoice|וְתָגֵ֣ל\rb*.
\q1 \rb Let them say|וְיֹאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb among the nations|בַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb reigns|מָלָֽךְ׃\rb*!’
\q1 \v 32 \rb Let the sea|הַיָּם֙\rb* \rb resound|יִרְעַ֤ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and all that fills it|וּמְלוֹא֔וֹ\rb*;
\q1 \rb let the fields|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb exult|יַעֲלֹ֥ץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in them|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb Then|אָ֥ז\rb* \rb the trees|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the forest|הַיָּ֑עַר\rb* \rb will sing for joy|יְרַנְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb He is coming|בָ֖א\rb* \rb to judge|לִשְׁפּ֥וֹט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 34 \rb Give thanks|הוֹד֤וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He is good|ט֔וֹב\rb*;\rb |כִּ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 16:34 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb endures forever|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 35 \rb Then cry out|וְאִמְר֕וּ\rb*: ‘\rb Save us|הוֹשִׁיעֵ֙נוּ֙\rb*, \rb O God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our salvation|יִשְׁעֵ֔נוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb gather|וְקַבְּצֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb and deliver us|וְהַצִּילֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb that we may give thanks|לְהֹדוֹת֙\rb* \rb to Your holy|קָדְשֶׁ֔ךָ\rb* \rb name|לְשֵׁ֣ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb that we may glory|לְהִשְׁתַּבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb in Your praise|בִּתְהִלָּתֶֽךָ׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 36 \rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb everlasting|הָעוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb everlasting|הָעֹלָ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb Then all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb*, “\rb Amen|אָמֵ֔ן\rb*!” \rb and “Praise|וְהַלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*!”
\s1 Worship before the Ark
\p \v 37 \rb So David left|וַיַּֽעֲזָב־\rb* \rb Asaph|לְאָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb and his associates|וּלְאֶחָ֑יו\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb to minister|לְשָׁרֵ֞ת\rb* \rb there|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |הָאָר֛וֹן\rb* \rb regularly|תָּמִ֖יד\rb* \rb according to the daily|י֥וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb requirements|לִדְבַר־\rb*, \v 38 \rb |וְעֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb along with Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֛ם\rb* \rb and his sixty-eight|שִׁשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb relatives|וַאֲחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \rb Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jeduthun|יְדִית֛וּן\rb*, \rb and also Hosah|וְחֹסָ֖ה\rb*, \rb were to be gatekeepers|לְשֹׁעֲרִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb And|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb David left Zadok|צָד֣וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb and his fellow|וְאֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the tabernacle|מִשְׁכַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb at the high place|בַּבָּמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Gibeon|בְּגִבְעֽוֹן׃\rb* \v 40 \rb to regularly|תָּמִ֖יד\rb* \rb present|לְֽהַעֲלוֹת֩\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֨וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֧ח\rb* \rb of burnt offerings|הָעֹלָ֛ה\rb*, \rb morning|לַבֹּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb and evening|וְלָעָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb according to all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb that was written|הַכָּתוּב֙\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had commanded|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Israel to keep|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 41 \rb With them|וְעִמָּהֶם֙\rb* \rb were Heman|הֵימָ֣ן\rb*, \rb Jeduthun|וִֽידוּת֔וּן\rb*, \rb and the rest|וּשְׁאָר֙\rb* \rb of those chosen|הַבְּרוּרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and designated|נִקְּב֖וּ\rb* \rb by name|בְּשֵׁמ֑וֹת\rb* \rb to give thanks|לְהֹדוֹת֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* “\rb His loving devotion|חַסְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb endures forever|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 42 \rb Heman|הֵימָ֨ן\rb* \rb and Jeduthun|וִֽידוּת֜וּן\rb* \rb had with them|וְעִמָּהֶם֩\rb* \rb trumpets|חֲצֹצְר֤וֹת\rb* \rb and cymbals|וּמְצִלְתַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb for the music|לְמַשְׁמִיעִ֔ים\rb* \rb and instruments|וּכְלֵ֖י\rb* \rb for the songs|שִׁ֣יר\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*.\f + \fr 16:42 \ft Or \fqa instruments for the sacred music\f* \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jeduthun|יְדוּת֖וּן\rb* \rb were stationed at the gate|לַשָּֽׁעַר׃\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb Then all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb for their homes|לְבֵית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb returned home|וַיִּסֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb to bless|לְבָרֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his household|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\c 17
\s1 God’s Covenant with David
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 7:1–17|2SA 7:1-17\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb After|וַיְהִ֕י\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb had settled|יָשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb into his palace|בְּבֵית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb*, “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb*, \rb living|יוֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb in a house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of cedar|הָֽאֲרָזִ֔ים\rb*, \rb while the ark|וַאֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb a tent|יְרִיעֽוֹת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb And Nathan|נָתָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied to|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*, “\rb Do|עֲשֵׂ֑ה\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in your heart|בִּֽלְבָבְךָ֖\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb is with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But that|הַה֑וּא\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 4 “\rb Go|לֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: \rb You|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the one to build|תִּבְנֶה־\rb* \rb Me|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb a house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb in which to dwell|לָשָֽׁבֶת׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb dwelt|יָשַׁ֙בְתִּי֙\rb* \rb in a house|בְּבַ֔יִת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I brought|הֶעֱלֵ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel up out of Egypt|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\f + \fr 17:5 \fqa Out of Egypt\ft is implied, but not included in the Hebrew; see \ref 2 Samuel 7:6|2SA 7:6\ref*.\f* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb but I have moved|וָֽאֶהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb from tent|מֵאֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb tent|אֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb and dwelling to dwelling|וּמִמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb In all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb My journeys|הִתְהַלַּכְתִּי֮\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb have I ever asked|דִּבַּ֗רְתִּי\rb*\rb |הֲדָבָ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb any|אַחַד֙\rb* \rb of the leaders|שֹׁפְטֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 17:6 \ft Or \fqa judges\ft ; see verse 10.\f*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I appointed|צִוִּ֛יתִי\rb* \rb to shepherd|לִרְע֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* ‘\rb Why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb haven’t|לֹא־\rb* \rb you built|בְנִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb Me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb a house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of cedar|אֲרָזִֽים׃\rb*?’
\p \v 7 \rb Now|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb* \rb then|כֹּֽה־\rb*, \rb you are to tell|תֹאמַ֞ר\rb* \rb My servant|לְעַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֗ידס\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb took|לְקַחְתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb you from|מִן־\rb* \rb the pasture|הַנָּוֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb following|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֑אן\rb*, \rb to be|לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb the ruler|נָגִ֔יד\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb I have been|וָֽאֶהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֗\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have gone|הָלַ֔כְתָּ\rb*, \rb and I have cut off|וָאַכְרִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אוֹיְבֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from before you|מִפָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Now I will make|וְעָשִׂ֤יתִֽי\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֔ם\rb* \rb like that of|כְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb the greatest|הַגְּדוֹלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb And I will provide|וְשַׂמְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb a place|מָ֠קוֹם\rb* \rb for My people|לְעַמִּ֨י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb and will plant them|וּנְטַעְתִּ֙יהוּ֙\rb* \rb so that they may dwell in|וְשָׁכַ֣ן\rb* \rb a place of their own|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb* \rb and be disturbed|יִרְגַּ֖ז\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb more|ע֑וֹד\rb*. \rb No|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|יוֹסִ֤יפוּ\rb* \rb will the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of wickedness|עַוְלָה֙\rb* \rb oppress them|לְבַלֹּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb as they did|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb at the beginning|בָּרִאשׁוֹנָֽה׃\rb* \v 10 \rb and have done since the day|וּלְמִיָּמִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I appointed|צִוִּ֤יתִי\rb* \rb judges|שֹֽׁפְטִים֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb And I will subdue|וְהִכְנַ֖עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אוֹיְבֶ֑יךָ\rb*.
\p \rb Moreover , I declare|וָאַגִּ֣ד\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb will build|יִֽבְנֶה־\rb* \rb a house|וּבַ֖יִת\rb* \rb for you|לְּךָ֥\rb*. \v 11 \rb And|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your days|יָמֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb are fulfilled|מָלְא֤וּ\rb* \rb and you go to be|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb I will raise up|וַהֲקִֽימוֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your descendant|זַרְעֲךָ֙\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֶ֔יךָ\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb one of your own sons|מִבָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and I will establish|וַהֲכִינוֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַלְכוּתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb He|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb will build|יִבְנֶה־\rb* \rb a house|בָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb for Me|לִּ֖י\rb*, \rb and I will establish|וְכֹנַנְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his throne|כִּסְא֖וֹ\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will be|אֶֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb his|לּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Father|לְאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb My|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb son|לְבֵ֑ן\rb*. \rb And I will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb remove|אָסִ֣יר\rb* \rb My loving devotion|וְחַסְדִּי֙\rb* \rb from him|מֵֽעִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I removed it|הֲסִיר֔וֹתִי\rb* \rb from your predecessor|מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb But I will set him|וְהַֽעֲמַדְתִּ֛יהוּ\rb* \rb over My house|בְּבֵיתִ֥י\rb* \rb and My kingdom|וּבְמַלְכוּתִ֖י\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |הָעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and his throne|וְכִסְא֕וֹ\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb established|נָכ֖וֹן\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb So|כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb relayed|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽיד׃פ\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb entire|וּכְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb revelation|הֶחָז֣וֹן\rb*.
\s1 David’s Prayer of Thanksgiving
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 7:18–29|2SA 7:18-29\ref*)
\p \v 16 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb went in|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb*, \rb sat|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb am I|אֲנִ֞י\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*, \rb and what|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb is my house|בֵיתִ֔י\rb*, \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb You have brought me|הֲבִיאֹתַ֖נִי\rb* \rb this|עַד־\rb* \rb far|הֲלֹֽם׃\rb*? \v 17 \rb And as if this|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb was a small thing|וַתִּקְטַ֨ן\rb* \rb in Your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb You have spoken|וַתְּדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the future|לְמֵרָח֑וֹק\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb and have regarded me|וּרְאִיתַ֗נִי\rb* \rb as a man|הָאָדָ֛ם\rb*\rb |כְּת֧וֹר\rb* \rb of great distinction|הַֽמַּעֲלָ֖ה\rb*,\f + \fr 17:17 \ft Or \fqa and have shown me future generations\f* \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb more|יּוֹסִ֨יף\rb*\rb |ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb can David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb say to You|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb for honoring|לְכָב֣וֹד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb*? \rb For You|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb know|יָדָֽעְתָּ׃\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb*, \v 19 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֕ה\rb*.\f + \fr 17:19 \ft See \ref 2 Samuel 7:20|2SA 7:20\ref*; many translators \fqa \fv 18\fv*...For You know Your servant. \fv 19\fv*O LORD,\f* \rb For the sake|בַּעֲב֤וּר\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb and according to Your own heart|וּֽכְלִבְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb You have accomplished|עָשִׂ֕יתָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb great thing|הַגְּדוּלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and made known|לְהֹדִ֖יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these great promises|הַגְּדֻלּֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb there is none|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb like You|כָּמ֔וֹךָ\rb*, \rb and there is no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb but You|זוּלָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb according to everything|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we have heard|שָׁמַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb with our own ears|בְּאָזְנֵֽינוּ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And who|וּמִי֙\rb* \rb is like Your people|כְּעַמְּךָ֣\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* — \rb the one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb nation|גּ֥וֹי\rb* \rb on earth|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb went out|הָלַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb to redeem|לִפְדּ֧וֹת\rb* \rb as a people|עָ֗ם\rb* \rb for Himself|ל֣וֹ\rb*? \rb You made|לָשׂ֤וּם\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֚ם\rb* \rb for Yourself|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb through great|גְּדֻלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and awesome wonders|וְנֹרָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb by driving out|לְגָרֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִֽם׃\rb* \rb from before|מִפְּנֵ֧י\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֛\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You redeemed|פָּדִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb*. \v 22 \rb For You have made|וַ֠תִּתֵּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֨\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל׀\rb* \rb Your very own|לְךָ֛\rb*\rb |לְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and You|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb have become|הָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb let the word|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb You have spoken|דִּבַּ֤רְתָּ\rb* \rb concerning|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb* \rb be established|יֵאָמֵ֖ן\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Do|וַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have promised|דִּבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb*, \v 24 \rb so that Your name|שִׁמְךָ֤\rb* \rb will be established|וְ֠יֵֽאָמֵן\rb* \rb and magnified|וְיִגְדַּ֨ל\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb when it is said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb is God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb over Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.’ \rb And may the house|וּבֵית־\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb* \rb be established|נָכ֥וֹן\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֗י\rb*, \rb have revealed|גָּלִ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֹ֣זֶן\rb* \rb to Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb that You will build|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb for him|ל֖וֹ\rb*.\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Therefore|כֵּן֙\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb has found the courage|מָצָ֣א\rb* \rb to pray|לְהִתְפַּלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb You|אַתָּה־\rb* \rb are|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*! \rb And You have promised|וַתְּדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb goodness|הַטּוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb*. \v 27 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb You have been pleased|הוֹאַ֙לְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to bless|לְבָרֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb that it may continue|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb have blessed it|בֵּרַ֔כְתָּ\rb*, \rb and it will be blessed|וּמְבֹרָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\c 18
\s1 David’s Triumphs
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 8:1–14|2SA 8:1-14\ref*; \ref Psalm 60:1–12|PSA 60:1-12\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Some time later|וַיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb defeated|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb subdued them|וַיַּכְנִיעֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֛ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Gath|גַּ֥ת\rb* \rb and its villages|וּבְנֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb David also defeated|וַיַּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Moabites|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb*, \rb and they|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb became|וַיִּהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb subject|עֲבָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb and brought him|נֹשְׂאֵ֖י\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְחָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb As far as Hamath|חֲמָ֑תָה\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also defeated|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֥זֶר\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָ֖ה\rb*, \rb who had marched out|בְּלֶכְתּ֕וֹ\rb* \rb to establish|לְהַצִּ֥יב\rb* \rb his dominion|יָד֖וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 18:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa his hand\f* \rb along the Euphrates|פְּרָֽת׃\rb* \rb River|בִּֽנְהַר־\rb*. \v 4 \rb David|דָּוִ֨יד\rb* \rb captured|וַיִּלְכֹּד֩\rb* \rb from him|מִמֶּ֜נּוּ\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֗כֶב\rb*, \rb seven|וְשִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb charioteers|פָּֽרָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb foot soldiers|רַגְלִ֑י\rb*, \rb and he hamstrung|וַיְעַקֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |דָּוִיד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the horses|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb except a hundred|מֵ֥אָה\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb he kept|וַיּוֹתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb for the chariots|רָֽכֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When the Arameans|אֲרַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּרְמֶ֔שֶׂק\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to help|לַעְז֕וֹר\rb* \rb King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hadadezer|לַהֲדַדְעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָ֑ה\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*\rb |בַּאֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִֽים־\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb of their men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Then he|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb placed garrisons|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb*\f + \fr 18:6 \ft LXX and Vulgate (see also \ref 2 Samuel 8:6|2SA 8:6\ref* and Syriac); Hebrew does not include \fqa garrisons\ft .\f* \rb in Aram|בַּאֲרַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּרְמֶ֔שֶׂק\rb*, \rb and the Arameans|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb became|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb subject|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb and brought him|נֹשְׂאֵ֣י\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְחָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb made David|לְדָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb victorious|וַיּ֤וֹשַׁע\rb*\f + \fr 18:6 \ft Or \fqa the LORD saved David\ft ; also in verse 13\f* \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he went|הָלָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And David|דָּוִ֗יד\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb shields|שִׁלְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belonged|הָי֔וּ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the officers|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעָ֑זֶר\rb* \rb and brought them|וַיְבִיאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And from Tibhath|וּמִטִּבְחַ֤ת\rb*\f + \fr 18:8 \fqa Tibhath \ft is a variant of \fqa Tebah\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 8:8|2SA 8:8\ref* LXX.\f* \rb and Cun|וּמִכּוּן֙\rb*, \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֔זֶר\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb took|לָקַ֥ח\rb* \rb a large|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb amount|רַבָּ֣ה\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb*, \rb with which|בָּ֣הּ׀\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb Sea|יָ֤ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the pillars|הָֽעַמּוּדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and various|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb bronze|הַנְּחֹֽשֶׁת׃פ\rb* \rb articles|כְּלֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Tou|תֹּ֖עוּ\rb*\f + \fr 18:9 \fqa Tou \ft is a variant of \fqa Toi\ft ; also in verse 10; see \ref 2 Samuel 8:9|2SA 8:9\ref*.\f* \rb of Hamath|חֲמָ֑ת\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֕ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֔יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had defeated|הִכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|חֵ֖יל\rb* \rb of Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֥זֶר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָֽה׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Hadoram|הֲדֽוֹרָם־\rb*\f + \fr 18:10 \fqa Hadoram \ft is a variant of \fqa Joram\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 8:10|2SA 8:10\ref*.\f* \rb to greet|לִשְׁאוֹל\rb*\rb |ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb David|דָּ֠וִיד\rb*\rb |לְשָׁל֜וֹם\rb* \rb and bless him|וּֽלְבָרֲכ֗וֹ\rb* \rb for|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb fighting|נִלְחַ֤ם\rb* \rb and defeating|וַיַּכֵּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb Hadadezer|בַּהֲדַדְעֶ֙זֶר֙\rb*, \rb who|כִּי־\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |הֲדַדְעָ֑זֶר\rb* \rb had been|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb at war|מִלְחֲמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb with Tou|תֹּ֖עוּ\rb*. \rb Hadoram brought all kinds|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb of articles|כְּלֵ֛י\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb and silver|וָכֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb and bronze|וּנְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb dedicated|הִקְדִּ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb these|אֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb along with|עִם־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had carried off|נָשָׂ֖א\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb these nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* — \rb from Edom|מֵֽאֱד֤וֹם\rb* \rb and Moab|וּמִמּוֹאָב֙\rb*, \rb and from the Ammonites|וּמִבְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb Philistines|וּמִפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb and Amalekites|וּמֵֽעֲמָלֵֽק׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Moreover, Abishai|וְאַבְשַׁ֣י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֗ה\rb* \rb struck down|הִכָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb eighteen|שְׁמוֹנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb thousand|אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb Edomites|אֱדוֹם֙\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּגֵ֣יא\rb* \rb of Salt|הַמֶּ֔לַח\rb*. \v 13 \rb He placed|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb garrisons|נְצִיבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in Edom|בֶּֽאֱדוֹם֙\rb*, \rb and all|כָל־\rb* \rb the Edomites|אֱד֖וֹם\rb* \rb were|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb subject|עֲבָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֑יד\rb*. \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb victorious|וַיּ֤וֹשַׁע\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he went|הָלָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\s1 David’s Officers
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 8:15–18|2SA 8:15-18\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb Thus David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb administered|עֹשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb* \rb and righteousness|וּצְדָקָ֖ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 15 \rb Joab|וְיוֹאָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֖ה\rb* \rb was over|עַל־\rb* \rb the army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb*;
\li1 \rb Jehoshaphat|וִיהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahilud|אֲחִיל֖וּד\rb* \rb was the recorder|מַזְכִּֽיר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 16 \rb Zadok|וְצָד֧וֹק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahitub|אֲחִיט֛וּב\rb* \rb and Ahimelech|וַאֲבִימֶ֥לֶךְ\rb*\f + \fr 18:16 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, Vulgate, and Syriac (see also \ref 2 Samuel 8:17|2SA 8:17\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Abimelech\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb* \rb were priests|כֹּהֲנִ֑ים\rb*;
\li1 \rb Shavsha|וְשַׁוְשָׁ֖א\rb*\f + \fr 18:16 \fqa Shavsha \ft is also called \fqa Seraiah\ft , \fqa Sheva\ft , and \fqa Shisha\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 8:17|2SA 8:17\ref*, 2 Samuel 20:25, and 1 Kings 4:3.\f* \rb was the scribe|סוֹפֵֽר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 17 \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְה֣וֹיָדָ֔ע\rb* \rb was over|עַל־\rb* \rb the Cherethites|הַכְּרֵתִ֖י\rb* \rb and Pelethites|וְהַפְּלֵתִ֑י\rb*;
\li1 \rb and David’s|דָוִ֥יד\rb* \rb sons|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb were chief officials|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb at the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb* \rb side|לְיַ֥ד\rb*.
\c 19
\s1 David’s Messengers Disgraced
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 10:1–8|2SA 10:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Some time later|אַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb Nahash|נָחָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֕מָת\rb* \rb and was succeeded by|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 2 \rb And David|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will show|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֣סֶד׀\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb Hanun|חָנ֣וּן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nahash|נָחָ֗שׁ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֤יו\rb* \rb showed|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֔סֶד\rb* \rb to me|עִמִּי֙\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb to console Hanun|לְנַחֲמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb*. \rb But when David’s|דָוִ֜יד\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹאוּ֩\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֛וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |חָנ֖וּן\rb* \rb to console him|לְנַחֲמֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb the princes|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֩\rb* \rb to Hanun|לְחָנ֗וּן\rb*, “\rb Just because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb David has sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb comforters|מְנַחֲמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb do you really believe|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb he is|דָּוִ֤יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb showing respect|הַֽמְכַבֵּ֨ד\rb* \rb for your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb*? \rb Have not|הֲלֹ֡א\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb come|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃פ\rb*\rb |בַּ֠עֲבוּר\rb* \rb to explore|לַחְקֹ֨ר\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb spy it out|וּלְרַגֵּל֙\rb*, \rb and overthrow it|וְלַהֲפֹ֤ךְ\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb So Hanun|חָנ֜וּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִיד֙\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb*, \rb shaved their beards|וַֽיְגַלְּחֵ֔ם\rb*, \rb cut off|וַיִּכְרֹ֧ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their garments|מַדְוֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |בַּחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb at|עַד־\rb* \rb the hips|הַמִּפְשָׂעָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and sent them away|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When someone came|וַיֵּלְכוּ֩\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגִּ֨ידוּ\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֤יד\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb his men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers to meet them|לִקְרָאתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb since|כִּי־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb had been|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb thoroughly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb humiliated|נִכְלָמִ֣ים\rb*. \rb The king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb told them|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Stay|שְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in Jericho|בִֽירֵח֔וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your beards|זְקַנְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb have grown back|יְצַמַּ֥ח\rb*, \rb and then return|וְשַׁבְתֶּֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb When the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb realized that|וַיִּרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb they had become a stench|הִֽתְבָּאֲשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb Hanun|חָ֠נוּן\rb* \rb and the Ammonites|וּבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 19:6 \fqa 1,000 talents \ft is approximately 37.7 tons or 34.2 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb to hire|לִשְׂכֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb for themselves|לָ֠הֶם\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֖כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּפָרָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֨ם\rb* \rb Aram-naharaim|נַהֲרַ֜יִם\rb*,\f + \fr 19:6 \ft That is, Mesopotamia; \fqa Aram-naharaim \ft means \fqa Aram of the two rivers\ft , likely the region between the Euphrates and Balih Rivers in northwestern Mesopotamia.\f*\rb |וּמִן־\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֤ם\rb* \rb Aram-maacah|מַעֲכָה֙\rb*, \rb and Zobah|וּמִצּוֹבָ֔ה\rb*. \v 7 \rb So they hired|וַיִּשְׂכְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֡ם\rb* \rb thirty-two|שְׁנַיִם֩\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֜לֶף\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֗כֶב\rb*, \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Maacah|מַעֲכָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with his troops|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb who came|וַיָּבֹ֕אוּ\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb near|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Medeba|מֵידְבָ֑א\rb* \rb while the Ammonites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֗וֹן\rb* \rb were mustered from their cities|מֵעָ֣רֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb and marched out|נֶאֶסְפוּ֙\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb On hearing this|וַיִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|צָבָ֖א\rb* \rb of mighty men|הַגִּבּוֹרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb The Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb marched out|וַיֵּצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb and arrayed themselves|וַיַּֽעַרְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb for battle|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb while the kings|וְהַמְּלָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֔אוּ\rb* \rb stayed by themselves|לְבַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in the open country|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 David Defeats Ammon and Aram
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 10:9–19|2SA 10:9-19\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb When Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |הָיְתָ֧ה\rb* \rb the battle lines|הַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb before him|פָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and behind him|וְאָח֑וֹר\rb*, \rb he selected|וַיִּבְחַ֗ר\rb* \rb some of|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the best|בָּחוּר֙\rb* \rb men of Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and arrayed them|וַֽיַּעֲרֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb he placed|נָתַ֕ן\rb* \rb the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb under the command|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of his brother|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb Abishai|אַבְשַׁ֣י\rb*, \rb who arrayed them|וַיַּ֣עַרְכ֔וּ\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֖את\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb are too strong|תֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb* \rb for me|מִמֶּ֙נִּי֙\rb*,” \rb said Joab|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb then you will come|וְהָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb to my|לִּ֖י\rb* \rb rescue|לִתְשׁוּעָ֑הס\rb*. \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֛וֹן\rb* \rb are too strong|יֶֽחֶזְק֥וּ\rb* \rb for you|מִמְּךָ֖\rb*, \rb then I will come to your rescue|וְהוֹשַׁעְתִּֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Be strong|חֲזַ֤ק\rb* \rb and let us fight bravely|וְנִֽתְחַזְּקָה֙\rb* \rb for|בְּעַד־\rb* \rb our people|עַמֵּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and for|וּבְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb May the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb do|הַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb what is good|יַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb in His sight|בְּעֵינָ֖יו\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֜ב\rb* \rb and his troops|וְהָעָ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |עִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb advanced|וַיִּגַּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֖ם\rb*, \rb who fled|וַיָּנ֖וּסוּ\rb* \rb before|מִפָּנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb him|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb*. \v 15 \rb When the Ammonites|וּבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֤וֹן\rb* \rb saw|רָאוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb had fled|נָ֣ס\rb*, \rb they|הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb too|גַם־\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנ֣וּסוּ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb Joab’s brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb Abishai|אַבְשַׁ֣י\rb*, \rb and they entered|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑ירָה\rb*. \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb went back|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb When the Arameans|אֲרָ֗ם\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they had been defeated|נִגְּפוּ֮\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb they sent|וַֽיִּשְׁלְחוּ֙\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to bring|וַיּוֹצִ֣יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb more Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb from beyond|מֵעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֑ר\rb*,\f + \fr 19:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb with Shophach|וְשׁוֹפַ֛ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 19:16 \fqa Shophach \ft is a variant of \fqa Shobach\ft ; also in verse 18; see \ref 2 Samuel 10:16|2SA 10:16\ref*.\f* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of Hadadezer’s|הֲדַדְעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb army|צְבָ֥א\rb* \rb leading them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb When this was reported|וַיֻּגַּ֣ד\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֗יד\rb*, \rb he gathered|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֤ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb crossed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb advanced|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb toward|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָם֙\rb*, \rb and arrayed for battle|וַֽיַּעֲרֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb against them|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb When David|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb lined up|וַיַּעֲרֹ֨ךְ\rb* \rb to engage them|לִקְרַ֤את\rb* \rb in battle|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb they fought|וַיִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But the Arameans|אֲרָם֮\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּ֣נָס\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb and David|דָּוִ֜יד\rb*\rb |מֵאֲרָ֗ם\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּהֲרֹ֨ג\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb of their charioteers|רֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb foot soldiers|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |רַגְלִ֑י\rb*.\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb He also killed|הֵמִֽית׃\rb* \rb Shophach|שׁוֹפַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the commander|שַֽׂר־\rb* \rb of their army|הַצָּבָ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb When Hadadezer’s|הֲדַדְעֶ֗זֶר\rb* \rb subjects|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֞וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they had been defeated|נִגְּפוּ֙\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb they made peace|וַיַּשְׁלִ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb and became subject to him|וַיַּֽעַבְדֻ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb So the Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb were unwilling|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |אָבָ֣ה\rb* \rb to help|לְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb anymore|עֽוֹד׃פ\rb*.
\c 20
\s1 The Capture of Rabbah
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 12:26–31|2SA 12:26-31\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb In|לְעֵת֩\rb* \rb the spring|תְּשׁוּבַ֨ת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנָ֜ה\rb*,\f + \fr 20:1 \ft Literally \fqa At the turn of the year\f* \rb at the time when|לְעֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֗ים\rb* \rb march out to war|צֵ֣את\rb*, \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb led out|וַיִּנְהַ֣ג\rb* \rb the army|חֵ֨יל\rb*\rb |הַצָּבָ֜א\rb* \rb and ravaged|וַיַּשְׁחֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֗וֹן\rb*. \rb He came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to Rabbah|רַבָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and besieged it|וַיָּ֣צַר\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but David|וְדָוִ֖יד\rb* \rb remained|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*. \rb And Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb attacked|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb Rabbah|רַבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and demolished it|וַיֶּֽהֶרְסֶֽהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the crown|עֲטֶֽרֶת־\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֨ל\rb* \rb the head|רֹאשׁ֜וֹ\rb* \rb of their king|מַלְכָּם֩\rb*.\f + \fr 20:2 \ft Or \fqa from the head of Milcom\ft . Milcom, also called Molech, was god of the Ammonites; see \ref Leviticus 18:21|LEV 18:21\ref* and 1 Kings 11:7.\f* \rb It was found|וַֽיִּמְצָאָ֣הּ׀\rb* \rb to weigh|מִשְׁקַ֣ל\rb* \rb a talent|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֗ב\rb*\f + \fr 20:2 \fqa A talent \ft is approximately 75.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f* \rb and was set|וּבָהּ֙\rb* \rb with precious|יְקָרָ֔ה\rb* \rb stones|אֶ֣בֶן\rb*, \rb and it was|וַתְּהִ֖י\rb* \rb placed on|עַל־\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*. \rb And David took|הוֹצִ֖יא\rb* \rb a great amount|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb of plunder|וּשְׁלַ֥ל\rb* \rb from the city|הָעִ֛יר\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb David brought out|הוֹצִ֗יא\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb there|בָּ֜הּ\rb* \rb and put them to work|וַיָּ֨שַׂר\rb*\f + \fr 20:3 \ft Or \fqa cut them\f* \rb with saws|בַּמְּגֵרָ֜ה\rb*, \rb iron|הַבַּרְזֶל֙\rb* \rb picks|וּבַחֲרִיצֵ֤י\rb*, \rb and axes|וּבַמְּגֵר֔וֹת\rb*. \rb And he|דָוִ֔יד\rb* \rb did|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the same|וְכֵן֙\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the Ammonite|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb*. \rb Then David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֧שָׁב\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Battles against the Philistines
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 21:15–22|2SA 21:15-22\ref*)
\p \v 4 \rb Some time later|וַיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיכֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb war|מִלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb broke out|וַתַּעֲמֹ֧ד\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb at Gezer|בְּגֶ֖זֶר\rb*. \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Sibbecai|סִבְּכַ֣י\rb* \rb the Hushathite|הַחֻֽשָׁתִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb killed|הִכָּ֞ה\rb* \rb Sippai|סִפַּ֛י\rb*,\f + \fr 20:4 \fqa Sippai \ft is a variant of \fqa Saph\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 21:18|2SA 21:18\ref*.\f* \rb a descendant|מִילִדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Rephaim|הָרְפָאִ֖ים\rb*,\f + \fr 20:4 \ft Or \fqa the giants\ft ; see also \fqa descendants of Rapha \ft in verses 6 and 8.\f* \rb and the Philistines were subdued|וַיִּכָּנֵֽעוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Once again|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb there was|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb a battle|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb and Elhanan|אֶלְחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jair|יָעוּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּ֞ךְ\rb* \rb Lahmi|לַחְמִי֙\rb* \rb the brother|אֲחִי֙\rb*\f + \fr 20:5 \ft Or \fqa Elhanan son of Jair the Bethlehemite killed the brother\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 21:19|2SA 21:19\ref*.\f* \rb of Goliath|גָּלְיָ֣ת\rb* \rb the Gittite|הַגִּתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb the shaft|וְעֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of whose spear|חֲנִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb was like a weaver’s|אֹרְגִֽים׃\rb* \rb beam|כִּמְנ֖וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb And there was|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb also|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb a battle|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Gath|בְּגַ֑ת\rb*, \rb where there was|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of great stature|מִדָּ֗ה\rb* \rb with six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb fingers on each hand|וְאֶצְבְּעֹתָ֤יו\rb* \rb and six toes on each foot|וָשֵׁשׁ֙\rb*— \rb twenty-four in all|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֔ע\rb*. \rb He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb too|וְגַם־\rb* \rb was descended|נוֹלַ֥ד\rb* \rb from Rapha|לְהָרָפָֽא׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb and when he taunted|וַיְחָרֵ֖ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִֽיד׃\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֥י\rb* \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעָ֖א\rb* \rb killed him|וַיַּכֵּ֙הוּ֙\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb So these|אֵ֛ל\rb* \rb descendants|נוּלְּד֥וּ\rb* \rb of Rapha|לְהָרָפָ֖א\rb* \rb in Gath|בְּגַ֑ת\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb at the hands|בְיַד־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb*\rb |וּבְיַד־\rb* \rb and his servants|עֲבָדָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 21
\s1 David’s Military Census
\r (\ref Exodus 30:11–16|EXO 30:11-16\ref*; \ref 2 Samuel 24:1–9|2SA 24:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Satan|שָׂטָ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 21:1 \ft That is, \fqa the Accuser \ft or \fqa the Adversary\f* \rb rose up|וַיַּֽעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and incited|וַיָּ֙סֶת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb to take a census|לִמְנ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Go|לְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb and count|סִפְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb from|מִבְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Dan|דָּ֑ן\rb* \rb and bring me a report|וְהָבִ֣יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb*, \rb so that I may know|וְאֵדְעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their number|מִסְפָּרָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb multiply|יוֹסֵף֩\rb* \rb His troops|עַמּ֤וֹ׀\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb times|פְעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb over|כָּהֵם֙\rb*. \rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb are they not|הֲלֹא֙\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּ֥ם\rb* \rb servants|לַעֲבָדִ֑ים\rb* \rb of my lord|לַאדֹנִ֖י\rb*? \rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb does my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb want|יְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to do this|זֹאת֙\rb*? \rb Why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb should he bring|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb guilt|לְאַשְׁמָ֖ה\rb* \rb on Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb Nevertheless , the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb word|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb prevailed|חָזַ֣ק\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֑ב\rb*. \rb So Joab|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb and traveled|וַיִּתְהַלֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and then he returned|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And Joab|יוֹאָ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reported|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb the total|מִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb number|מִפְקַד־\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb*. \rb In all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb there were|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb 1,100,000|אֶ֣לֶף\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֩\rb*\rb |וּמֵאָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶ֤לֶף\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who drew|שֹׁ֣לֵֽף\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*, \rb including 470,000|אַרְבַּע֩\rb*\rb |מֵא֨וֹת\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |שֹׁ֥לֵֽף\rb*\rb |חָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb in Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֕ה\rb*. \v 6 \rb But Joab did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb include|פָקַ֖ד\rb* \rb Levi|וְלֵוִי֙\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb in the count|בְּתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb command|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb was detestable|נִתְעַ֥ב\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb him|יוֹאָֽב׃\rb*.
\s1 Judgment for David’s Sin
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 24:10–14|2SA 24:10-14\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb This|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb command|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb was also evil|וַיֵּ֙רַע֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*; \rb so He struck|וַיַּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Then David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, “\rb I have sinned|חָטָ֣אתִֽי\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb thing|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*. \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb I beg You|נָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to take away|הַֽעֲבֶר־\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲו֣וֹן\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have acted very|מְאֹֽד׃פ\rb* \rb foolishly|נִסְכַּ֖לְתִּי\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb instructed|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb Gad|גָּ֔ד\rb*, \rb David’s|דָוִ֖יד\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb seer|חֹזֵ֥ה\rb*, \v 10 “\rb Go|לֵךְ֩\rb* \rb and tell|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֨\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am offering|נֹטֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb you three options|שָׁל֕וֹשׁ\rb*. \rb Choose|בְּחַר־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֵ֖נָּה\rb*, \rb and I will carry it out|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb against you|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 11 \rb So Gad|גָ֖ד\rb* \rb went|וַיָּ֥בֹא\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb*: ‘\rb You must choose|קַבֶּל־\rb*\rb |לָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 12 \rb between|אִם־\rb* \rb three|שָׁל֨וֹשׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb of famine|רָעָ֗ב\rb*,\rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֨ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb of being swept away|נִסְפֶּ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 21:12 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate \fqa of fleeing\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 24:13|2SA 24:13\ref*.\f* \rb before|מִפְּנֵי־\rb* \rb your enemies|צָרֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb and overtaken|לְמַשֶּׂגֶת֒\rb* \rb by their swords|וְחֶ֣רֶב\rb*\rb |אוֹיְבֶ֣ךָ׀\rb*, \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָ֠מִים\rb* \rb of the sword|חֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*— \rb days of plague|וְדֶ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb upon the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb with the angel|וּמַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb ravaging|מַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb* \rb every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb part|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.’ \rb Now then|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb decide|רְאֵ֔ה\rb* \rb how|מָֽה־\rb* \rb I should reply|אָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃פ\rb* \rb to Him who sent me|שֹׁלְחִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb Gad|גָּ֖ד\rb*, “\rb I am deeply distressed|צַר־\rb*\rb |לִ֣י\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*. \rb Please|נָּ֣א\rb*, \rb let me fall|אֶפְּלָה־\rb* \rb into the hand|בְיַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb His mercies are|רַחֲמָיו֙\rb* \rb very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb great|רַבִּ֤ים\rb*; \rb but do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let me fall|אֶפֹּֽל׃\rb* \rb into the hands|וּבְיַד־\rb* \rb of men|אָדָ֖ם\rb*.”
\s1 A Plague on Israel
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 24:15–17|2SA 24:15-17\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb a plague|דֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb upon Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb of Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb fell dead|וַיִּפֹּל֙\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then God|הָאֱלֹהִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb an angel|מַלְאָ֥ךְ׀\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁחִיתָהּ֒\rb* \rb Jerusalem|לִֽירוּשָׁלִַם֮\rb*, \rb but as the angel was doing so|וּכְהַשְׁחִ֗ית\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb saw it|רָאָ֤ה\rb* \rb and relented|וַיִּנָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb the calamity|הָֽרָעָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and He said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to the angel|לַמַּלְאָ֤ךְ\rb* \rb who was destroying the people|הַמַּשְׁחִית֙\rb*, “\rb Enough|רַ֔ב\rb*! \rb Withdraw|הֶ֣רֶף\rb* \rb your hand|יָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb*!”
\p \rb At that time the angel|וּמַלְאַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was standing|עֹמֵ֔ד\rb* \rb by|עִם־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|גֹּ֖רֶן\rb* \rb of Ornan|אָרְנָ֥ן\rb*\f + \fr 21:15 \fqa Ornan \ft is a variant of \fqa Araunah\ft ; also in verses 18–28; see \ref 2 Samuel 24:16|2SA 24:16\ref*.\f* \rb the Jebusite|הַיְבוּסִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb When David|דָוִ֜יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lifted up|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֞רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֗ד\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*, \rb with a drawn|שְׁלוּפָה֙\rb* \rb sword|וְחַרְבּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb stretched out|נְטוּיָ֖ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֧יד\rb* \rb and the elders|וְהַזְּקֵנִ֛ים\rb*, \rb clothed|מְכֻסִּ֥ים\rb* \rb in sackcloth|בַּשַּׂקִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֨ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb facedown|פְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֡ים\rb*, “\rb Was it not|הֲלֹא֩\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb who gave the order|אָמַ֜רְתִּי\rb* \rb to count|לִמְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the people|בָּעָ֗ם\rb*? \rb I|וַאֲנִי־\rb*\f + \fr 21:17 \ft Or \fqa I, the shepherd,\ft see \ref 2 Samuel 24:17|2SA 24:17\ref* DSS and LXX.\f* \rb am the one|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has sinned|חָטָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb and acted wickedly|וְהָרֵ֣עַ\rb*\rb |הֲרֵע֔וֹתִי\rb*. \rb But these|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb sheep|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*, \rb what|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have they done|עָשׂ֑וּ\rb*? \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֗י\rb*, \rb please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb let Your hand|יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb fall upon|תְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb me|בִּ֚י\rb* \rb and my father’s|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb house|וּבְבֵ֣ית\rb*, \rb but do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb let this plague|לְמַגֵּפָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb remain upon Your people|וּֽבְעַמְּךָ֖\rb*.”
\s1 David Builds an Altar
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 24:18–25|2SA 24:18-25\ref*)
\p \v 18 \rb Then the angel|וּמַלְאַ֧ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb ordered|אָמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Gad|גָּ֖ד\rb* \rb to tell|לֵאמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֑יד\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb to go up|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |דָוִ֗יד\rb* \rb and build|לְהָקִ֤ים\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the threshing floor|בְּגֹ֖רֶן\rb* \rb of Ornan|אָרְנָ֥ן\rb* \rb the Jebusite|הַיְבֻסִֽי׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb So David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb at the word|בִּדְבַר־\rb* \rb that Gad|גָּ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now Ornan|אָרְנָ֗ן\rb* \rb was threshing|דָּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb wheat|חִטִּֽים׃\rb* \rb when he|וְאָרְנָ֖ן\rb* \rb turned|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֔ךְ\rb*; \rb and his four|וְאַרְבַּ֧עַת\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb* \rb who were with him|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb hid themselves|מִֽתְחַבְּאִ֑ים\rb*. \v 21 \rb David|דָוִ֖יד\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Ornan|אָרְנָ֑ן\rb*, \rb and when Ornan|אָרְנָן֙\rb* \rb looked out|וַיַּבֵּ֤ט\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb*, \rb he left|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|הַגֹּ֔רֶן\rb* \rb and bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֧חוּ\rb* \rb facedown|אַפַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |אָֽרְצָה׃\rb* \rb before David|לְדָוִ֛יד\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ornan|אָרְנָ֗ן\rb*, “\rb Grant|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּי֙\rb* \rb the site|מְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb of this threshing floor|הַגֹּ֔רֶן\rb*, \rb that I may build|וְאֶבְנֶה־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Sell it|תְּנֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb for the full|מָלֵא֙\rb* \rb price|בְּכֶ֤סֶף\rb*, \rb so that the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb upon|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb may be halted|וְתֵעָצַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb Ornan|אָרְנָ֤ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*, “\rb Take|קַֽח־\rb* \rb it|לָ֔ךְ\rb*! \rb May my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb do|וְיַ֛עַשׂ\rb* \rb whatever seems good|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb to him|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb*. \rb Look|רְאֵה֩\rb*, \rb I will give|נָתַ֨תִּי\rb* \rb the oxen|הַבָּקָ֜ר\rb* \rb for the burnt offerings|לָֽעֹל֗וֹת\rb*, \rb the threshing sledges|וְהַמּוֹרִגִּ֧ים\rb* \rb for the wood|לָעֵצִ֛ים\rb*, \rb and the wheat|וְהַחִטִּ֥ים\rb* \rb for the grain offering|לַמִּנְחָ֖ה\rb*— \rb I will give|נָתָֽתִּי׃\rb* \rb it all|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb*.”
\p \v 24 “\rb No|לֹ֕א\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |לְאָרְנָ֔ן\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*, “\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I insist on paying|קָנֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶקְנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the full|מָלֵ֑א\rb* \rb price|בְּכֶ֣סֶף\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb I will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb take|אֶשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb belongs to you|לְךָ֙\rb*, \rb nor will I offer|וְהַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb that cost me nothing|חִנָּֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb So David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb paid|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb Ornan|לְאָרְנָ֖ן\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb shekels|שִׁקְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*\f + \fr 21:25 \fqa 600 shekels \ft is approximately 15.1 pounds or 6.8 kilograms of gold.\f*\rb |מִשְׁקָ֖ל\rb* \rb for the site|בַּמָּק֑וֹם\rb*. \v 26 \rb And|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֨ם\rb* \rb he built|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and offered|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וּשְׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*. \rb He called|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb who answered him|וַיַּֽעֲנֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb with fire|בָאֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb spoke|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to the angel|לַמַּלְאָ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb who put his sword|חַרְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb back|וַיָּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb its sheath|נְדָנָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb At that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb when David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb saw|בִּרְא֤וֹת\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had answered him|עָנָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb at the threshing floor|בְּגֹ֖רֶן\rb* \rb of Ornan|אָרְנָ֣ן\rb* \rb the Jebusite|הַיְבוּסִ֑י\rb*, \rb he offered sacrifices|וַיִּזְבַּ֖ח\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb For the tabernacle|וּמִשְׁכַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַמִּדְבָּ֛ר\rb* \rb and the altar|וּמִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb were presently|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb at the high place|בַּבָּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Gibeon|בְּגִבְעֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb but David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb could|יָכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb go|לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb before it|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְרֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he was afraid|נִבְעַ֔ת\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֕י\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb of the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\c 22
\s1 Preparations for the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Here|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb shall be|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb as well as|וְזֶה־\rb* \rb the altar|מִּזְבֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb of burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb for Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb So David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb gave orders|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to gather|לִכְנוֹס֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreigners|הַגֵּרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb from whom he appointed|וַיַּעֲמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb stonecutters|חֹֽצְבִ֗ים\rb* \rb to prepare|לַחְצוֹב֙\rb* \rb finished|גָזִ֔ית\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb for building|לִבְנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb David|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb provided|הֵכִ֣ין\rb* \rb a large quantity of|לָ֠רֹב\rb* \rb iron|וּבַרְזֶ֣ל׀\rb* \rb to make the nails|לַֽמִּסְמְרִ֞ים\rb* \rb for the doors|לְדַלְת֧וֹת\rb* \rb of the gateways|הַשְּׁעָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb and for the fittings|וְלַֽמְחַבְּר֖וֹת\rb*, \rb together with more|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb bronze|וּנְחֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb than could be weighed|מִשְׁקָֽל׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and more|מִסְפָּ֑ר\rb* \rb cedar|אֲרָזִ֖ים\rb* \rb logs|וַעֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb than could be counted|לְאֵ֣ין\rb*; \rb for|כִּֽי\rb* \rb the Sidonians|הַצִּֽידֹנִ֨ים\rb* \rb and Tyrians|וְהַצֹּרִ֜ים\rb* \rb had brought|הֵ֠בִיאוּ\rb* \rb a large quantity of|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb cedar|אֲרָזִ֛ים\rb* \rb logs|עֲצֵ֧י\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִֽיד׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb And David|דָּוִ֗יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb My son|בְנִי֮\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb is young|נַ֣עַר\rb* \rb and inexperienced|וָרָךְ֒\rb*, \rb and the house|וְהַבַּ֜יִת\rb* \rb to be built|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb must be exceedingly|לְמַ֜עְלָה\rb* \rb magnificent|לְהַגְדִּ֨יל׀\rb* — \rb famous|לְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb and glorious|וּלְתִפְאֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb throughout all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb lands|הָ֣אֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb*. \rb Therefore|נָּ֖א\rb* \rb I must make preparations|אָכִ֥ינָה\rb* \rb for it|ל֑וֹ\rb*.” \rb So David|דָּוִ֛יד\rb* \rb made lavish|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb preparations|וַיָּ֧כֶן\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb his death|מוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Solomon Anointed to Build the Temple
\p \v 6 \rb Then David called for|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb and instructed him|וַיְצַוֵּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 7 “\rb My son|בְּנוֹ\rb*,”\rb |אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, “\rb it was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb my heart|לְבָבִ֔י\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb but this word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb to me|עָלַ֤י\rb*: ‘\rb You have shed|שָׁפַ֔כְתָּ\rb* \rb much|לָרֹב֙\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֤ם\rb* \rb and waged|עָשִׂ֑יתָ\rb* \rb great|גְּדֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb wars|וּמִלְחָמ֥וֹת\rb*. \rb You are not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to build|תִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a house|בַ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֔י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb you have shed|שָׁפַ֥כְתָּ\rb* \rb so much|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb blood|דָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנָֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb But|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a son|בֵ֞ן\rb* \rb will be born|נוֹלָ֣ד\rb* \rb to you|לָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb who|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of rest|מְנוּחָ֔ה\rb*. \rb I will give him rest|וַהֲנִח֥וֹתִי\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb his enemies|אוֹיְבָ֖יו\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb his name|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb*,\f + \fr 22:9 \fqa Solomon \ft sounds like and is probably derived from the Hebrew word for \fqa peace\ft .\f* \rb and I will grant|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb peace|וְשָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb and quiet|וָשֶׁ֛קֶט\rb* \rb during his reign|בְּיָמָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb is the one who will build|יִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a house|בַ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֔י\rb*. \rb He|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb My|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb son|לְבֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb and I will be|וַאֲנִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb Father|לְאָ֑ב\rb*. \rb And I will establish|וַהֲכִ֨ינוֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֧א\rb* \rb of his kingdom|מַלְכוּת֛וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 11 \rb Now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb my son|בְנִ֔י\rb*, \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and may you succeed|וְהִצְלַחְתָּ֗\rb* \rb in building|וּבָנִ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֚ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb you would|עָלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Above all|אַ֣ךְ\rb*, \rb may the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb give|יִֽתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לְּךָ֤\rb* \rb insight|שֵׂ֣כֶל\rb* \rb and understanding|וּבִינָ֔ה\rb* \rb when He puts you in command|וִֽיצַוְּךָ֖\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb so that you may keep|וְלִשְׁמ֕וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb you will succeed|תַּצְלִ֔יחַ\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you carefully|תִּשְׁמ֗וֹר\rb* \rb follow|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the statutes|הַֽחֻקִּ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Be strong|חֲזַ֣ק\rb* \rb and courageous|וֶאֱמָ֔ץ\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֖א\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged|תֵּחָֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Now behold|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I have taken great pains|בְעָנְיִ֜י\rb* \rb to provide|הֲכִינ֣וֹתִי\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*— \rb 100,000|מֵֽאָה־\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּרִ֤ים\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֞ב\rb*,\f + \fr 22:14 \fqa 100,000 talents \ft is approximately 3,770 tons or 3,420 metric tons of gold.\f* \rb 1,000,000|אֶ֤לֶף\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb of silver|וְכֶ֗סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 22:14 \fqa 1,000,000 talents \ft is approximately 37,700 tons or 34,200 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb and bronze|וְלַנְּחֹ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb and iron|וְלַבַּרְזֶל֙\rb* \rb too great|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |הָיָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לָרֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb to be weighed|מִשְׁקָ֔ל\rb*. \rb I have also provided|הֲכִינ֔וֹתִי\rb* \rb timber|וְעֵצִ֤ים\rb* \rb and stone|וַאֲבָנִים֙\rb*, \rb and you may add|תּוֹסִֽיף׃\rb* \rb to them|וַעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb You also have|וְעִמְּךָ֤\rb* \rb many|לָרֹב֙\rb* \rb workers|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb*\rb |מְלָאכָ֔ה\rb*: \rb stonecutters|חֹצְבִ֕ים\rb*, \rb masons|וְחָרָשֵׁ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶ֖בֶן\rb*, \rb carpenters|וָעֵ֑ץ\rb*, \rb and men skilled|חָכָ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb* \rb in every kind|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of work|מְלָאכָֽה׃\rb* — \v 16 \rb in gold|לַזָּהָ֥ב\rb* \rb and silver|לַכֶּ֛סֶף\rb*, \rb bronze|וְלַנְּחֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb and iron|וְלַבַּרְזֶ֖ל\rb*— \rb craftsmen beyond|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb number|מִסְפָּ֑ר\rb*. \rb Now begin|ק֣וּם\rb* \rb the work|וַעֲשֵׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb and may the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb be|וִיהִ֥י\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Then David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb ordered|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the leaders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to help|לַעְזֹ֖ר\rb* \rb his son|בְנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb*: \v 18 “\rb Is not|הֲלֹ֨א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and has He not granted you rest|וְהֵנִ֥יחַ\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb He has given|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb into my hand|בְּיָדִ֗י\rb*,\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb and the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb has been subdued|וְנִכְבְּשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and His people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb set|תְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb your heart|לְבַבְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and soul|וְנַפְשְׁכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Begin|וְק֗וּמוּ\rb* \rb building|וּבְנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|מִקְדַּשׁ֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb so that you may bring|לְהָבִ֞יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and the holy|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb articles|וּכְלֵי֙\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb into the temple|לַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb that will be built|הַנִּבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 23
\s1 The Divisions of the Levites
\p \v 1 \rb When David|וְדָוִ֥יד\rb* \rb was old|זָקֵ֖ן\rb* \rb and full of|וְשָׂבַ֣ע\rb* \rb years|יָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb he installed his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb* \rb as king|וַיַּמְלֵ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Then he gathered|וַיֶּאֱסֹף֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the leaders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb as well as the priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb or older|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb were counted|וַיִּסָּֽפְרוּ֙\rb*, \rb and the total number|מִסְפָּרָ֤ם\rb* \rb of men|לִגְבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb 38,000|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃\rb*\rb |לְגֻלְגְּלֹתָם֙\rb*. \v 4 “\rb Of these,” said David,|מֵאֵ֗לֶּה\rb*\f + \fr 23:4 \ft Hebrew does not include \fqa said David,\f* \rb “24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb are to oversee|לְנַצֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb 6,000|שֵׁ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb* \rb are to be officers|וְשֹׁטְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and judges|וְשֹׁפְטִ֖ים\rb*, \v 5 \rb 4,000|וְאַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb are to be gatekeepers|שֹׁעֲרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and 4,000|וְאַרְבַּ֤עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb are to praise|מְהַֽלְלִ֣ים\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with the instruments|בַּכֵּלִ֕ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have made|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb for giving praise|לְהַלֵּֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb divided the Levites|וַיֶּֽחָלְקֵ֥ם\rb* \rb into divisions|מַחְלְק֑וֹתס\rb* \rb according to the sons|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִ֔י\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Gershon|לְגֵרְשׁ֖וֹן\rb*, \rb Kohath|קְהָ֥ת\rb*, \rb and Merari|וּמְרָרִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Gershonites
\r (\ref Numbers 3:21–26|NUM 3:21-26\ref*; \ref Numbers 4:21–28|NUM 4:21-28\ref*)
\li1 \v 7 \rb The Gershonites|לַגֵּרְשֻׁנִּ֖י\rb*: \rb Ladan|לַעְדָּ֥ן\rb*\f + \fr 23:7 \fqa Ladan \ft is a variant of \fqa Libni\ft ; also in verses 8 and 9; see \ref 1 Chronicles 6:17|1CH 6:17\ref*.\f* \rb and Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 8 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Ladan|לַעְדָּ֗ן\rb*: \rb Jehiel|יְחִיאֵ֛ל\rb*\f + \fr 23:8 \fqa Jehiel \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehieli\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 26:21|1CH 26:21\ref*.\f* \rb the first|הָרֹ֧אשׁ\rb*, \rb Zetham|וְזֵתָ֥ם\rb*, \rb and Joel|וְיוֹאֵ֖ל\rb*— \rb three in all|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 9 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֗י\rb*: \rb Shelomoth|שְׁלֹמוֹת\rb*, \rb Haziel|וַחֲזִיאֵ֛ל\rb*, \rb and Haran|וְהָרָ֖ן\rb*— \rb three in all|שְׁלֹשָׁ֑ה\rb*. \rb These were|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the families|הָאָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Ladan|לְלַעְדָּֽן׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 10 \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֔י\rb*:\f + \fr 23:10 \fqa Shimei \ft was possibly a son or grandson of the \fqa Shimei \ft listed in verse 9.\f* \rb Jahath|יַ֣חַת\rb*, \rb Zina|זִינָ֔א\rb*,\f + \fr 23:10 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; one Hebrew manuscript, LXX, and Vulgate (see also verse 11) \fqa Zizah\f* \rb Jeush|וִיע֖וּשׁ\rb*, \rb and Beriah|וּבְרִיעָ֑ה\rb*. \rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb were the sons|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֖י\rb*— \rb four in all|אַרְבָּעָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Jahath|יַ֣חַת\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb the first|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb and Zizah|וְזִיזָ֖ה\rb* \rb was the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb*; \rb but Jeush|וִיע֤וּשׁ\rb* \rb and Beriah|וּבְרִיעָה֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb have many|הִרְבּ֣וּ\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb so they were counted as|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb one family|אָ֔ב\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb and received a single|אֶחָֽת׃ס\rb* \rb assignment|לִפְקֻדָּ֖ה\rb*.
\s1 The Kohathites
\r (\ref Numbers 3:27–32|NUM 3:27-32\ref*; \ref Numbers 4:1–20|NUM 4:1-20\ref*)
\li1 \v 12 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Kohath|קְהָ֗ת\rb*: \rb Amram|עַמְרָ֥ם\rb*, \rb Izhar|יִצְהָ֛ר\rb*, \rb Hebron|חֶבְר֥וֹן\rb*, \rb and Uzziel|וְעֻזִּיאֵ֖ל\rb*— \rb four in all|אַרְבָּעָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 13 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Amram|עַמְרָ֖ם\rb*: \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*. \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֡ן\rb* \rb and his descendants|וּבָנָיו֙\rb* \rb were set apart|וַיִּבָּדֵ֣ל\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb to consecrate|לְֽהַקְדִּישׁוֹ֩\rb* \rb the most holy things|קֹ֨דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |קָֽדָשִׁ֤ים\rb*,\rb |הֽוּא־\rb* \rb to burn incense|לְהַקְטִיר֩\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*, \rb to minister before Him|לְשָׁרְת֛וֹ\rb*, \rb and to pronounce blessings|וּלְבָרֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in His name|בִּשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb As for Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֕יו\rb* \rb were named|יִקָּרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb among|עַל־\rb* \rb the tribe|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of Levi|הַלֵּוִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 15 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*: \rb Gershom|גֵּרְשֹׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and Eliezer|וֶאֱלִיעֶֽזֶר׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 16 \rb The descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Gershom|גֵרְשׁ֖וֹם\rb*: \rb Shebuel|שְׁבוּאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb was the first|הָרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 17 \rb The descendants|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Eliezer|אֱלִיעֶ֖זֶר\rb*: \rb Rehabiah|רְחַבְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb was|וַיִּֽהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb the first|הָרֹ֑אשׁ\rb*. \rb Eliezer|לֶאֱלִיעֶ֙זֶר֙\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb have|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb any other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb but the sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Rehabiah|רְחַבְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb were very|לְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb numerous|רָב֥וּ\rb*.
\li1 \v 18 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Izhar|יִצְהָ֖ר\rb*: \rb Shelomith|שְׁלֹמִ֥ית\rb* \rb was the first|הָרֹֽאשׁ׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 19 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Hebron|חֶבְר֑וֹן\rb*: \rb Jeriah|יְרִיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb was the first|הָרֹאשׁ֙\rb*, \rb Amariah|אֲמַרְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*, \rb Jahaziel|יַחֲזִיאֵל֙\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb and Jekameam|וִֽיקַמְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb the fourth|הָרְבִיעִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 20 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Uzziel|עֻזִּיאֵ֑ל\rb*: \rb Micah|מִיכָ֣ה\rb* \rb was the first|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb and Isshiah|וְיִשִּׁיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Merarites
\r (\ref Numbers 3:33–37|NUM 3:33-37\ref*; \ref Numbers 4:29–33|NUM 4:29-33\ref*)
\li1 \v 21 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִי֙\rb*: \rb Mahli|מַחְלִ֣י\rb* \rb and Mushi|וּמוּשִׁ֔י\rb*.
\li1 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Mahli|מַחְלִ֖י\rb*: \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֥ר\rb* \rb and Kish|וְקִֽישׁ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֔ר\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֙מָת֙\rb* \rb without|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb having any|הָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb*; \rb he had only|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Their cousins|אֲחֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Kish|קִ֖ישׁ\rb*, \rb married them|וַיִּשָּׂא֥וּם\rb*.
\li1 \v 23 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Mushi|מוּשִׁ֗י\rb*: \rb Mahli|מַחְלִ֥י\rb*, \rb Eder|וְעֵ֛דֶר\rb*, \rb and Jeremoth|וִירֵמ֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 23:23 \fqa Jeremoth \ft is a variant of \fqa Jerimoth\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 24:30|1CH 24:30\ref*.\f*— \rb three in all|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb*.
\s1 Levite Duties Revised
\p \v 24 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were the descendants|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִי֩\rb* \rb by their families|אֲבֹתֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֨ית\rb*— \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֧י\rb* \rb of families|הָאָב֣וֹת\rb*, \rb registered|לִפְקוּדֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |בְּמִסְפַּ֤ר\rb* \rb individually|לְגֻלְגְּלֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb by name|שֵׁמוֹת֙\rb*— \rb those twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb or older|וָמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb who worked|עֹשֵׂה֙\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the service|לַעֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb has given rest|הֵנִ֛יחַ\rb* \rb to His people|לְעַמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and has come to dwell|וַיִּשְׁכֹּ֥ן\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb So now|וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb no|אֵין־\rb* \rb longer need to carry|לָשֵׂ֧את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the articles|כֵּלָ֖יו\rb* \rb for its service|לַעֲבֹדָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb according to the final|הָאַ֣חֲרֹנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb instructions|בְדִבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִיד֙\rb*, \rb the Levites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |לֵוִ֑י\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb or older|וּלְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb were counted|מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb*, \v 28 \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb their duty|מַעֲמָדָ֞ם\rb* \rb was to assist|לְיַד־\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb with the service|לַעֲבֹדַת֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb being responsible for|עַל־\rb* \rb the courts|הַחֲצֵרוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֔וֹת\rb*,\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb the purification|טָהֳרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the holy things|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and the work|וּמַֽעֲשֵׂ֔ה\rb* \rb of the service|עֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*, \v 29 \rb as well as for the rows|הַֽמַּעֲרֶ֜כֶת\rb* \rb of the showbread|וּלְלֶ֨חֶם\rb*, \rb the fine flour|וּלְסֹ֤לֶת\rb* \rb for the grain offering|לְמִנְחָה֙\rb*, \rb the wafers|וְלִרְקִיקֵ֣י\rb* \rb of unleavened bread|הַמַּצּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb the baking|וְלַֽמַּחֲבַ֖ת\rb*, \rb the mixing|וְלַמֻּרְבָּ֑כֶת\rb*, \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb measurements of quantity|מְשׂוּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and size|וּמִדָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb They were also to stand|וְלַעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb every morning|בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb to give thanks|לְהֹד֥וֹת\rb* \rb and praise|וּלְהַלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and likewise|וְכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in the evening|לָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb Whenever|וּלְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb were presented|הַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the Sabbaths|לַשַּׁבָּת֔וֹת\rb*, \rb New Moons|לֶחֳדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*, \rb and appointed feasts|וְלַמֹּעֲדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb they were to serve regularly|תָּמִ֖יד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb in the numbers|בְּמִסְפָּ֨ר\rb* \rb prescribed|כְּמִשְׁפָּ֧ט\rb* \rb for them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*. \v 32 \rb So the Levites were to carry out|וְשָׁמְר֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the responsibilities|מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb for the Tent|אֹֽהֶל־\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֗ד\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb the Holy Place|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and, under|וּמִשְׁמֶ֕רֶת\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*, \rb the service|לַעֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 24
\s1 Twenty-Four Divisions of Priests
\p \v 1 \rb These were the divisions|מַחְלְקוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the descendants|וְלִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*. \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb were Nadab|נָדָב֙\rb*, \rb Abihu|וַאֲבִיה֔וּא\rb*, \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb*, \rb and Ithamar|וְאִיתָמָֽר׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb But Nadab|נָדָ֤ב\rb* \rb and Abihu|וַאֲבִיהוּא֙\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֨מָת\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their father did|אֲבִיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and they had|הָי֣וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb sons|וּבָנִ֖ים\rb*; \rb so Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb* \rb and Ithamar|וְאִיתָמָֽר׃\rb* \rb served as priests|וַֽיְכַהֲנ֔וּ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb With the help of Eleazar’s|אֶלְעָזָ֔ר\rb* \rb descendant|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Zadok|וְצָדוֹק֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb and Ithamar’s|אִיתָמָ֑ר\rb* \rb descendant|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Ahimelech|וַאֲחִימֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb divided them|וַיֶּֽחָלְקֵ֣ם\rb* \rb according to the offices|לִפְקֻדָּתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of their service|בַּעֲבֹדָתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Since more|רַבִּ֞ים\rb* \rb leaders|לְרָאשֵׁ֧י\rb*\rb |הַגְּבָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb were found|וַיִּמָּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb among Eleazar’s|אֶלְעָזָ֡ר\rb* \rb descendants|בְֽנֵי־\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb those|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Ithamar|אִיתָמָ֖ר\rb*, \rb they were divided accordingly|וַֽיַּחְלְק֑וּם\rb*. \rb There were sixteen|שִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb heads|רָאשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb of families|אָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb from the descendants|לִבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֜ר\rb* \rb and eight|שְׁמוֹנָֽה׃\rb*\rb |אֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb from the descendants|וְלִבְנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Ithamar|אִיתָמָ֛ר\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Thus they were divided|וַיַּחְלְק֥וּם\rb* \rb by lot|בְּגוֹרָל֖וֹת\rb*,\rb |אֵ֣לֶּה\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb*\rb |אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb there were|הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb officers|שָֽׂרֵי־\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|קֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb and officers|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb among both Eleazar’s|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb*\rb |וּבִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and Ithamar’s|אִיתָמָֽר׃ס\rb* \rb descendants|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb The scribe|הַסּוֹפֵ֜ר\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְֽׁמַֽעְיָה֩\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Nethanel|נְתַנְאֵ֨ל\rb*, \rb a Levite|הַלֵּוִ֗י\rb*, \rb recorded their names|וַֽיִּכְתְּבֵ֡ם\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and of the officers|וְהַשָּׂרִים֙\rb*: \rb Zadok|וְצָד֣וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb Ahimelech|וַאֲחִימֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and the heads|וְרָאשֵׁי֙\rb* \rb of families|הָֽאָב֔וֹת\rb* \rb of the priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and the Levites|וְלַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* — \rb one|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb family|אָ֣ב\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb being taken|אָחֻז֙\rb* \rb from Eleazar|לְאֶלְעָזָ֔ר\rb*,\rb |וְאָחֻ֥ז׀\rb* \rb and then one|אָחֻ֖ז\rb* \rb from Ithamar|לְאִיתָמָֽר׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 7 \rb The first|הָרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֤ל\rb* \rb fell|וַיֵּצֵ֞א\rb* \rb to Jehoiarib|לִיה֣וֹיָרִ֔יב\rb*,
\li1 \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִֽי׃\rb* \rb to Jedaiah|לִֽידַעְיָ֖ה\rb*,
\li1 \v 8 \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb to Harim|לְחָרִם֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the fourth|הָרְבִעִֽי׃\rb* \rb to Seorim|לִשְׂעֹרִ֖ים\rb*,
\li1 \v 9 \rb the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb to Malchijah|לְמַלְכִּיָּה֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּֽׁי׃\rb* \rb to Mijamin|לְמִיָּמִ֖ן\rb*,
\li1 \v 10 \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִ֔י\rb* \rb to Hakkoz|לְהַקּוֹץ֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִֽי׃\rb* \rb to Abijah|לַאֲבִיָּ֖ה\rb*,
\li1 \v 11 \rb the ninth|הַתְּשִׁעִ֔י\rb* \rb to Jeshua|לְיֵשׁ֙וּעַ֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the tenth|הָעֲשִׂרִֽי׃\rb* \rb to Shecaniah|לִשְׁכַנְיָ֖הוּ\rb*,
\li1 \v 12 \rb the eleventh|עַשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb to Eliashib|לְאֶלְיָשִׁיב֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the twelfth|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb to Jakim|לְיָקִ֖ים\rb*,
\li1 \v 13 \rb the thirteenth|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb to Huppah|לְחֻפָּה֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the fourteenth|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb to Jeshebeab|לְיֶֽשֶׁבְאָ֖ב\rb*,
\li1 \v 14 \rb the fifteenth|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb to Bilgah|לְבִלְגָּה֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the sixteenth|שִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb to Immer|לְאִמֵּ֖ר\rb*,
\li1 \v 15 \rb the seventeenth|שִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb to Hezir|לְחֵזִיר֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the eighteenth|שְׁמוֹנָ֥ה\rb* \rb to Happizzez|עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*\rb |לְהַפִּצֵּ֖ץ\rb*,
\li1 \v 16 \rb the nineteenth|תִּשְׁעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb to Pethahiah|לִֽפְתַחְיָה֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the twentieth|הָעֶשְׂרִֽים׃\rb* \rb to Jehezkel|לִֽיחֶזְקֵ֖אל\rb*,
\li1 \v 17 \rb the twenty-first|אֶחָ֣ד\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to Jachin|לְיָכִין֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb the twenty-second|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִֽים׃\rb* \rb to Gamul|לְגָמ֖וּל\rb*,
\li1 \v 18 \rb the twenty-third|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to Delaiah|לִדְלָיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*,
\li1 \rb and the twenty-fourth|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb to Maaziah|לְמַֽעַזְיָ֖הוּ\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb This was|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb their appointed order|פְקֻדָּתָ֞ם\rb* \rb for service|לַעֲבֹדָתָ֗ם\rb* \rb when they entered|לָב֤וֹא\rb* \rb the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb according to the regulations|כְּמִשְׁפָּטָ֔ם\rb* \rb prescribed for them|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb by their forefather|אֲבִיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*, \rb had commanded him|צִוָּ֔הוּ\rb*.
\s1 The Rest of the Levites
\p \v 20 \rb Now these were the rest of the|הַנּוֹתָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb descendants|וְלִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִ֖י\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb From the sons|לִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Amram|עַמְרָם֙\rb*: \rb Shubael|שֽׁוּבָאֵ֔ל\rb*;\f + \fr 24:20 \fqa Shubael \ft (twice in this verse) is a variant of \fqa Shebuel\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 23:16|1CH 23:16\ref* and 1 Chronicles 26:24.\f*
\li1 \rb from the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Shubael|שׁוּבָאֵ֖ל\rb*: \rb Jehdeiah|יֶחְדְּיָֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 21 \rb As for Rehabiah|לִרְחַבְיָ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb from his sons|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |רְחַבְיָ֔הוּ\rb*: \rb The first|הָרֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb was Isshiah|יִשִּׁיָּֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 24:21 \fqa Isshiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jeshaiah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 26:25|1CH 26:25\ref*.\f*
\li1 \v 22 \rb From the Izharites|לַיִּצְהָרִ֣י\rb*: \rb Shelomoth|שְׁלֹמ֔וֹת\rb*;\f + \fr 24:22 \fqa Shelomoth \ft (twice in this verse) is a variant of \fqa Shelomith\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 23:18|1CH 23:18\ref*.\f*
\li1 \rb from the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Shelomoth|שְׁלֹמ֖וֹת\rb*: \rb Jahath|יָֽחַת׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 23 \rb From the sons of Hebron|וּבְנָ֖י\rb*: \rb Jeriah was the first|יְרִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*,\f + \fr 24:23 \ft Hebrew \fqa From the sons: Jeriah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 23:19|1CH 23:19\ref*.\f* \rb Amariah|אֲמַרְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*, \rb Jahaziel|יַחֲזִיאֵל֙\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb and Jekameam|יְקַמְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb the fourth|הָרְבִיעִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 24 \rb From the sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Uzziel|עֻזִּיאֵל֙\rb*: \rb Micah|מִיכָ֔ה\rb*;
\li1 \rb from the sons of|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Micah|מִיכָ֖ה\rb*: \rb Shamir|שָׁמוּר׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 25 \rb The brother|אֲחִ֤י\rb* \rb of Micah|מִיכָה֙\rb*: \rb Isshiah|יִשִּׁיָּ֔ה\rb*;
\li1 \rb from the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Isshiah|יִשִּׁיָּ֖ה\rb*: \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 26 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִי֙\rb*: \rb Mahli|מַחְלִ֣י\rb* \rb and Mushi|וּמוּשִׁ֔י\rb*.
\li1 \rb The son|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jaaziah|יַעֲזִיָּ֥הֽוּ\rb*: \rb Beno|בְנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 27 \rb The descendants|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִ֑י\rb* \rb from Jaaziah|לְיַֽעֲזִיָּ֣הֽוּ\rb*: \rb Beno|בְנ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb Shoham|וְשֹׁ֥הַם\rb*, \rb Zaccur|וְזַכּ֖וּר\rb*, \rb and Ibri|וְעִבְרִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 28 \rb From Mahli|לְמַחְלִי֙\rb*: \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֔ר\rb*, \rb who had|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִֽים׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 29 \rb From Kish|לְקִ֖ישׁ\rb*: \rb Jerahmeel|יְרַחְמְאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb the son|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Kish|קִ֥ישׁ\rb*.
\li1 \v 30 \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Mushi|מוּשִׁ֔י\rb*: \rb Mahli|מַחְלִ֥י\rb*, \rb Eder|וְעֵ֖דֶר\rb*, \rb and Jerimoth|וִירִימ֑וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 24:30 \fqa Jerimoth \ft is a variant of \fqa Jeremoth\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 23:23|1CH 23:23\ref*.\f*
\p \rb These|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb were the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb*, \rb according to their families|אֲבֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb*. \v 31 \rb As|לְעֻמַּ֣ת׀\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Aaron did|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb*, \rb they|הֵ֨ם\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb cast|וַיַּפִּילוּ֩\rb* \rb lots|גּוֹרָל֜וֹת\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֤יד\rb* \rb and of Zadok|וְצָד֣וֹק\rb*, \rb Ahimelech|וַאֲחִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb and the heads|וְרָאשֵׁי֙\rb* \rb of the families|הָֽאָב֔וֹת\rb* \rb of the priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְלַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*— \rb the family|אָב֣וֹת\rb* \rb heads|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb and their younger|הַקָּטָֽן׃ס\rb* \rb brothers|אָחִ֥יו\rb* \rb alike|לְעֻמַּ֖ת\rb*.
\c 25
\s1 Twenty-Four Divisions of Musicians
\p \v 1 \rb Additionally, David|דָּוִיד֩\rb* \rb and the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the army|הַצָּבָ֜א\rb*\rb |לַעֲבֹדָ֗ה\rb* \rb set apart|וַיַּבְדֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb some of the sons|לִבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָף֙\rb*, \rb Heman|וְהֵימָ֣ן\rb*, \rb and Jeduthun|וִֽידוּת֔וּן\rb* \rb to prophesy|הַנְּבִּיאִים\rb* \rb with the accompaniment of lyres|בְּכִנֹּר֥וֹת\rb*, \rb harps|בִּנְבָלִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and cymbals|וּבִמְצִלְתָּ֑יִם\rb*. \rb The following|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb is the list|מִסְפָּרָ֔ם\rb* \rb of the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb who performed|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb this service|לַעֲבֹדָתָֽם׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 2 \rb From the sons|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָ֗ף\rb*: \rb Zaccur|זַכּ֧וּר\rb*, \rb Joseph|וְיוֹסֵ֛ף\rb*, \rb Nethaniah|וּנְתַנְיָ֥ה\rb*, \rb and Asarelah|וַאֲשַׂרְאֵ֖לָה\rb*. \rb These sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָ֑ף\rb* \rb were under|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the direction|יַד־\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָ֔ף\rb*, \rb who prophesied|הַנִּבָּ֖א\rb* \rb under|עַל־\rb* \rb the direction|יְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 3 \rb |לִידוּת֑וּן\rb* \rb From the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jeduthun|יְדוּת֡וּן\rb*: \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Zeri|וּצְרִ֡י\rb*, \rb Jeshaiah , Shimei|וִֽ֠ישַׁעְיָהוּ\rb*,\f + \fr 25:3 \ft One Hebrew manuscript and some LXX manuscripts (see also verse 17); most Hebrew manuscripts do not include \fqa Shimei\ft .\f* \rb Hashabiah|חֲשַׁבְיָ֨הוּ\rb*, \rb and Mattithiah|וּמַתִּתְיָ֜הוּ\rb* — \rb six in all|שִׁשָּׁ֗ה\rb* — \rb under|עַל֩\rb* \rb the direction|יְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb of their father|אֲבִיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb Jeduthun|יְדוּתוּן֙\rb*, \rb who prophesied|הַנִּבָּ֕א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb with the harp|בַּכִּנּ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb giving thanks|הֹד֥וֹת\rb* \rb and praise|וְהַלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 4 \rb |לְהֵימָ֑ן\rb* \rb From the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Heman|הֵימָ֡ן\rb*: \rb Bukkiah|בֻּקִּיָּ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Mattaniah|מַתַּנְיָ֡הוּ\rb*, \rb Uzziel|עֻ֠זִּיאֵל\rb*, \rb Shebuel|שְׁבוּאֵ֨ל\rb*,\f + \fr 25:4 \fqa Shebuel \ft is a variant of \fqa Shubael\ft ; see verse 20.\f* \rb Jerimoth|וִֽירִימ֜וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 25:4 \fqa Jerimoth \ft is a variant of \fqa Jeremoth\ft ; see verse 22.\f* \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Hanani|חֲנָ֗נִי\rb*, \rb Eliathah|אֱלִיאָ֤תָה\rb*, \rb Giddalti|גִדַּ֙לְתִּי֙\rb*,\rb |וְרֹמַ֣מְתִּי\rb* \rb Romamti-ezer|עֶ֔זֶר\rb*, \rb Joshbekashah|יָשְׁבְּקָ֣שָׁה\rb*, \rb Mallothi|מַלּ֔וֹתִי\rb*, \rb Hothir|הוֹתִ֖יר\rb*, \rb and Mahazioth|מַחֲזִיאֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֜ים\rb* \rb of Heman|לְהֵימָ֗ן\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb seer|חֹזֵ֥ה\rb* \rb were given him through the promises|בְּדִבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb to exalt|לְהָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb him|קָ֑רֶן\rb*, \rb for God|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb had given|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb Heman|לְהֵימָ֗ן\rb* \rb fourteen|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֛ים\rb* \rb and three|שָׁלֽוֹשׁ׃\rb* \rb daughters|וּבָנ֥וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these were|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb under|עַל־\rb* \rb the direction|יְדֵי֩\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבִיהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb for the music|בַּשִּׁ֜יר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb with cymbals|בִּמְצִלְתַּ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb harps|נְבָלִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and lyres|וְכִנֹּר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb for the service|לַעֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*.
\p \rb Asaph|אָסָ֥ף\rb*, \rb Jeduthun|וִידוּת֖וּן\rb*, \rb and Heman|וְהֵימָֽן׃\rb* \rb were under|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the direction|יְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְס\rb*. \v 7 \rb Together with|עִם־\rb* \rb their relatives|אֲחֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb who were all|כָּל־\rb* \rb trained|מְלֻמְּדֵי־\rb* \rb and skillful|הַ֨מֵּבִ֔ין\rb* \rb in the songs|שִׁ֖יר\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb they numbered|מִסְפָּרָם֙\rb* \rb 288|מָאתַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |שְׁמוֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb They cast|וַיַּפִּ֜ילוּ\rb* \rb lots|גּוֹרָל֣וֹת\rb* \rb for their duties|מִשְׁמֶ֗רֶת\rb*,\rb |לְעֻמַּת֙\rb* \rb young|כַּקָּטֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and old alike|כַּגָּד֔וֹל\rb*, \rb teacher|מֵבִ֖ין\rb* \rb as|עִם־\rb* \rb well as pupil|תַּלְמִֽיד׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 9 \rb The first|הָרִאשׁ֛וֹן\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָ֧ל\rb*, \rb which was for Asaph|לְאָסָ֖ף\rb*, \rb fell|וַיֵּצֵ֞א\rb* \rb to Joseph, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all|לְיוֹסֵ֑ף\rb*;\f + \fr 25:9 \ft See LXX and the total in verse 7; Hebrew does not include \fqa his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;\f*
\li1 \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb to Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |הֽוּא־\rb*, \rb his sons|וּבָנָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֥יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 10 \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֣י\rb* \rb to Zaccur|זַכּ֔וּר\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 11 \rb the fourth|הָרְבִיעִי֙\rb* \rb to Izri|לַיִּצְרִ֔י\rb*,\f + \fr 25:11 \fqa Izri \ft is a variant of \fqa Zeri\ft ; see verse 3.\f* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 12 \rb the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֣י\rb* \rb to Nethaniah|נְתַנְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 13 \rb the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֣י\rb* \rb to Bukkiah|בֻקִּיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 14 \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִ֣י\rb* \rb to Jesarelah|יְשַׂרְאֵ֔לָה\rb*,\f + \fr 25:14 \fqa Jesarelah \ft is a variant of \fqa Asarelah\ft ; see verse 2.\f* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 15 \rb the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֣י\rb* \rb to Jeshaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 16 \rb the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִ֣י\rb* \rb to Mattaniah|מַתַּנְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 17 \rb the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִ֣י\rb* \rb to Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֔י\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 18 \rb the eleventh|עַשְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb to Azarel|עֲזַרְאֵ֔ל\rb*,\f + \fr 25:18 \fqa Azarel \ft is a variant of \fqa Uzziel\ft ; see verse 4.\f* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 19 \rb the twelfth|הַשְּׁנֵ֤ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Hashabiah|לַחֲשַׁבְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 20 \rb the thirteenth|לִשְׁלֹשָׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Shubael|שֽׁוּבָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 21 \rb the fourteenth|לְאַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Mattithiah|מַתִּתְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 22 \rb the fifteenth|לַחֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Jeremoth|לִֽירֵמ֔וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 25:22 \fqa Jeremoth \ft is a variant of \fqa Jerimoth\ft ; see verse 4.\f* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 23 \rb the sixteenth|לְשִׁשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Hananiah|לַחֲנַנְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 24 \rb the seventeenth|לְשִׁבְעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Joshbekashah|לְיָשְׁבְּקָ֔שָׁה\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 25 \rb the eighteenth|לִשְׁמוֹנָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Hanani|לַחֲנָ֔נִי\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 26 \rb the nineteenth|לְתִשְׁעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb to Mallothi|לְמַלּ֔וֹתִי\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 27 \rb the twentieth|לְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb* \rb to Eliathah|לֶֽאֱלִיָּ֔תָה\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 28 \rb the twenty-first|לְאֶחָ֤ד\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb* \rb to Hothir|לְהוֹתִ֔יר\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 29 \rb the twenty-second|לִשְׁנַ֤יִם\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb* \rb to Giddalti|לְגִדַּ֔לְתִּי\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 30 \rb the twenty-third|לִשְׁלֹשָׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb* \rb to Mahazioth|לְמַ֣חֲזִיא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 31 \rb and the twenty-fourth|לְאַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |לְרוֹמַ֣מְתִּי\rb* \rb to Romamti-ezer|עָ֔זֶר\rb*, \rb his sons|בָּנָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb*— \rb 12 in all|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃פ\rb*.
\c 26
\s1 The Divisions of the Gatekeepers
\p \v 1 \rb These were the divisions|לְמַחְלְק֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the gatekeepers|לְשֹׁעֲרִ֑ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb From the Korahites|לַקָּרְחִ֕ים\rb*: \rb Meshelemiah|מְשֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Kore|קֹרֵ֖א\rb*, \rb one of|מִן־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָֽף׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 2 \rb Meshelemiah|וְלִמְשֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb had sons|בָּנִ֑ים\rb*: \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb the firstborn|הַבְּכוֹר֙\rb*, \rb Jediael|יְדִֽיעֲאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*, \rb Zebadiah|זְבַדְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb Jathniel|יַתְנִיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb the fourth|הָרְבִיעִֽי׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb Elam|עֵילָ֤ם\rb* \rb the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁי֙\rb*, \rb Jehohanan|יְהוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֔י\rb*, \rb and Eliehoenai|אֶלְיְהוֹעֵינַ֖י\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִֽי׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 4 \rb |וּלְעֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb And Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֖ם\rb* \rb also had sons|בָּנִ֑ים\rb*: \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb the firstborn|הַבְּכוֹר֙\rb*, \rb Jehozabad|יְהוֹזָבָ֣ד\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*, \rb Joah|יוֹאָ֤ח\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁי֙\rb*, \rb Sachar|וְשָׂכָ֣ר\rb* \rb the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֔י\rb*, \rb Nethanel|וּנְתַנְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb the fifth|הַחֲמִישִֽׁי׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb Ammiel|עַמִּיאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁי֙\rb*, \rb Issachar|יִשָׂשכָ֣ר\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb*, \rb and Peullethai|פְּעֻלְּתַ֖י\rb* \rb the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֑י\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb had blessed Obed-edom|בֵרֲכ֖וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 6 \rb Also to his son|בְנוֹ֙\rb* \rb Shemaiah|וְלִֽשְׁמַֽעְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb were born|נוֹלַ֣ד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who ruled|הַמִּמְשָׁלִ֖ים\rb* \rb over their families|אֲבִיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb were strong|גִבּ֥וֹרֵי\rb*, \rb capable men|חַ֖יִל\rb*. \v 7 \rb Shemaiah’s|שְׁמַֽעְיָ֗ה\rb* \rb sons were|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Othni|עָ֠תְנִי\rb*, \rb Rephael|וּרְפָאֵ֨ל\rb*, \rb Obed|וְעוֹבֵ֧ד\rb*, \rb and Elzabad|אֶלְזָבָ֛ד\rb*; \rb his brothers were|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb Elihu|אֱלִיה֖וּ\rb* \rb and Semachiah|וּסְמַכְיָֽהוּ׃\rb*, \rb also capable|חָ֑יִל\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵי־\rb*. \v 8 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these were|אֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י׀\rb*\rb |עֹבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb of Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֗ם\rb*; \rb they|הֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb and their sons|וּבְנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and brothers|וַאֲחֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb were capable|חַ֥יִל\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb with strength|בַּכֹּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to do the work|לַעֲבֹדָ֑ה\rb*— \rb 62|שִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb in all|לְעֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb from Obed-edom|אֱדֹֽם׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 9 \rb Meshelemiah|וְלִמְשֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb also had sons|בָּנִ֧ים\rb* \rb and brothers|וְאַחִ֛ים\rb* \rb who were capable|חָ֖יִל\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵי־\rb*— \rb 18 in all|שְׁמוֹנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃ס\rb*.
\li1 \v 10 \rb Hosah|וּלְחֹסָ֥ה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the Merarite|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |מְרָרִ֖י\rb* \rb also had sons|בָּנִ֑ים\rb*: \rb Shimri|שִׁמְרִ֤י\rb* \rb the first|הָרֹאשׁ֙\rb* (\rb although|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְכ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb his father|אָבִ֖יהוּ\rb* \rb had appointed him|וַיְשִׂימֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb as the first|לְרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb*), \v 11 \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִי֙\rb*, \rb Tebaliah|טְבַלְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb and Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the fourth|הָרְבִעִ֑י\rb*. \rb The sons|בָּנִ֧ים\rb* \rb and brothers|וְאַחִ֛ים\rb* \rb of Hosah|לְחֹסָ֖ה\rb* \rb numbered 13|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb These|לְ֠אֵלֶּה\rb* \rb divisions|מַחְלְק֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the gatekeepers|הַשֹּֽׁעֲרִ֜ים\rb*, \rb through their chief|לְרָאשֵׁ֧י\rb* \rb men|הַגְּבָרִ֛ים\rb*, \rb had duties|מִשְׁמָר֖וֹת\rb* \rb for ministering|לְשָׁרֵ֖ת\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \rb just as|לְעֻמַּ֣ת\rb* \rb their relatives did|אֲחֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \v 13 \rb They cast|וַיַּפִּ֨ילוּ\rb* \rb lots|גוֹרָל֜וֹת\rb* \rb for each gate|לְשַׁ֥עַר\rb*,\rb |וָשָֽׁעַר׃פ\rb* \rb according to their families|אֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb*, \rb young|כַּקָּטֹ֧ן\rb* \rb and old alike|כַּגָּד֛וֹל\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 14 \rb The lot|הַגּוֹרָ֛ל\rb* \rb for the East Gate|מִזְרָ֖חָה\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֧ל\rb* \rb to Shelemiah|לְשֶֽׁלֶמְיָ֑הוּ\rb*.\f + \fr 26:14 \fqa Shelemiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Meshelemiah\ft ; see verse 2.\f*
\li1 \rb Then lots|גּֽוֹרָל֔וֹת\rb* \rb were cast|הִפִּ֙ילוּ֙\rb* \rb for his son|בְנ֜וֹ\rb* \rb Zechariah|וּזְכַרְיָ֨הוּ\rb*, \rb a wise|בְּשֶׂ֗כֶל\rb* \rb counselor|יוֹעֵ֣ץ׀\rb*, \rb and the lot|גוֹרָל֖וֹ\rb* \rb for the North Gate|צָפֽוֹנָה׃ס\rb* \rb fell to him|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb*.
\li1 \v 15 \rb The lot for the South Gate|נֶ֑גְבָּה\rb* \rb fell to|לְעֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb Obed-edom|אֱדֹ֖ם\rb*, \rb and the lot for the storehouses|בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |הָאֲסֻפִּֽים׃\rb* \rb to his sons|וּלְבָנָ֖יו\rb*.
\li1 \v 16 \rb The lots for the West Gate|לַֽמַּעֲרָ֔ב\rb* \rb and|עִ֚ם\rb* \rb the Shallecheth|שַׁלֶּ֔כֶת\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb on the ascending|הָעוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb highway|בַּֽמְסִלָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 26:16 \ft Or \fqa on the upper road\f* \rb fell to Shuppim|לְשֻׁפִּ֤ים\rb* \rb and Hosah|וּלְחֹסָה֙\rb*.
\p \rb There were guards|מִשְׁמָ֖ר\rb* \rb stationed|לְעֻמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb at every watch|מִשְׁמָֽר׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Each day|לַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb there were six|שִׁשָּׁה֒\rb* \rb Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֣ם\rb* \rb on the east|לַמִּזְרָח֮\rb*, \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the north|לַצָּפ֤וֹנָה\rb*, \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb on the south|לַנֶּ֥גְבָּה\rb*, \rb and two pairs|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |שְׁנָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb at the storehouse|וְלָאֲסֻפִּ֖ים\rb*. \v 18 \rb As for the court|לַפַּרְבָּ֖ר\rb*\f + \fr 26:18 \ft Hebrew \fqa parbar\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb on the west|לַֽמַּעֲרָ֑ב\rb*, \rb there were four|אַרְבָּעָה֙\rb* \rb at the highway|לַֽמְסִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and two|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb at the court|לַפַּרְבָּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb These were|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb the divisions|מַחְלְקוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the gatekeepers|הַשֹּׁ֣עֲרִ֔ים\rb* \rb who were descendants|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Korah|הַקָּרְחִ֖י\rb* \rb and|וְלִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Merari|מְרָרִֽי׃\rb*.
\s1 The Treasurers, Officers, and Judges
\p \v 20 \rb Now their fellow Levites were|וְֽהַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲחִיָּ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 26:20 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa As for the Levites, Ahijah was\f* \rb in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the treasuries|אֽוֹצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and the treasuries|וּלְאֹֽצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the dedicated things|הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb From the descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Ladan|לַ֠עְדָּן\rb*, \rb who were|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb Gershonites|הַגֵּרְשֻׁנִּ֜י\rb* \rb through Ladan|לְלַעְדָּ֗ן\rb*\f + \fr 26:21 \fqa Ladan \ft is a variant of \fqa Libni\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 6:17|1CH 6:17\ref*.\f* \rb and heads|רָאשֵׁ֧י\rb* \rb of the families|הָאָב֛וֹת\rb* \rb of Ladan|לְלַעְדָּ֥ן\rb* \rb the Gershonite|הַגֵּרְשֻׁנִּ֖י\rb*, \rb were Jehieli|יְחִיאֵלִֽי׃\rb*,\f + \fr 26:21 \fqa Jehieli \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehiel\ft ; also in verse 22; see \ref 1 Chronicles 23:8|1CH 23:8\ref*.\f* \v 22 \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jehieli|יְחִֽיאֵלִ֑י\rb*, \rb Zetham|זֵתָם֙\rb*, \rb and his brother|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb Joel|וְיוֹאֵ֣ל\rb*. \rb They were in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the treasuries|אֹצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb From the Amramites|לַֽעַמְרָמִי֙\rb*, \rb the Izharites|לַיִּצְהָרִ֔י\rb*, \rb the Hebronites|לַֽחֶבְרוֹנִ֖י\rb*, \rb and the Uzzielites|לָֽעָזִּיאֵלִֽי׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 24 \rb Shebuel|וּשְׁבֻאֵל֙\rb*, \rb a descendant|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Gershom|גֵּרְשׁ֣וֹם\rb* \rb son of|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb was the officer|נָגִ֖יד\rb* \rb in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the treasuries|הָאֹצָרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb His relatives|וְאֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb through Eliezer included|לֶֽאֱלִיעֶ֑זֶר\rb* \rb Rehabiah|רְחַבְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֜וֹ\rb*, \rb Jeshaiah|וִֽישַׁעְיָ֤הוּ\rb*\f + \fr 26:25 \fqa Jeshaiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Isshiah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 24:21|1CH 24:21\ref*.\f* \rb his son|בְנוֹ֙\rb*, \rb Joram|וְיֹרָ֣ם\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb Zichri|וְזִכְרִ֥י\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and Shelomith|וּשְׁלֹמוֹת\rb* \rb his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb This|ה֧וּא\rb* \rb Shelomith|שְׁלֹמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָ֗יו\rb* \rb were in charge of|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the treasuries|אֹצְר֤וֹת\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb for the things|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb dedicated|הִקְדִּ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb by King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*, \rb by the heads|וְרָאשֵׁ֧י\rb* \rb of families|הָאָב֛וֹת\rb* \rb who were the commanders|לְשָׂרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִ֥ים\rb* \rb and of hundreds|וְהַמֵּא֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and by the army|הַצָּבָֽא׃\rb* \rb commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb*. \v 27 \rb They had dedicated|הִקְדִּ֑ישׁוּ\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the plunder|הַשָּׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb their battles|הַמִּלְחָמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb to the repair|לְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb Everything|וְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb that had been dedicated|הַֽהִקְדִּ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb by Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb the seer|הָרֹאֶה֙\rb*, \rb Saul|וְשָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kish|קִ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb Abner|וְאַבְנֵ֣ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb and Joab|וְיוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb along with everything else|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb that was dedicated|הַמַּקְדִּ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb was under|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb the care|יַד־\rb* \rb of Shelomith|שְׁלֹמִ֖ית\rb* \rb and his brothers|וְאֶחָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 29 \rb From the Izharites|לַיִּצְהָרִ֞י\rb*, \rb Chenaniah|כְּנַנְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb had the outside|הַחִֽיצוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb duties|לַמְּלָאכָ֤ה\rb*\f + \fr 26:29 \ft Or \fqa the duties outside (the temple) \ft or \fqa the duties outside (Jerusalem)\f* \rb as officers|לְשֹׁטְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and judges|וּלְשֹׁפְטִֽים׃\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*.
\li1 \v 30 \rb From the Hebronites|לַֽחֶבְרוֹנִ֡י\rb*, \rb Hashabiah|חֲשַׁבְיָהוּ֩\rb* \rb and his relatives|וְאֶחָ֨יו\rb*, \rb 1,700|אֶ֣לֶף\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַע־\rb*\rb |מֵא֗וֹת\rb*\rb |עַ֚ל\rb* \rb capable|חַ֜יִל\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵי־\rb*, \rb had charge of the affairs|פְּקֻדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |מֵעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb west|מַעְרָ֑בָה\rb* \rb of the Jordan|לַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb for all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the work|מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and for the service|וְלַעֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb As for the Hebronites|לַֽחֶבְרוֹנִי֙\rb*, \rb Jerijah|יְרִיָּ֣ה\rb*\f + \fr 26:31 \fqa Jerijah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jeriah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 23:19|1CH 23:19\ref*.\f* \rb was the chief|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb of the Hebronites|לַֽחֶבְרוֹנִ֥י\rb*, \rb according to the genealogies|לְתֹלְדֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb of his ancestors|לְאָב֑וֹת\rb*. \rb In the fortieth|הָֽאַרְבָּעִ֜ים\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of David’s|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb reign|לְמַלְכ֤וּת\rb* \rb the records were searched|נִדְרָ֔שׁוּ\rb*, \rb and strong|גִּבּ֥וֹרֵי\rb*, \rb capable men|חַ֖יִל\rb* \rb were found|וַיִּמָּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb among the Hebronites|בָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb at Jazer|בְּיַעְזֵ֥יר\rb* \rb in Gilead|גִּלְעָֽד׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb Among Jerijah’s relatives|וְאֶחָ֣יו\rb* \rb there were 2,700|אַלְפַּ֛יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַ֥ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb capable|חַ֗יִל\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb who were heads|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of families|הָאָב֑וֹת\rb*. \rb King|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb appointed them|וַיַּפְקִידֵ֞ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the Reubenites|הָראוּבֵנִ֤י\rb*, \rb the Gadites|וְהַגָּדִי֙\rb*, \rb and the half-tribe|וַחֲצִי֙\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשִּׁ֔י\rb* \rb for every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb matter pertaining to|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and for the affairs|וּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb*.
\c 27
\s1 Twelve Captains for Twelve Months
\p \v 1 \rb This is the list|לְֽמִסְפָּרָ֡ם\rb*\rb |וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל׀\rb*— \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of families|הָאָב֣וֹת\rb*, \rb the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of thousands|הָֽאֲלָפִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb and of hundreds|וְהַמֵּא֡וֹת\rb*, \rb and their officers|וְשֹׁטְרֵיהֶם֩\rb* \rb who served|הַמְשָׁרְתִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb in every|לְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb matter|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb concerning the divisions|הַֽמַּחְלְק֗וֹת\rb* \rb on rotating military duty|הַבָּאָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְהַיֹּצֵאת֙\rb* \rb each month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |בְּחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb throughout|לְכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |חָדְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb the year|הַשָּׁנָ֑ה\rb*. \rb There were 24,000 men|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb in each|הָֽאַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb division|הַֽמַּחֲלֹ֙קֶת֙\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 2 \rb Jashobeam|יָֽשָׁבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zabdiel|זַבְדִּיאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb was in charge of|עַ֞ל\rb* \rb the first|הָרִֽאשׁוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb division|הַמַּחֲלֹ֤קֶת\rb*, \rb which was assigned the first|הָרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַֽחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*. \v 3 \rb |מִן־\rb* \rb He was a descendant|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Perez|פֶ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb and chief|הָרֹ֛אשׁ\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the army|הַצְּבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the first|הָרִאשֽׁוֹן׃\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*.
\li1 \v 4 \rb Dodai|דּוֹדַ֤י\rb*\f + \fr 27:4 \fqa Dodai \ft is a variant of \fqa Dodo\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 23:9|2SA 23:9\ref*.\f* \rb the Ahohite|הָאֲחוֹחִי֙\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַ֞ל\rb* \rb the division|מַחֲלֹ֣קֶת׀\rb* \rb for the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֗י\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and Mikloth|וּמִקְל֖וֹת\rb* \rb was the leader|הַנָּגִ֑יד\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb*\rb |מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb his division|וּמַ֣חֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 5 \rb The third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb army|הַצָּבָ֤א\rb* \rb commander|שַׂ֣ר\rb*, \rb as chief|רֹ֑אשׁ\rb* \rb for the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֛ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*. \v 6 \rb This|ה֧וּא\rb* \rb Benaiah|בְנָיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb was mighty|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb among the Thirty|הַשְּׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and was over|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the Thirty|הַשְּׁלֹשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb Ammizabad|עַמִּיזָבָ֖ד\rb* \rb was in charge of his division|וּמַ֣חֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 7 \rb The fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִ֞י\rb*, \rb for the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Joab’s|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֣י\rb*\rb |עֲשָׂה־\rb* \rb Asahel|אֵל֙\rb*, \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Zebadiah|וּזְבַדְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb was commander after him|אַחֲרָ֑יו\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 8 \rb The fifth|הַחַמִישִׁי֙\rb*, \rb for the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was the commander|הַשַּׂ֖ר\rb* \rb Shamhuth|שַׁמְה֣וּת\rb*\f + \fr 27:8 \fqa Shamhuth \ft is a variant of \fqa Shammoth \ft or \fqa Shammah\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 11:27|1CH 11:27\ref* and 2 Samuel 23:25.\f* \rb the Izrahite|הַיִּזְרָ֑ח\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 9 \rb The sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁי֙\rb*, \rb for the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Ira|עִירָ֥א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ikkesh|עִקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the Tekoite|הַתְּקוֹעִ֑י\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 10 \rb The seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִי֙\rb*, \rb for the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Helez|חֶ֥לֶץ\rb* \rb the Pelonite|הַפְּלוֹנִ֖י\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb an Ephraimite|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 11 \rb The eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִי֙\rb*, \rb for the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Sibbecai|סִבְּכַ֥י\rb* \rb the Hushathite|הַחֻשָׁתִ֖י\rb*, \rb a Zerahite|לַזַּרְחִ֑י\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 12 \rb The ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִי֙\rb*, \rb for the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Abiezer|אֲבִיעֶ֥זֶר\rb* \rb the Anathothite|הָעַנְּתֹתִ֖י\rb*, \rb a Benjamite|לַבֶּנְיְמִינִי\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 13 \rb The tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִי֙\rb*, \rb for the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִ֔י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Maharai|מַהְרַ֥י\rb* \rb the Netophathite|הַנְּטֽוֹפָתִ֖י\rb*, \rb a Zerahite|לַזַּרְחִ֑י\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַֽחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 14 \rb The eleventh|עַשְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb*, \rb for the eleventh|לְעַשְׁתֵּ֣י־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the Pirathonite|הַפִּרְעָתוֹנִ֖י\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb an Ephraimite|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\li1 \v 15 \rb The twelfth|הַשְּׁנֵ֤ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb*, \rb for the twelfth|לִשְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb was Heldai|חֶלְדַּ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 27:15 \fqa Heldai \ft is a variant of \fqa Heled\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 11:30|1CH 11:30\ref* and 2 Samuel 23:29.\f* \rb the Netophathite|הַנְּטוֹפָתִ֖י\rb*, \rb from the family of Othniel|לְעָתְנִיאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb There were 24,000|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃פ\rb* \rb men in|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb his division|מַחֲלֻקְתּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\s1 The Leaders of the Twelve Tribes
\p \v 16 \rb These officers were in charge of|וְעַל֙\rb*\rb |נָגִ֔יד\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Over the Reubenites|לָרֽאוּבֵנִ֣י\rb* \rb was Eliezer|אֱלִיעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zichri|זִכְרִ֑יס\rb*;
\li1 \rb over the Simeonites|לַשִּׁ֨מְעוֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb was Shephatiah|שְׁפַטְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Maacah|מַעֲכָֽה׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 17 \rb over Levi|לְלֵוִ֛י\rb* \rb was Hashabiah|חֲשַׁבְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Kemuel|קְמוּאֵ֖ל\rb*;
\li1 \rb over Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb was Zadok|צָדֽוֹק׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 18 \rb over Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֕ה\rb* \rb was Elihu|אֱלִיה֖וּ\rb*, \rb one of David’s|דָוִ֑יד\rb* \rb brothers|מֵאֲחֵ֣י\rb*;
\li1 \rb over Issachar|לְיִ֨שָׂשכָ֔ר\rb* \rb was Omri|עָמְרִ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Michael|מִיכָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 19 \rb over Zebulun|לִזְבוּלֻ֕ן\rb* \rb was Ishmaiah|יִֽשְׁמַֽעְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Obadiah|עֹבַדְיָ֑הוּ\rb*;
\li1 \rb over Naphtali|לְנַ֨פְתָּלִ֔י\rb* \rb was Jerimoth|יְרִימ֖וֹת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Azriel|עַזְרִיאֵֽל׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 20 \rb over the Ephraimites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb was Hoshea|הוֹשֵׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Azaziah|עֲזַזְיָ֑הוּ\rb*;
\li1 \rb over one of the half-tribes|לַחֲצִי֙\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb was Joel|יוֹאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Pedaiah|פְּדָיָֽהוּ׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 21 \rb over the half-tribe|לַחֲצִ֤י\rb* \rb of Manasseh|הַֽמְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb in Gilead|גִּלְעָ֔דָה\rb* \rb was Iddo|יִדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֑הוּס\rb*;
\li1 \rb over Benjamin|לְבִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb was Jaasiel|יַעֲשִׂיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abner|אַבְנֵֽר׃ס\rb*;
\q1 \v 22 \rb and over Dan|לְדָ֕ן\rb* \rb was Azarel|עֲזַרְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jeroham|יְרֹחָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb These were|אֵ֕לֶּה\rb* \rb the leaders|שָׂרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb David|דָוִיד֙\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb count|נָשָׂ֤א\rb*\rb |מִסְפָּרָ֔ם\rb* \rb the men|לְמִבֶּ֛ן\rb* \rb aged|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb or under|וּלְמָ֑טָּה\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had said that|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb He would make Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as numerous|לְהַרְבּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as the stars|כְּכוֹכְבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the sky|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֨ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֜ה\rb* \rb began|הֵחֵ֤ל\rb* \rb to count the men|לִמְנוֹת֙\rb* \rb but did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb finish|כִלָּ֔ה\rb*. \rb For because of this census|בָזֹ֛את\rb* \rb wrath|קֶ֖צֶף\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and the number|הַמִּסְפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb was not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb entered|עָלָה֙\rb*\rb |בְּמִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb in the Book|דִּבְרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽיד׃ס\rb*.
\s1 David’s Various Overseers
\li1 \v 25 \rb Azmaveth|עַזְמָ֖וֶת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Adiel|עֲדִיאֵ֑לס\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb storehouses|אֹצְר֣וֹת\rb*.
\li1 \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּֽהוּ׃ס\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the storehouses|הָֽאֹצָר֡וֹת\rb* \rb in the country|בַּשָּׂדֶ֞ה\rb*, \rb in the cities|בֶּעָרִ֤ים\rb*, \rb in the villages|וּבַכְּפָרִים֙\rb*, \rb and in the fortresses|וּבַמִּגְדָּל֔וֹת\rb*.
\li1 \v 26 \rb Ezri|עֶזְרִ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Chelub|כְּלֽוּב׃\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַ֗ל\rb* \rb the workers|עֹשֵׂי֙\rb*\rb |מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb* \rb in the fields|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb who tilled|לַעֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb the soil|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb*.
\li1 \v 27 \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֖י\rb* \rb the Ramathite|הָרָֽמָתִ֑י\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the vineyards|הַ֨כְּרָמִ֔ים\rb*.
\li1 \rb Zabdi|זַבְדִּ֖י\rb* \rb the Shiphmite|הַשִּׁפְמִֽי׃ס\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַ֤ל\rb* \rb the produce of the vineyards|שֶׁבַּכְּרָמִים֙\rb* \rb for the wine|הַיַּ֔יִן\rb* \rb vats|לְאֹצְר֣וֹת\rb*.
\li1 \v 28 \rb Baal-hanan|חָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb the Gederite|הַגְּדֵרִ֑יס\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the olive|הַזֵּיתִ֤ים\rb* \rb and sycamore trees|וְהַשִּׁקְמִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the foothills|בַּשְּׁפֵלָ֔ה\rb*.\f + \fr 27:28 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f*
\li1 \rb Joash|יוֹעָֽשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the stores|אֹצְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of olive oil|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb*.
\li1 \v 29 \rb Shitrai|שִׁטְרַי\rb* \rb the Sharonite|הַשָּׁרוֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the herds|הַבָּקָר֙\rb* \rb grazing|הָרֹעִ֣ים\rb* \rb in Sharon|בַּשָּׁר֔וֹן\rb*.
\li1 \rb Shaphat|שָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Adlai|עַדְלָֽי׃ס\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the herds|הַבָּקָר֙\rb* \rb in the valleys|בָּֽעֲמָקִ֔ים\rb*.
\li1 \v 30 \rb Obil|אוֹבִ֖יל\rb* \rb the Ishmaelite|הַיִּשְׁמְעֵלִ֑י\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the camels|הַ֨גְּמַלִּ֔ים\rb*.
\li1 \rb Jehdeiah|יֶחְדְּיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the Meronothite|הַמֵּרֹנֹתִֽי׃ס\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the donkeys|הָ֣אֲתֹנ֔וֹת\rb*.
\li1 \v 31 \rb Jaziz|יָזִ֣יז\rb* \rb the Hagrite|הַֽהַגְרִ֑י\rb* \rb was in charge of|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the flocks|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*.
\li1 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb officials were|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb in charge of King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִֽיד׃\rb* \rb property|הָרְכ֔וּשׁ\rb*.\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*
\s1 The Counselors
\li1 \v 32 \rb David’s|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb uncle|דּוֹד־\rb* \rb Jonathan|וִֽיהוֹנָתָ֤ן\rb* \rb was a counselor|יוֹעֵ֔ץ\rb*; \rb he|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb was a man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of insight|מֵבִ֥ין\rb* \rb and a scribe|וְסוֹפֵ֖ר\rb*.
\li1 \rb Jehiel|וִֽיחִיאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hachmoni|חַכְמוֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb attended to|עִם־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 33 \rb Ahithophel|וַאֲחִיתֹ֖פֶל\rb* \rb was the king’s|לַמֶּ֑לֶךְס\rb* \rb counselor|יוֹעֵ֣ץ\rb*.
\li1 \rb Hushai|וְחוּשַׁ֥י\rb* \rb the Archite|הָאַרְכִּ֖י\rb* \rb was the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb friend|רֵ֥עַ\rb*.
\li1 \v 34 \rb Ahithophel|אֲחִיתֹ֗פֶל\rb* \rb was succeeded by|וְאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֤ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*, \rb then by Abiathar|וְאֶבְיָתָ֔ר\rb*.
\li1 \rb Joab|יוֹאָֽב׃פ\rb* \rb was the commander|וְשַׂר־\rb* \rb of the king’s|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb army|צָבָ֥א\rb*.
\c 28
\s1 David Commissions Solomon
\p \v 1 \rb Now David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיַּקְהֵ֣ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the leaders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*: \rb the leaders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the tribes|הַשְּׁבָטִ֣ים\rb*, \rb the leaders|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the divisions|הַמַּחְלְק֣וֹת\rb* \rb in the king’s|הַמֶּ֟לֶךְ\rb* \rb service|הַמְשָׁרְתִ֪ים\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִ֣ים\rb* \rb and|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּא֡וֹת\rb*, \rb and the officials|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb in charge of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the property|רְכוּשׁ־\rb* \rb and cattle|וּמִקְנֶה֩׀\rb* \rb of the king|לַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֜יו\rb*, \rb along with|עִם־\rb* \rb the court officials|הַסָּרִיסִ֧ים\rb* \rb and mighty men|וְהַגִּבּוֹרִ֛ים\rb*— \rb every|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb mighty man|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of valor|חָ֖יִל\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb rose|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb his feet|רַגְלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Listen to me|שְׁמָע֖וּנִי\rb*, \rb my brothers|אַחַ֣י\rb* \rb and my people|וְעַמִּ֑י\rb*.\rb |אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb It was in|עִם־\rb* \rb my heart|לְבָבִ֡י\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנוֹת֩\rb* \rb a house|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb as a resting place|מְנוּחָ֜ה\rb* \rb for the ark|לַאֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and as a footstool|וְלַהֲדֹם֙\rb*\rb |רַגְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb for our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*. \rb I had made preparations|וַהֲכִינ֖וֹתִי\rb* \rb to build it|לִבְנֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb but God|וְהָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb said|אָ֣מַר\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb*, ‘\rb You are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to build|תִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a house|בַ֖יִת\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֑י\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַ֖תָּה\rb* \rb are a man|אִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמ֛וֹת\rb* \rb who has shed|שָׁפָֽכְתָּ׃\rb* \rb blood|וְדָמִ֥ים\rb*.’
\p \v 4 \rb Yet the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֩\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb*, \rb chose|וַיִּבְחַ֡ר\rb* \rb me|בִּ֜י\rb* \rb out of all|מִכֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb my father’s|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֨וֹת\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֔ם\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb He chose|בָּחַ֣ר\rb* \rb Judah|בִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb as leader|לְנָגִ֔יד\rb*, \rb and from the house|וּבְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb He chose my father’s|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and from my father’s|אָבִ֔י\rb*\rb |בִּ֣י\rb* \rb sons|וּבִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb He was pleased|רָצָ֔ה\rb* \rb to make me king|לְהַמְלִ֖יךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And of all|וּמִכָּ֨ל־\rb* \rb my sons|בָּנַ֔י\rb*— \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb has given|נָ֥תַן\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֣ים\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֔ים\rb*— \rb He has chosen|וַיִּבְחַר֙\rb* \rb Solomon|בִּשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb my son|בְנִ֔י\rb* \rb to sit|לָשֶׁ֗בֶת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֛א\rb* \rb of the kingdom|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb*, ‘\rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb your son|בִנְךָ֔\rb* \rb is the one|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb who will build|יִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb My house|בֵיתִ֖י\rb* \rb and My courts|וַחֲצֵרוֹתָ֑י\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb I have chosen him|בָחַ֨רְתִּי\rb* \rb as|ב֥וֹ\rb* \rb My|לִי֙\rb* \rb son|לְבֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will be|אֶֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb his|לּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Father|לְאָֽב׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb I will establish|וַהֲכִינוֹתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַלְכוּת֖וֹ\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb he resolutely|יֶחֱזַ֗ק\rb* \rb carries out|לַעֲשׂ֛וֹת\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֥י\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*, \rb as is being done|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb this day|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*.’
\p \v 8 \rb So now|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֨י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb*, \rb the assembly|קְהַל־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb and in the hearing|וּבְאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb keep|שִׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb and seek out|וְדִרְשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb you may possess|תִּֽירְשׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and leave it as an inheritance|וְהִנְחַלְתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb to your descendants|לִבְנֵיכֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*. \v 9 \rb As for you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה־\rb* \rb my son|בְנִ֡י\rb*, \rb know|דַּע֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֜יךָ\rb* \rb and serve Him|וְעָבְדֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb wholeheartedly|בְּלֵ֤ב\rb*\rb |שָׁלֵם֙\rb* \rb and with a willing|חֲפֵצָ֔ה\rb* \rb mind|וּבְנֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb searches|דּוֹרֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb heart|לְבָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb and understands|מֵבִ֑ין\rb* \rb the intent|יֵ֥צֶר\rb* \rb of every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb thought|מַחֲשָׁב֖וֹת\rb*. \rb If|אִֽם־\rb* \rb you seek Him|תִּדְרְשֶׁ֙נּוּ֙\rb*, \rb He will be found|יִמָּ֣צֵא\rb* \rb by you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*; \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you forsake Him|תַּֽעַזְבֶ֖נּוּ\rb*, \rb He will reject you|יַזְנִיחֲךָ֥\rb* \rb forever|לָעַֽד׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Consider|רְאֵ֣ה׀\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has chosen|בָּ֧חַר\rb* \rb you|בְּךָ֛\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֥יִת\rb* \rb for the sanctuary|לַמִּקְדָּ֖שׁ\rb*. \rb Be strong|חֲזַ֥ק\rb* \rb and do it|וַעֲשֵֽׂה׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 The Plans for the Temple
\p \v 11 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֡וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb the plans|תַּבְנִ֣ית\rb* \rb for the portico of the temple|הָאוּלָם֩\rb*,\f + \fr 28:11 \ft LXX; Hebrew does not include \fqa of the temple\ft .\f*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb its buildings|בָּ֨תָּ֜יו\rb*, \rb storehouses|וְגַנְזַכָּ֧יו\rb*, \rb upper rooms|וַעֲלִיֹּתָ֛יו\rb*, \rb inner|הַפְּנִימִ֖ים\rb* \rb rooms|וַחֲדָרָ֥יו\rb*, \rb and the room|וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb for the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּֽרֶת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 28:11 \ft Or \fqa atonement cover\f* \v 12 \rb The plans|וְתַבְנִ֗ית\rb* \rb contained everything|כֹּל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb David had|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb in|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb mind|בָר֙וּחַ֙\rb*\f + \fr 28:12 \ft Or \fqa had with him by the Spirit\f* \rb for the courts|לְחַצְר֧וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb for all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb the surrounding|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb rooms|הַלְּשָׁכ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb for the treasuries|לְאֹֽצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וּלְאֹצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the dedicated things|הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb for the divisions|וּֽלְמַחְלְקוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*, \rb for all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלֶ֖אכֶת\rb* \rb of service|עֲבוֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and for all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of service|עֲבוֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 14 \rb the weight|בַּמִּשְׁקָל֙\rb*\rb |לַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the gold|לַזָּהָ֤ב\rb* \rb articles|כְּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb for every kind of service|עֲבוֹדָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וַעֲבוֹדָ֑ה\rb*;
\li1 \rb the weight|בְּמִשְׁקָ֔ל\rb* \rb of all|לְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb articles|כְּלֵ֤י\rb* \rb for every kind|לְכָל־\rb*\rb |כְּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of service|עֲבוֹדָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וַעֲבוֹדָֽה׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 15 \rb the weight|וּמִשְׁקָ֞ל\rb* \rb of the gold|הַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb lampstands|לִמְנֹר֣וֹת\rb* \rb and their|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb lamps|וְנֵרֹֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb including the weight|בְּמִשְׁקַל־\rb* \rb of each lampstand|מְנוֹרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּמְנוֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and its lamps|וְנֵרֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb*;
\li1 \rb the weight|בְּמִשְׁקָל֙\rb* \rb of each silver|הַכֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb lampstand|וְלִמְנֹר֨וֹת\rb* \rb and its lamps|וְנֵרֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb according to the use|כַּעֲבוֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of each lampstand|לִמְנוֹרָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְנוֹרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּמְנוֹרָֽה׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 16 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the weight|מִשְׁקָ֛ל\rb* \rb of gold|הַזָּהָ֥ב\rb* \rb for each table|לְשֻׁלְחֲנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of showbread|הַֽמַּעֲרֶ֖כֶת\rb*, \rb and of silver|וְכֶ֖סֶף\rb*\rb |לְשֻׁלְחֲנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb for the silver|הַכָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb tables|לְשֻׁלְחַ֣ן\rb*\rb |וְשֻׁלְחָ֑ן\rb*;
\li1 \v 17 \rb the weight of the pure|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb for the forks|וְהַמִּזְלָג֧וֹת\rb*, \rb sprinkling bowls|וְהַמִּזְרָק֛וֹת\rb*, \rb and pitchers|וְהַקְּשָׂוֺ֖ת\rb*;
\li1 \rb the weight|בְּמִשְׁקָל֙\rb* \rb of each gold|הַזָּהָ֤ב\rb* \rb dish|וְלִכְפוֹרֵ֨י\rb*\rb |לִכְפ֣וֹר\rb*;
\li1 \rb the weight|בְּמִשְׁקָ֖ל\rb*\rb |לִכְפ֥וֹר\rb*\rb |וּכְפֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb of each silver|הַכֶּ֛סֶף\rb* \rb bowl|וּכְפ֔וֹר\rb*\rb |וְלִכְפוֹרֵ֥י\rb*;
\li1 \v 18 \rb the weight|בַּמִּשְׁקָ֑ל\rb* \rb of the refined|מְזֻקָּ֖ק\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb for the altar|וּלְמִזְבַּ֧ח\rb* \rb of incense|הַקְּטֹ֛רֶת\rb*;
\li1 \rb and the plans|וּלְתַבְנִ֣ית\rb* \rb for the chariot|הַמֶּרְכָּבָ֗ה\rb* \rb of the gold|זָהָב֙\rb* \rb cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִ֤ים\rb* \rb that spread their wings|לְפֹ֣רְשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb and overshadowed|וְסֹכְכִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 “\rb All this,” said David|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb*, “\rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the details|מַלְאֲכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of this plan|הַתַּבְנִֽית׃פ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has made clear to me|הִשְׂכִּ֑יל\rb* \rb in writing|בִּכְתָ֛ב\rb* \rb by His hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַ֣י\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb David also|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Be strong|חֲזַ֤ק\rb* \rb and courageous|וֶאֱמַץ֙\rb*, \rb and do it|וַעֲשֵׂ֔ה\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֖א\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged|תֵּחָ֑ת\rb*, \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb*, \rb my God|אֱלֹהַי֙\rb*, \rb is with you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb*. \rb He will neither|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb fail you|יַרְפְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb nor forsake you|יַֽעַזְבֶ֔ךָּ\rb* \rb before|עַד־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלֶ֖אכֶת\rb* \rb for the service|עֲבוֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb is finished|לִכְל֕וֹת\rb*. \v 21 \rb The divisions|מַחְלְקוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb are ready|וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the service|עֲבוֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|וְעִמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb every|בְכָל־\rb* \rb willing man|נָדִ֤יב\rb* \rb of every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb skill|בַּֽחָכְמָה֙\rb* \rb will be at your disposal for the work|מְלָאכָ֜ה\rb*. \rb The officials|וְהַשָּׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and all|לְכָל־\rb*\rb |עֲבוֹדָ֔ה\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְכָל־\rb* \rb are fully at your|וְכָל־\rb* \rb command|דְּבָרֶֽיךָ׃פ\rb*.”
\c 29
\s1 Offerings for the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֔ל\rb*, “\rb My son|בְנִ֥י\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֨ה\rb*, \rb the one|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb whom|בּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has chosen|בָּֽחַר־\rb*, \rb is young|נַ֣עַר\rb* \rb and inexperienced|וָרָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb The task|וְהַמְּלָאכָ֣ה\rb* \rb is great|גְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this palace|הַבִּירָ֔ה\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb for man|לְאָדָם֙\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Now with all|וּֽכְכָל־\rb* \rb my ability|כֹּחִ֞י\rb* \rb I have made provision|הֲכִינ֣וֹתִי\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהַ֗י\rb* — \rb gold|הַזָּהָ֣ב׀\rb* \rb for the gold articles|לַ֠זָּהָב\rb*, \rb silver|וְהַכֶּ֨סֶף\rb* \rb for the silver|לַכֶּ֜סֶף\rb*, \rb bronze|וְהַנְּחֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb for the bronze|לַנְּחֹ֗שֶׁת\rb*, \rb iron|הַבַּרְזֶל֙\rb* \rb for the iron|לַבַּרְזֶ֔ל\rb*, \rb and wood|וְהָעֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the wood|לָעֵצִ֑ים\rb*, \rb as well as onyx|אַבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |שֹׁ֨הַם\rb* \rb for the settings|וּמִלּוּאִ֜ים\rb*, \rb turquoise|אַבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |פ֣וּךְ\rb*, \rb stones of various colors|וְרִקְמָ֗ה\rb*, \rb all kinds|וְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb of precious|יְקָרָ֛ה\rb* \rb stones|אֶ֧בֶן\rb*, \rb and slabs|וְאַבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of marble|שַׁ֖יִשׁ\rb* — \rb all in abundance|לָרֹֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Moreover|וְע֗וֹד\rb*, \rb because of my delight|בִּרְצוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהַ֔י\rb*,\rb |יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb I now give|נָתַ֤תִּי\rb* \rb for it|לְבֵית־\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהַי֙\rb* \rb my personal treasures|סְגֻלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and silver|וָכָ֑סֶף\rb*, \rb over and above|לְמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb that I have provided|הֲכִינ֖וֹתִי\rb* \rb for this holy|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb temple|לְבֵ֥ית\rb*: \v 4 \rb three|שְׁלֹ֧שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֛ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכְּרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb*\f + \fr 29:4 \fqa 3,000 talents \ft is approximately 113 tons or 103 metric tons of gold.\f* (\rb the gold|מִזְּהַ֣ב\rb* \rb of Ophir|אוֹפִ֑יר\rb*) \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעַ֨ת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֤ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of refined|מְזֻקָּ֔ק\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb*,\f + \fr 29:4 \fqa 7,000 talents \ft is approximately 264 tons or 239.5 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb to overlay|לָט֖וּחַ\rb* \rb the walls|קִיר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the buildings|הַבָּתִּֽים׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb |לַזָּהָ֤ב\rb* \rb for the gold work|לַזָּהָב֙\rb* \rb and the silver work|וְלַכֶּ֣סֶף\rb*\rb |לַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb*, \rb and for all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb the work|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to be done by|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb the craftsmen|חָרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*. \rb Now who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb is willing|מִתְנַדֵּ֔ב\rb* \rb to consecrate|לְמַלֹּ֥אות\rb* \rb himself|יָד֛וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*?”
\p \v 6 \rb Then the leaders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the families|הָאָב֜וֹת\rb*, \rb the officers|וְשָׂרֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of thousands|הָאֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb and of hundreds|וְהַמֵּא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and the officials|וּלְשָׂרֵ֖י\rb* \rb in charge of the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb* \rb gave willingly|וַיִּֽתְנַדְּבוּ֩\rb*. \v 7 \rb Toward the service|לַעֲבוֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God’s|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb they gave|וַֽיִּתְּנ֞וּ\rb* \rb 5,000|חֲמֵֽשֶׁת־\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֮\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּרִ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 29:7 \fqa 5,000 talents \ft is approximately 188.5 tons or 171 metric tons of gold.\f* \rb and 10,000|רִבּוֹ֒\rb* \rb darics|וַאֲדַרְכֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֞ב\rb*,\f + \fr 29:7 \ft Or \fqa 10,000 gold drachmas\ft ; that is, approximately 185.2 pounds or 84 kilograms of gold coins\f* \rb 10,000|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּרִים֙\rb* \rb of silver|וְכֶ֗סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 29:7 \fqa 10,000 talents \ft is approximately 377 tons or 342 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb 18,000|רִבּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמוֹנַ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb of bronze|וּנְחֹ֕שֶׁת\rb*,\f + \fr 29:7 \fqa 18,000 talents \ft is approximately 678.6 tons or 615.6 metric tons of bronze.\f* \rb and 100,000|מֵֽאָה־\rb*\rb |אֶ֥לֶף\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּרִֽים׃\rb* \rb of iron|וּבַרְזֶ֖ל\rb*.\f + \fr 29:7 \fqa 100,000 talents \ft is approximately 3,770 tons or 3,420 metric tons of iron.\f* \v 8 \rb Whoever had|וְהַנִּמְצָ֤א\rb*\rb |אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb precious stones|אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb gave them|נָתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb to the treasury|לְאוֹצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb under|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb the care|יַד־\rb* \rb of Jehiel|יְחִיאֵ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 29:8 \fqa Jehiel \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehieli\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 26:21|1CH 26:21\ref*.\f* \rb the Gershonite|הַגֵּרְשֻׁנִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb And the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמְח֤וּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the willing response of their leaders|הִֽתְנַדְּבָ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb they had given|הִֽתְנַדְּב֖וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD freely|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |בְּלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and wholeheartedly|שָׁלֵ֔ם\rb*. \rb And King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb also|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb rejoiced|שָׂמַ֖ח\rb*\rb |שִׂמְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb greatly|גְדוֹלָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 David’s Prayer of Blessing
\p \v 10 \rb Then David|דָּוִיד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the assembly|הַקָּהָ֑ל\rb* \rb and|דָּוִ֗יד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb May You|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb be blessed|בָּר֨וּךְ\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of our father|אָבִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb from everlasting|מֵעוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 11 \rb Yours|לְךָ֣\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb*, \rb is the greatness|הַגְּדֻלָּ֨ה\rb* \rb and the power|וְהַגְּבוּרָ֤ה\rb* \rb and the glory|וְהַתִּפְאֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb and the splendor|וְהַה֔וֹד\rb* \rb and the majesty|וְהַנֵּ֣צַח\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb everything|כֹ֖ל\rb* \rb in heaven|בַּשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb and on earth belongs to You|וּבָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.
\pmo \rb Yours|לְךָ֤\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb is the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and You are exalted|וְהַמִּתְנַשֵּׂ֖א\rb* \rb as head|לְרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb* \rb over all|לְכֹ֥ל׀\rb*. \v 12 \rb Both riches|וְהָעֹ֤שֶׁר\rb* \rb and honor|וְהַכָּבוֹד֙\rb* \rb come from You|מִלְּפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and You|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb are the ruler|מוֹשֵׁ֣ל\rb* \rb over all|בַּכֹּ֔ל\rb*. \rb In Your hands|וּבְיָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb are power|כֹּ֣חַ\rb* \rb and might|וּגְבוּרָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וּבְיָ֣דְךָ֔\rb* \rb to exalt|לְגַדֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb and give strength|וּלְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb to all|לַכֹּֽל׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 13 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb we|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb*\rb |לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb give You thanks|מוֹדִ֥ים\rb*, \rb and we praise|וּֽמְהַֽלְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb Your glorious|תִּפְאַרְתֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb name|לְשֵׁ֥ם\rb*. \v 14 \rb But|וְכִ֨י\rb* \rb who am|מִ֤י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb and who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb are my people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we should be able|נַעְצֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |כֹּ֔חַ\rb* \rb to give as generously|לְהִתְנַדֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb as this|כָּזֹ֑את\rb*? \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb comes from You|מִמְּךָ֣\rb*, \rb and from Your own hand|וּמִיָּדְךָ֖\rb* \rb we have given|נָתַ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb to You|לָֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֧חְנוּ\rb* \rb are foreigners|גֵרִ֨ים\rb* \rb and strangers|וְתוֹשָׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Your presence|לְפָנֶ֛יךָ\rb*, \rb as were all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb our forefathers|אֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb Our days|יָמֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb are like a shadow|כַּצֵּ֧ל׀\rb*, \rb without|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb hope|מִקְוֶֽה׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 16 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb from Your hand|מִיָּדְךָ֥\rb* \rb comes|הִיא\rb* \rb all|כֹ֣ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb abundance|הֶהָמ֤וֹן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we have provided|הֲכִינֹ֔נוּ\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb You|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb a house|בַ֖יִת\rb* \rb for Your holy|קָדְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Name|לְשֵׁ֣ם\rb*, \rb and all of it|הַכֹּֽל׃\rb* \rb belongs to You|וּלְךָ֥\rb*. \v 17 \rb I know|וְיָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb*, \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֔י\rb*, \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb test|בֹּחֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the heart|לֵבָ֔ב\rb* \rb and delight|תִּרְצֶ֑ה\rb* \rb in uprightness|וּמֵישָׁרִ֖ים\rb*. \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb have given willingly|הִתְנַדַּ֣בְתִּי\rb* \rb and with an upright|בְּיֹ֤שֶׁר\rb* \rb heart|לְבָבִי֙\rb*, \rb and now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb who are present|הַנִּמְצְאוּ־\rb* \rb here|פֹ֔ה\rb* \rb giving joyfully|בְשִׂמְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb and willingly|לְהִֽתְנַדֶּב־\rb* \rb to You|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 18 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱ֠לֹהֵי\rb* \rb of our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֞ם\rb*, \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֤ק\rb*, \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb keep|שֳׁמְרָה־\rb* \rb this|זֹּ֣את\rb* \rb desire|לְיֵ֥צֶר\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the intentions|מַחְשְׁב֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the hearts|לְבַ֣ב\rb* \rb of Your people|עַמֶּ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb and direct|וְהָכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb their hearts|לְבָבָ֖ם\rb* \rb toward You|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And give|תֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb my son|בְנִ֗י\rb* \rb Solomon|וְלִשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb a whole|שָׁלֵ֔ם\rb* \rb heart|לֵבָ֣ב\rb* \rb to keep|לִשְׁמוֹר֙\rb* \rb and carry out|וְלַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb all|הַכֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb Your commandments|מִצְוֺתֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb decrees|עֵדְוֺתֶ֖יךָ\rb*, \rb and statutes|וְחֻקֶּ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and to build|וְלִבְנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb Your palace|הַבִּירָ֥ה\rb* \rb for which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have made provision|הֲכִינֽוֹתִי׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb Then David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֔ל\rb*, “\rb Bless|בָּֽרְכוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb So the whole|כָֽל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֗ל\rb* \rb blessed|וַיְבָרֲכ֣וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבֹֽתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb They bowed down|וַיִּקְּד֧וּ\rb* \rb and paid homage|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֛וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and to the king|וְלַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\s1 Solomon Anointed King
\r (\ref 1 Kings 1:32–40|1KI 1:32-40\ref*)
\p \v 21 \rb The next day|לְֽמָחֳרַת֮\rb*\rb |הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַהוּא֒\rb* \rb they offered|וַיִּזְבְּח֣וּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְ֠בָחִים\rb*\rb |וַיַּעֲל֨וּ\rb*\rb |לַיהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb and presented burnt offerings|עֹל֜וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֗ה\rb*: \rb a thousand|אֶ֜לֶף\rb* \rb bulls|פָּרִ֨ים\rb*, \rb a thousand|אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb rams|אֵילִ֥ים\rb*, \rb and a thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb lambs|כְּבָשִׂ֥ים\rb*, \rb along with their drink offerings|וְנִסְכֵּיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and other sacrifices|וּזְבָחִ֥ים\rb* \rb in abundance|לָרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb That|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb they ate|וַיֹּאכְל֨וּ\rb* \rb and drank|וַיִּשְׁתּ֜וּ\rb* \rb with great|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb joy|בְּשִׂמְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*.
\p \rb Then, for a second|שֵׁנִית֙\rb* \rb time, they designated David’s|דָּוִ֔יד\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb as king|וַיַּמְלִ֤יכוּ\rb*, \rb anointing him|וַיִּמְשְׁח֧וּ\rb* \rb before the LORD|לַיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb as ruler|לְנָגִ֥יד\rb*, \rb and Zadok|וּלְצָד֖וֹק\rb* \rb as the priest|לְכֹהֵֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb So Solomon|שְׁ֠לֹמֹה\rb* \rb sat|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֨א\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה׀\rb* \rb as king|לְמֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb in place of|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥יד\rb*. \rb He prospered|וַיַּצְלַ֑ח\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb obeyed him|וַיִּשְׁמְע֥וּ\rb*.\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \v 24 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the officials|הַשָּׂרִים֙\rb* \rb and mighty men|וְהַגִּבֹּרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb as well as|וְגַ֕ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֑יד\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*, \rb pledged|נָ֣תְנוּ\rb* \rb their allegiance|יָ֔ד\rb* \rb to|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb highly|לְמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb exalted|וַיְגַדֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and bestowed|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb on him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb royal|מַלְכ֔וּת\rb* \rb majesty|ה֣וֹד\rb* \rb such as|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb been|הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb bestowed on|עַל־\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb king|מֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb*.
\s1 David’s Reign and Death
\r (\ref 1 Kings 2:10–12|1KI 2:10-12\ref*)
\p \v 26 \rb David|וְדָוִיד֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשָׁ֔י\rb* \rb was king|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb The length|וְהַיָּמִ֗ים\rb* \rb of David’s|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb reign|מָלַךְ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was forty|אַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* — \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֤וֹן\rb*\rb |מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb and thirty-three years|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֽוֹשׁ׃\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֥ם\rb*. \v 28 \rb He died|וַיָּ֙מָת֙\rb* \rb at a ripe|טוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb old age|בְּשֵׂיבָ֣ה\rb*, \rb full|שְׂבַ֥ע\rb* \rb of years|יָמִ֖ים\rb*, \rb riches|עֹ֣שֶׁר\rb*, \rb and honor|וְכָב֑וֹד\rb*, \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb Now the acts|וְדִבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb*, \rb from first|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to last|וְהָאֲחרֹנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the Seer|הָרֹאֶ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the Prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*, \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Gad|גָּ֥ד\rb* \rb the Seer|הַחֹזֶֽה׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb together with|עִ֥ם\rb* \rb all the details|כָּל־\rb* \rb of his reign|מַלְכוּת֖וֹ\rb*, \rb his might|וּגְבוּרָת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and the circumstances|וְהָעִתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb came|עָבְר֤וּ\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the lands|הָאֲרָצֽוֹת׃פ\rb*.
